 right, it might be that individual cells have too variable opinions to make strong statements on what compacts and conspiracies have as a general opinion.<br /> <br /> Which still seems like kind of a waste; I'd like VASCU and the Nine Stars to have opinions on each other, since they are both law enforcement and have likely bumped into each other if Nine Stars has any international presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>to be fair, this is not the first time this has happened. changeling does not have them either","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T17:15:44-08:00","id":1366437,"title":"","content":"I would not mourn the loss of stereotype sidebars. To me they're usually too quippy and shallow to be useful - though Hunter did have the best ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T17:19:45-08:00","id":1366440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366437#post1366437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not mourn the loss of stereotype sidebars. To me they're usually too quippy and shallow to be useful - though Hunter did have the best ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>we are not really mourning it. it's just it gives a VERY broad idea on what an organization thinks of another, and it adds flavor to them too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T17:56:40-08:00","id":1366447,"title":"","content":"Maybe it'll be added as a stretch goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T18:20:56-08:00","id":1366448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366447#post1366447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it'll be added as a stretch goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok that's pretty funny. I just want volume 2 of Compacts and Conspiracies for the past supplement organizations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T21:32:33-08:00","id":1366473,"title":"","content":"I know everyone's worried about Hong Kong police-hunters to be martial artists (and realistically they would know some as part of basic hand-to-hand defense) but there are other ways they could go.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/MBhFlRJ.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T21:39:27-08:00","id":1366475,"title":"","content":"The new fluff about how hunters keep sane by keeping in contact with elements of their mundane lives made me realize the Cainite Heresy needs an update; their whole thing was that they were a mysterious cult who doesn't deal with the mundane world. Which is fine, because the Rites of Denial needed to be generalized; the Rites are meant for vampires, but if a Cainite deems that another monster is their enabler, it's easy enough to alter the formulae to target them instead. The thing the Rites Deny is the capacity of monsters to abuse humans, it's just the Cainites view vampires as personifications of abuse (unsurprising, given how many of them are ex-ghouls).<br /> <br /> The idea I have is that Cainites are just as much a survivor support network as they are a religion of slayers, if not more so. Their real goal is not just revenge, but to break the justifications the bloodsuckers use for themselves. They are <i>not </i>your friends, <i>not </i>your only option, and you are <i>not </i>just as bad for hating them for what they've done. They provide a new, bloody faith that allows those broken by leeches to rebuild themselves around, but more than that they provide a haven for other broken people. Which is to say, if you're not a leech, they're probably pretty willing to talk things over civilly. If they sincerely believe you've been hurt, they'll give you the time of day to listen; they can't offer much in the way of help, unless it's assistance in ridding you of a user, but they will provide a shoulder to cry on, and sometimes that's what's needed. The <i>practical </i>upshot of this is that the Cainites don't care if you're technically not human, if you don't drain life (they may even be willing to overlook draining life literally, if you don't drain it metaphorically and are actively repulsed by the idea enough; it's in the sense of &quot;we'll let you absolve your sins before you join the rest on the fire&quot;, but they'll help prevent the darkness within from corrupting the absolution) - which means they have plenty of favors to call on to make it seem like they've got an infinite array of powers. Pay no attention to the werewolf behind the curtain - not that a leech would be less scared if they knew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 02-09-2020, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T01:21:26-08:00","id":1366505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366264#post1366264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know how good the quality of the Storyteller Screen will be? <br /> I still own the thick and sturdy Screen from the first edition of the new World Of Darkness. So when I received my copy of the \u201cChangeling: The Lost - Storyteller Screen\u201d, it was a huge disappointment! It\u2019s very thin and looks already very used on the edges while the old one still looks like new... It also contains only three pages instead of four.. \ud83d\ude15</div> </div> </div> </div>And I would also like to know whether there are any plans for new dice? Maybe as a stretch goal?<br /> (It\u2019s really an advantage, while playing in a dark room, to have all the successes highlighted.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T08:45:31-08:00","id":1366563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366475#post1366475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new fluff about how hunters keep sane by keeping in contact with elements of their mundane lives made me realize the Cainite Heresy needs an update; their whole thing was that they were a mysterious cult who doesn't deal with the mundane world. Which is fine, because the Rites of Denial needed to be generalized; the Rites are meant for vampires, but if a Cainite deems that another monster is their enabler, it's easy enough to alter the formulae to target them instead. The thing the Rites Deny is the capacity of monsters to abuse humans, it's just the Cainites view vampires as personifications of abuse (unsurprising, given how many of them are ex-ghouls).<br /> <br /> The idea I have is that Cainites are just as much a survivor support network as they are a religion of slayers, if not more so. Their real goal is not just revenge, but to break the justifications the bloodsuckers use for themselves. They are <i>not </i>your friends, <i>not </i>your only option, and you are <i>not </i>just as bad for hating them for what they've done. They provide a new, bloody faith that allows those broken by leeches to rebuild themselves around, but more than that they provide a haven for other broken people. Which is to say, if you're not a leech, they're probably pretty willing to talk things over civilly. If they sincerely believe you've been hurt, they'll give you the time of day to listen; they can't offer much in the way of help, unless it's assistance in ridding you of a user, but they will provide a shoulder to cry on, and sometimes that's what's needed. The <i>practical </i>upshot of this is that the Cainites don't care if you're technically not human, if you don't drain life (they may even be willing to overlook draining life literally, if you don't drain it metaphorically and are actively repulsed by the idea enough; it's in the sense of &amp;quot;we'll let you absolve your sins before you join the rest on the fire&amp;quot;, but they'll help prevent the darkness within from corrupting the absolution) - which means they have plenty of favors to call on to make it seem like they've got an infinite array of powers. Pay no attention to the werewolf behind the curtain - not that a leech would be less scared if they knew.</div> </div> </div> </div>the cainites can still have mundane connections though. I dont see any need of a re-write. to make them not see everything as vampires would to take away from their extremism and still being considered a &quot;heresy&quot; even by hunter standards. the write-up even makes it a point they still see all of humanity as needing to be saved as they are better than the vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T09:02:24-08:00","id":1366569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366563#post1366563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the cainites can still have mundane connections though. I dont see any need of a re-write. to make them not see everything as vampires would to take away from their extremism and still being considered a &quot;heresy&quot; even by hunter standards. the write-up even makes it a point they still see all of humanity as needing to be saved as they are better than the vampires</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This doesn't conflict. Everything bad in the world is vampires, the source of their pain. I'm just giving them room to tell different stories and hunt other things than vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T09:08:41-08:00","id":1366570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366569#post1366569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This doesn't conflict. Everything bad in the world is vampires, the source of their pain. I'm just giving them room to tell different stories and hunt other things than vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>yes, but cainites, like the other supplemental conspiracies, were made for specific purposes. many times, they DO hunt other supernaturals since they can easily be misidentified to a group of broken fanatics.<br /> <br /> and I always the cainites were, in their own cult-tish way, a support group. I just dont see the point in softening up when they still allow for touchstones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T09:38:34-08:00","id":1366577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366570#post1366570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yes, but cainites, like the other supplemental conspiracies, were made for specific purposes. many times, they DO hunt other supernaturals since they can easily be misidentified to a group of broken fanatics.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't that, the problem is the Rites of Denial handicap them more than the Knights of St. George, Les Mysteries, the Faithful of Shulpae, the Knights of St. Adrian, or the Merrick Institute.<br /> <br /> All of them can at least hold their own against things not in their wheelhouse. The Rites explicitly have penalties attached to anything except hunting vampires. That makes the Cainites damn hard to use for anything except their mission statement, while the Merrick children can harass the enemy in their brains, the dragonslayers can neutralize Dread Powers and inflict Tilts (well, derangements, but those are Tilts in the new system), and the Faithful...well, they might enjoy something other than jerky.<br /> <br /> Cainites deserve a buff, and that means widening their obsessions a bit. Good point on them already trying to save humanity, but I say that being open to dark alliances makes them more realistic fanatics, not less. Fanatics are masters of doublethink if they feel it helps the cause, and it makes them an even better dark mirror (or is that a bright one) to Kindred; it gives them a side of seeming more powerful than they normally are, and they're just as morally messy if it helps them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T10:17:55-08:00","id":1366584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366577#post1366577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem isn't that, the problem is the Rites of Denial handicap them more than the Knights of St. George, Les Mysteries, the Faithful of Shulpae, the Knights of St. Adrian, or the Merrick Institute.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be noted that the original Aves Minerva's Red Rites did influenced other supernatural beings other than vampires. Assuming that the Sources have access to all of the knowledge that the Aves Minerva had, and taking into account the dynamic way that the book seems to use, it is not out of the picture for the Cainte to gain a more developed/expanded version of the Rites.<br /> <br /> Talking about the subject- am I the only one who finds it somewhat strange how dynamic the book feels like? I mean, as far as I recall, most other 2e Core books took a more static approach, and didn't outright stated certain splats from 1e have collapsed or absorbed into others. If there were changes for the setting, it was done through rectons instead of propagation in time. More than that, the writeup for the AO, a main splat, is described as on the verge of coming change, not to mention things like the recent mysterious attacks against &quot;non virtuous&quot; hunters, or the strange conflicts which rise between conspiracies as someone starts hording resources. All of it makes the Hunter setting feel as almost it is on the edge, and that some later boom is planned to expand on those plot points- but it is a core book for a new edition, so...<br /> <br /> Don't take me wrong- I don;t say it is a bad thing. If it is meant to show how unstable is the world the hunters live in it does an excellent job. But it is so different than how most other CofD's core books did things (kinda reminds me of the metaplot changes done in V:tM and other WoD games), that it just feels.. strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T10:20:06-08:00","id":1366585,"title":"","content":"Also, just less than 300$ for the next stretch goal! Maybe more limited tier rewards can be opened to encourage us to spend more money on the Kickstarter? *puppy eyes*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T10:28:11-08:00","id":1366587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366577#post1366577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem isn't that, the problem is the Rites of Denial handicap them more than the Knights of St. George, Les Mysteries, the Faithful of Shulpae, the Knights of St. Adrian, or the Merrick Institute.<br /> <br /> All of them can at least hold their own against things not in their wheelhouse. The Rites explicitly have penalties attached to anything except hunting vampires. That makes the Cainites damn hard to use for anything except their mission statement, while the Merrick children can harass the enemy in their brains, the dragonslayers can neutralize Dread Powers and inflict Tilts (well, derangements, but those are Tilts in the new system), and the Faithful...well, they might enjoy something other than jerky.<br /> <br /> Cainites deserve a buff, and that means widening their obsessions a bit. Good point on them already trying to save humanity, but I say that being open to dark alliances makes them more realistic fanatics, not less. Fanatics are masters of doublethink if they feel it helps the cause, and it makes them an even better dark mirror (or is that a bright one) to Kindred; it gives them a side of seeming more powerful than they normally are, and they're just as morally messy if it helps them.</div> </div> </div> </div>now I can get behind the doublethink, however with that, it should still be kept that even other supernaturals are &quot;vampires fault&quot;.<br /> <br /> as for buffing their endowment, I see the reasoning. personally, one person I know just requires extra ingredients for different splats. werewolves require a dash of silver in the vials, for example","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T11:35:27-08:00","id":1366597,"title":"","content":"Aaaand we got it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T12:35:21-08:00","id":1366610,"title":"","content":"We got $55,000 in funding - so we got 1st chapter <i>Tending the Flame</i> Companion book - about Cells and Tier One hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T15:58:50-08:00","id":1366650,"title":"","content":"I just discovered, there's apparently such a thing as a real <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cainites\" target=\"_blank\">Cainite strain of Gnostic Christianity</a>.<br /> <br /> I feel the 2E Cainites need to at least acknowledge them as forebears, even if they're a bit embarrassed by them (and should be, those guys were raving anti-Semites and major edgelords).<br /> <br /> Idea; the modern Cainite Heresy has jettisoned all but the general idea that Cain is a dark savior, and that the material world is ruled by an evil figure who is represented in the world by vampires. To be honest, the cosmology doesn't matter all that much; the Heresy is a faith of the <i>here </i>and <i>now, </i>and one doesn't really need a cosmic justification to remove the &quot;un&quot; part of the undead given what they do every night. But the Cainites who bother keeping a history and telling stories - ie, the ones who have semi-retired, generally, and now serve as instructors to the next generation of hunters - like to say Abel was the first vampire, with the offering of flesh being accepted only because the Demiurge enjoys suffering; Abel was long dead by the time Cain finished off his body, and it was not out of jealous rage but horror and understanding the creature he once viewed as God had betrayed them both and rose his brother as a tormented monster meant to exist only as a dark enforcer of its will. There was just enough of the real Abel left to restrain the urge to fight back before the Demiurge realized one of its slaves had broken free of its toxic influence.<br /> <br /> There were other vampires risen since then, generally people whose human sides actually would fight back and free their souls from this torment of being an Archon, but Cain survived all the horrors visited on him, liberated partly from his mortality by his original act of noble rebellion and denunciation of his mistreatment, and he taught his heirs the Rites of Denial, and the methods of stalking the night to free the living from their malice. The vampires were crafty though, and corrupted his teachings with the power of their enthralling blood, turning the Cainites into rabid madmen used to oppress living humans (though the Cainite teacher is <i>very clear </i>that the only bit faked is the story of Genesis, and even that's incomplete - the Cainites protect all of humanity or none at all, and in fact they accept any religious creed into their Heresy), but Cain awoke from his wanderings and saved them, turning the vampires against each other and bringing them back into the true path. The Question &quot;Who is Cain?&quot; is thus, a quiet taunting of the bit of the Demiurge that puppets them, pointing out that &quot;the First Murderer&quot;, the title the Dark Creator gave him, is a farce - the Demiurge murdered Abel, not Cain. It's not a inquiry, but a demand: &quot;who shall we know Cain by, since he was never a murderer?&quot; The answer, of course, is &quot;the First Hunter&quot; - allow his heirs to demonstrate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T16:20:43-08:00","id":1366652,"title":"","content":"again though, Cainites have never cared for their history. and their origins actually date to Rome, I believe in Requiem for Rome, you will find they were originally a vampire cult","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T16:38:48-08:00","id":1366654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366652#post1366652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">again though, Cainites have never cared for their history. and their origins actually date to Rome, I believe in Requiem for Rome, you will find they were originally a vampire cult</div> </div> </div> </div>That's largely what I'm invoking. Those Cainites are the Gnostic Cainites.<br /> <br /> And it's really not much of a history, it's a parable; the lesson is that (A) killing vampires isn't murder, and (B), Cainites are not immune to being corrupted either, especially if they forget their duty is to save humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T16:43:25-08:00","id":1366655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366585#post1366585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, just less than 300$ for the next stretch goal! Maybe more limited tier rewards can be opened to encourage us to spend more money on the Kickstarter? *puppy eyes*</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's good in terms of showing just how harsh the Vigil can be. the hunters are candles after all, and even a group (compacts) of them can be wiped away<br /> <br /> again though, I dont agree with them just scrapping the supplemental compacts. division 6 was great BECAUSE it was not an actual government conspiracy, the Bear Club is not composed of the rich and bored but those that want to test their skills against what is the greatest prey, the Barret commission was not a conspiracy because they wanted to be in the shadows, and no matter what, being put in a actual government conspiracy will put a big target on your back. I suspect the men in black exists, not politicians, businessmen, and military men discussing terms with socially inclined monsters.<br /> <br /> and if need be, I'll shut up on my ranting, I've made it obvious (annoyingly so) that I'm upset they are getting rid of these groups that all have fans. I think they could've just used past groups as examples and made up new ones that could show up in supplements that look to the past. and finally, the only way I could forgive this, is if compacts and conspiracies 2 s made for all of em (yes, extremely selfish, I know.)<br /> <br /> rant over","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T16:46:17-08:00","id":1366656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366654#post1366654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's largely what I'm invoking. Those Cainites are the Gnostic Cainites.<br /> <br /> And it's really not much of a history, it's a parable; the lesson is that (A) killing vampires isn't murder, and (B), Cainites are not immune to being corrupted either, especially if they forget their duty is to save humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm? I thought the cainites of Rome were non-existent before that vampire brought them together? <br /> <br /> and do the cainites really need to be connected to that group? they are much too ancient for the ones we have, and seems like it would not even matter too much. and the write-up does not cainites need to be careful about their own humanity, the Fatalists are actually called out for being too cruel, even by other cainites<br /> <br /> EDIT: I am reminded. please dont make the Lucifuge descended from god machine demons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-09-2020, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T18:21:00-08:00","id":1366672,"title":"","content":"I think in the preview or play test documents? they were still good old fire and brimestone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T18:38:36-08:00","id":1366674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366672#post1366672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in the preview or play test documents? they were still good old fire and brimestone.</div> </div> </div> </div>from Contagion Chronicles? sort that does not really point toward their origins at all. god machine demons can easily be fire and brimstone too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T18:44:48-08:00","id":1366677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366674#post1366674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> from Contagion Chronicles? sort that does not really point toward their origins at all. god machine demons can easily be fire and brimstone too</div> </div> </div> </div>no they had a playtest document out I think. It was to test the new integrity rules for hunter. I used to have it but I think it was on my old computer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T19:14:02-08:00","id":1366681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366677#post1366677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no they had a playtest document out I think. It was to test the new integrity rules for hunter. I used to have it but I think it was on my old computer.</div> </div> </div> </div>well if it clarified they were Inferno/kept it vague, then I guess so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T20:44:36-08:00","id":1366688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366656#post1366656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> hmm? I thought the cainites of Rome were non-existent before that vampire brought them together? <br /> <br /> and do the cainites really need to be connected to that group? they are much too ancient for the ones we have, and seems like it would not even matter too much. and the write-up does not cainites need to be careful about their own humanity, the Fatalists are actually called out for being too cruel, even by other cainites<br /> <br /> EDIT: I am reminded. please dont make the Lucifuge descended from god machine demons</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a little of both. That group, in Requiem for Rome, is the source of the modern Cainite Gnostics in the real world, and their theology. It's explicit in the the book that they were mostly following the leader because of Viniculum, and his death freed them, leaving them very angry about their mistreatment. It's also not new; the Cainite 1E writeup has that heresy as an element of the modern Heresy's past, they were protected by the Aves Minerva afterwards.<br /> <br /> Not protesting that, either, I'm just giving them some internal myths that extend beyond &quot;vampires bad&quot;; they have their own superstitions and folktales, I feel, ones that may or may not be true but serve as valuable practical and moral lessons that don't need to be put down to print. A group that old doesn't exist without some stories, Sources or not. I still have them as being very much not actually concerned with their past, both because they don't care and for security reasons. They know just enough to learn from experience, it doesn't matter what they were beyond &quot;this is how we avoid being infiltrated and learn to recognize when we are&quot;, along with helping build the us vs. the world feeling. I plan on pointing out that while the original Cainites, assuming these are even the same people, were Gnostic Christians, the modern ones honestly don't care what faith you are, or even if you believe the story. If you kill vampires and draw the Mark, you are as devout as you need to be - the sole tenet of their faith is &quot;leeches must die, and their influence eradicated.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T20:57:10-08:00","id":1366689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366656#post1366656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I am reminded. please dont make the Lucifuge descended from god machine demons</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Lucifuge is the Lucifuge&quot; is my shorthand for &quot;metaphysical line of descent is tricky at best, and doubly so when placed outside its native context&quot; for a reason.<br /> <br /> I'm content to not have a centuries-old conspiracy of devil-botherers who poke their noses into everything from the mainstream infernal host to fairies to legacy techgnostics be purely a splinter group from three blind Frenchmen who do Hell's work for genetics' sake. This is explicitly not a gameline that plays in neat little boxes at the best of times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T21:35:02-08:00","id":1366694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366689#post1366689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;The Lucifuge is the Lucifuge&amp;quot; is my shorthand for &amp;quot;metaphysical line of descent is tricky at best, and doubly so when placed outside its native context&amp;quot; for a reason.<br /> <br /> I'm content to not have a centuries-old conspiracy of devil-botherers who poke their noses into everything from the mainstream infernal host to fairies to legacy techgnostics be purely a splinter group from three blind Frenchmen who do Hell's work for genetics' sake. This is explicitly not a gameline that plays in neat little boxes at the best of times.</div> </div> </div> </div>honestly, while I'm not a fan of it, I'd rather have hodge podge of supernaturals rather than god machine. so yeah, I can compromise with that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T03:20:50-08:00","id":1366726,"title":"","content":"And we have <b>Loyalists of Thule &amp; The Cheiron Group</b> preview. I will compile interesting quotes in coming hours. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T04:27:27-08:00","id":1366735,"title":"","content":"Loyalists of Thule quotes compilation - interesting thing it that they take on themselves problems of modern neo-fasists movements...<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule \u2013 Indebted</b><br /> In the early 20th century, German occultists of the Thule Gesselshaft believed that the Aryan race, the inhabitants of Lost Thule, planted the roots of modern society. While many of Thule\u2019s early members were Nazi sympathizers, most left after Hitler severed ties with the group in 1920. The group slowly fell into decline and Loyalists studied privately until after World War II. In the aftermath of WWII, disbanded members regrouped in Germany to discuss their next steps. Most were shocked to learn how the Thule Gesselshaft\u2019s beliefs had been weaponized by the Nazis to justify attempted genocide.Despite their earnestness, the once-revered professors, archaeologists, and philosophers of the Thule Gesselshaft were largely ignored or forgotten. Devastated by the lukewarm reception, the Thule occultists spent the next decade forming the Loyalists of Thule. Their mission: Use their occult knowledge to save lives. <br /> For many years, the Loyalists of Thule fed valuable intel to other hunters. Largely, the organization\u2019s secretive nature and tightly controlled modus operandi have remained static for over 50 years. Members are descended from one of the Indebted, recruited aggressively, or blackmailed into joining. Intel is doled out to members using antiquated equipment and World War II-era ciphers, and hunters are expected to carry out orders without question.<br /> Unfortunately, no one has met or talked to the Munich-based founders for a few years, and Loyalists who\u2019ve done the math have realized the elders, if they\u2019re still alive, would be well over 100 years old. So who\u2019s issuing orders now? Some higher-ranking members are threatening to break protocol and fly to Munich to find out what\u2019s happening, but thus far the Loyalists have yet to do so. Now, the Loyalists of Thule remain suspicious, if not worried, that their organization is compromised. Its members cannot deny the growing threat of fascism spreading across the world yet struggle to understand why supernatural activity is clearly on the rise. While the Loyalists are not naive enough to believe that real world atrocities should be blamed on the occult, every act of fascism reminds them of their organization\u2019s dark past. Most Indebted believe that hate-filled<br /> atrocities caused by mortals are just as bad \u2014 if not worse \u2014 than the soulless creatures who prey on humankind and help where they can.<br /> While the Loyalists of Thule are trained to defend themselves, they pride themselves on the irintellectual prowess. <br /> Members deal with this plight in different ways by adding charitable works to their day-to-day studies. Some volunteer in their communities to prevent hate crimes, bring transgressors to justice, and help victims; others study cold cases to track down serial killers and mortal predators; and a third group has started a mentorship program to replenish the organization\u2019s numbers with eager proteges and talented, college-aged intellectuals.<br /> Ideally, the astute Loyalist passes the information they\u2019ve learned (or have received) to the best equipped hunters. The Indebted have traditionally viewed themselves as supportive of other hunters in The Union and SWORN but actively seek contact with other groups. Despite their scholarly reputation, many Loyalists are training to become more physically capable in response to their recent findings. Of all the compacts, the Indebted have their finger on the pulse of supernatural activity, and they have proof that the creatures of the night are more aggressive than ever before.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T04:28:06-08:00","id":1366736,"title":"","content":"I like the new, slightly brighter spin on Cheiron, though I wonder why their logo was changed. I liked the bow-and-arrow rune.<br /> <br /> I also suspect Melanie Sweetwater may indeed be a robot. Or a biosynthoid, close enough. Don't think I didn't notice the potential Deviant cross with the Thaumatech limit (given what Cheiron is, I'm almost entirely certain the surgeons occasionally ignore that limit and make an asset in-house, for the really scary jobs).<br /> <br /> And of course, the new edition of the field manual is a genuine reaction to the uselessness of the last one...and is even more useless now. Corporations, everybody!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T04:51:43-08:00","id":1366738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366694#post1366694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> honestly, while I'm not a fan of it, I'd rather have hodge podge of supernaturals rather than god machine. so yeah, I can compromise with that</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's not a compromise, that's just how the Lucifuge always was. In a world with the demon, demon, demon, demon, and demon problem, an organization founded of people whose claim to ancestry is a snake slipping between the legs is going to inherently be a dark, albeit burning, tree of unclear origins, made all the worse by how those curses and powers might spread, mingle and change when cousins start kissing. There's a reason Castigation works on faeries and spirits as well as it does demons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366736#post1366736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the new, slightly brighter spin on Cheiron, though I wonder why their logo was changed. I liked the bow-and-arrow rune.</div> </div> </div> </div>It hasn't? The Logo as described in the text(The Cernunnos/Pan caduceus) has been a long running point for Cheiron going back to the first book. The Field Projects Division is the branch that had the bow-and-arrow rune, and the artwork still clearly depicts that iconography.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-10-2020, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T05:19:25-08:00","id":1366744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366738#post1366738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it's not a compromise, that's just how the Lucifuge always was. In a world with the demon, demon, demon, demon, and demon problem, an organization founded of people whose claim to ancestry is a snake slipping between the legs is going to inherently be a dark, albeit burning, tree of unclear origins, made all the worse by how those curses and powers might spread, mingle and change when cousins start kissing. There's a reason Castigation works on faeries and spirits as well as it does demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>ehh, I've always seen them as from the Infernal, they all suffer from inner corruption in the blood, use genetics to try to find them (which to me, would only leave wolf blooded, Offspring, and Infernal blooded as Lucifuge material), and one of their endowments reveal a sorta &quot;true form&quot; unique to all of them that could be a demonic beast to a broken angel. that, and they have the Becoming and their evil counterpart, the Les Diaboliques (whatever they're called) are in the Infernal Sourcebook. oh, and I feel like if they really were just a collective of different supernaturals, it would've been extremely easy for all of them to eventually figure out &quot;huh, why is my partner similar to what those changelings call &quot;Fae Touched&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T05:33:12-08:00","id":1366745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366744#post1366744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ehh, I've always seen them as from the Infernal, they all suffer from inner corruption in the blood, use genetics to try to find them (which to me, would only leave wolf blooded, Offspring, and Infernal blooded as Lucifuge material), and one of their endowments reveal a sorta &quot;true form&quot; unique to all of them that could be a demonic beast to a broken angel. that, and they have the Becoming and their evil counterpart, the Les Diaboliques (whatever they're called) are in the Infernal Sourcebook. oh, and I feel like if they really were just a collective of different supernaturals, it would've been extremely easy for all of them to eventually figure out &quot;huh, why is my partner similar to what those changelings call &quot;Fae Touched&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, first of all, why would they inherently know what changeling call things, specifically fae-touched.<br /> <br /> Second off, in a game where I can depict Mephistopholes through a Strix, a Maeltinent, an Abyssal Demon, a Pandemonic demon, a Onerios-formed goetic demon, a qashmallim, a True Fae, a Geist, an Unchained, a Horror, and god knows a lot of options from blue books, have them all <i>look and act the same</i> to the undiscerning human who, by the way, is gonna be dealing with Integrity breaking rolls the entire time, at what point am I supposed to believe someone is going to know the difference on this side of mortality?<br /> <br /> We as players have the game books, but the character's <i>don't</i>. Their frame of reference deals with a lot of disparate things that look highly similar, and that's before they set themselves up to become a melting pot for powers and influences, which the Lucifuge discernably <i>is</i>. &quot;What is Lady Lucifuge?&quot; is a major enough thread of concern for the Lucifuge that they have an entire (nominally secret) branch dedicated to answering that question.<br /> <br /> Hunters are in over their heads because they only see things by the edge of firelight-and flickering light and deep shadow makes for a lot of confusion and alarm for what things are what. Known and Unknown are themes for a <i>reason</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-24-2020, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T06:12:54-08:00","id":1366752,"title":"","content":"And now Cherion. I like they are written much strongly as historical and corporation - with nice flavors I quote. I always liked them as Deviants creation facility, so I can see Sweetwater as Devoted one, for examples. New handbook plot is just cool and fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <b><b>Cherion Group \u2013 Field Projects Division</b></b><br /><br /> The name \u201cCheiron\u201d was first used in 1905, but the Cheiron Group is far older and may have formed in antiquity. No one \u2014 not even its own members \u2014 is certain, because the organization has used many names including the Acheron Shipping &amp; Trading Co., the House of Katz, the Helios Society for the Infirmed, and the Octavian Apothecary.<br /> In fact, the Cheiron Group\u2019s public face is far less enigmatic than its history. To the average citizen, TCG is a progressive, philanthropic corporation that globally distributes affordable drugs and treatments covering a wide range of ailments and diseases. Its growing list of partners manufactures prosthetics, radiation technology, and monitoring equipment \u2014 even pacemakers and artificial hearts. <br /> Now, of course, the newly-appointed brand manager, Melanie Sweetwater, appears so often in the news and online some broadcasters have jokingly wondered if she\u2019s been cloned. The Cheiron Group\u2019s salaried employees can\u2019t always explain how Sweetwater seems to be in three places at once, and why she reports solely to the board of directors. (<b> Wyrd\u2019s</b> note: Devoted Deviant? Or Clones based on Created Pyros? )<br /> On the books, the Field Projects Division (FPD) is the so-called experimental arm of TCG that deals with cutting edge science \u2014 if you can call capturing, dissecting, and experimenting with monster parts science. In exchange for their service, FPD employees sign an ironclad contract to receive a hefty salary, full health benefits, and a pension. The legalese is hard to read, and agents often don\u2019t realize what they\u2019re signing up for. In addition to extensive surgery, implants, and body modifications, FPD employees also sign the rights away to their bodies before and after death. While their enhancements help them face down the supernatural, employees aren\u2019t always happy with the terms of their deal.<br /> The Cheiron Group doesn\u2019t view the supernatural as a threat. They think of them as \u201cassets\u201d and their victims as \u201ccasualties.\u201d Most of the time, members speak in code using words like \u201cpotential asset\u201d or \u201cPA\u201d to describe a monster they haven\u2019t captured yet, and agents as \u201cfield resources.\u201d Each agent is given the power to conduct their operation the way they see fit, provided they meet their PA quota. When a field resource has identified and captured a PA, they call in a Dedicated Pickup Team (DPT) to retrieve and remove it. Dedicated Pickup Teams are glorified security guards who\u2019ll only transport a PA if it is secured and neutralized; they won\u2019t assist in the field under any circumstance. Many agents learned how unhelpful the DPT is the hard way \u2014 because they didn\u2019t decode or read the handbook.<br /> Most agents think the current edition of their field resource manual is a joke; it\u2019s an encrypted book of \u201cfirst-person accounts\u201d given to agents after their contract has been signed and delivered to HR. It has no TCG identifiers, never actually names the company, lists no authors, and has no ISBN or other book coding. The previous edition, a plain brown book that was billed to be a comprehensive guide, was far more official-looking than its successor. While that handbook contained a great deal of information, most of the data was either useless or severely outdated. Unfortunately, that bad intel led to \u201cthe incident\u201d \u2014 an event so horrifying, management is forbidden to speak of it.<br /> While recruits don\u2019t always feel prepared for field work, they have memorized three rules: Directives 53, 68, and 99. Directive 53, which refers to Safety Phrase 53 in an old EEC Council Directive (67/548/EEC), instructs companies to avoid public exposure to dangerous substances and to obtain special instructions before using them. Directive 68, on the other hand, states that field resources must ensure no member of the public believes a threat exists. Lastly, Directive 99 demands its field agents comport themselves as exemplary employees both on duty and off.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T07:05:30-08:00","id":1366765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366745#post1366745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, first of all, why would they inherently know what changeling call things, specifically fae-touched.<br /> <br /> Second of, in a game where I can depict Mephistopholes through a Strix, a Maeltinent, an Abyssal Demon, a Pandemonic demon, a Onerios-formed goetic demon, a qashmallim, a True Fae, a Geist, an Unchained, a Horror, and god knows a lot of options from blue books, have them all <i>look and act the same</i> to the undiscerning human who, by the way, is gonna be dealing with Integrity breaking rolls the entire time, at what point am I supposed to believe someone is going to know the difference on this side of mortality?<br /> <br /> We as players have the game books, but the character's <i>don't</i>. Their frame of reference deals with a lot of disparate things that look highly similar, and that's before they set themselves up to become a melting pot for powers and influences, which the Lucifuge discernably <i>is</i>. &amp;quot;What is Lady Lucifuge?&amp;quot; is a major enough thread of concern for the Lucifuge that they have an entire (nominally secret) branch dedicated to answering that question.<br /> <br /> Hunters are in over their heads because they only see things by the edge of firelight-and flickering light and deep shadow makes for a lot of confusion and alarm for what things are what. Known and Unknown are themes for a <i>reason</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not hostile to the idea of them being that way, I just think they are a little too connected to the Infernal to not have at least some truth to it. either way, their main theme could still easily be kept. whether they are infernal or a gathering of different supernaturals (and my example specifically included the hunter overhearing a Changeling calling someone &quot;fae touched&quot;, not him just knowing that)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T08:48:11-08:00","id":1366785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366744#post1366744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ehh, I've always seen them as from the Infernal, they all suffer from inner corruption in the blood, use genetics to try to find them (which to me, would only leave wolf blooded, Offspring, and Infernal blooded as Lucifuge material), and one of their endowments reveal a sorta &quot;true form&quot; unique to all of them that could be a demonic beast to a broken angel. that, and they have the Becoming and their evil counterpart, the Les Diaboliques (whatever they're called) are in the Infernal Sourcebook. oh, and I feel like if they really were just a collective of different supernaturals, it would've been extremely easy for all of them to eventually figure out &quot;huh, why is my partner similar to what those changelings call &quot;Fae Touched&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, they\u2019re ALL a hodge-podge at this point because the various recruited family lines of the Lucifuge all have their own demonic origins, but then they\u2019ve all intermarried with each other!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-10-2020, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T10:35:36-08:00","id":1366804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366785#post1366785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, they\u2019re ALL a hodge-podge at this point because the various recruited family lines of the Lucifuge all have their own demonic origins, but then they\u2019ve all intermarried with each other!</div> </div> </div> </div>in the end, I just think there are too many similarities each hunter has, and weird how no monsters ever say something like &quot;how the hell did that proximi gain those powers&quot; despite the theory (and yeah, I'm considering the Infernal origin a theory, not truth) that they are all different. but still, I would be ok with a hodge-podge. it would not limit them in their themes in any way, unlike being from the God machine (and i can acknowledge there would be some interesting plot hooks with the hodge podge take)<br /> <br /> anyway, loving the Loyalists and cheiron group. we even have an official rogue hunter hunting division now (and DAMN, a time manipulating implant? where the hell did they get that?). plus I do like that the notebook has hidden codes. the only weak point was it did not really tell what Hunters of that conspiracy do to keep in touch with humanity (since it seems like they work constantly) the Loyalists seem to be taking from Compacts and Conspiracies with its bigger focus on neo-nazism, and the mystery of the three old men is a good plot hook (I was wondering if they would be kept alive, glad they may or may not be). overall the same, but still great. <br /> <br /> cant wait for Network 0 and the Council of Bones. very excited for both the new advances in technology the Network utilizes and our first look at the new conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T10:39:48-08:00","id":1366806,"title":"","content":"I swear if anyone comes at me with the \u201cbut you\u2019re fine with monsters?\u201d fallacy for this, I\u2019m going to set something on fire.<br /> <br /> On the Chevron Group, the Board members can\u2019t be a secret if it\u2019s a publicly traded company that has a stock price. They would need official public figures then, even if the \u201cpeople\u201d who are REALLY running the company are hidden elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T11:06:02-08:00","id":1366814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366806#post1366806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I swear if anyone comes at me with the \u201cbut you\u2019re fine with monsters?\u201d fallacy for this, I\u2019m going to set something on fire.<br /> <br /> On the Chevron Group, the Board members can\u2019t be a secret if it\u2019s a publicly traded company that has a stock price. They would need official public figures then, even if the \u201cpeople\u201d who are REALLY running the company are hidden elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, now that you mention the &quot;publically traded&quot; part, that does not make sense. perhaps it's an oversight or assuming the reader is savvy enough to know the &quot;real&quot; directors are a secret?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T11:29:26-08:00","id":1366817,"title":"","content":"Think we wondered about this before and found that private companies can have stock, and Cheiron isn't explicitly called out as publicly-traded, even if it does have a public face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T11:45:10-08:00","id":1366820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366817#post1366817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think we wondered about this before and found that private companies can have stock, and Cheiron isn't explicitly called out as publicly-traded, even if it does have a public face.</div> </div> </div> </div>ahh ok. just wondering, why do you think Recruitment is kept out of the loop with the P.R retrieval division?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T11:53:36-08:00","id":1366821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366820#post1366820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ahh ok. just wondering, why do you think Recruitment is kept out of the loop with the P.R retrieval division?</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing 'if you try to go rogue, we have a special task force dedicated to hunting you down' may taint recruitment efforts. Even if it's not intentional, just knowing it can probably curb someone's interest in recruiting certain types of hunters, or cause them to let something slip.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T12:20:24-08:00","id":1366827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366817#post1366817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think we wondered about this before and found that private companies can have stock, and Cheiron isn't explicitly called out as publicly-traded, even if it does have a public face.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reference to consistently high stock price implies public trading pretty strongly, as the price in private negotiations wouldn\u2019t influence public perception, which is what the passage is talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T12:38:05-08:00","id":1366830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366821#post1366821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Knowing 'if you try to go rogue, we have a special task force dedicated to hunting you down' may taint recruitment efforts. Even if it's not intentional, just knowing it can probably curb someone's interest in recruiting certain types of hunters, or cause them to let something slip.</div> </div> </div> </div>ahh, I didnt think of it that way. smart way of looking at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T13:38:37-08:00","id":1366846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366806#post1366806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the Chevron Group, the Board members can\u2019t be a secret if it\u2019s a publicly traded company that has a stock price. They would need official public figures then, even if the \u201cpeople\u201d who are REALLY running the company are hidden elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in Witch Finders it is said that the Board have managed to defend their right for privacy in court. While it may be illegal in real world economics, we are talking about a far more corrupted world, where Cheiron have a lot of money the spend and god knows what eldritch powers to use for their benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T13:46:20-08:00","id":1366848,"title":"","content":"I just realized the drawback of a Hand of Glory is that it's got a mind of its own.<br /> <br /> I am going to make a Cheiron character whose primary narrative purpose is to be the vessel of comic relief for an extremely rude and snarky Hand.<br /> <br /> &quot;And now, foolish hunter, you will-&quot;<br /> <br /> *Hand starts wanking the air*<br /> <br /> &quot;DIE IMMEDIATELY, IMPUDENT WORM!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T14:00:03-08:00","id":1366854,"title":"","content":"This is probably more in the room of headcanon than something strictly outlined in the books AFAIR, but I've always believed that there is a central privately held corporation which has the &quot;board&quot; and then Cheiron has majority/controlling stakes in publicly traded subsidiaries. Or that it's an even weirder and complicated corporate structure that's more like a chaebol or Kaiser Permanente.<br /> <br /> The inner circle is effectively a mystery cult as much as they're a corporate hierarchy, so they wouldn't need exact public lines of control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T03:21:59-08:00","id":1366936,"title":"","content":"Backed, getting a hard copy - can't wait. My group has recently expressed interest in a &quot;down to earth urban fantasy game&quot; so this fits the bill as they will mostly need the COFD book and I can work off the preview notes behind the scenes. <br /> <br /> I don't know if this has already been asked and answered, bit how compatible will the mortal remains content be? I imagine dread powers are pretty much a direct port - but what about the compacts or dare I ask conspiracys? <br /> <br /> Fortunately I see we are getting build your own conspiracy and compact rules, so I can't imagine porting will be that hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T04:12:33-08:00","id":1366943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordofIron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366936#post1366936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Backed, getting a hard copy - can't wait. My group has recently expressed interest in a &quot;down to earth urban fantasy game&quot; so this fits the bill as they will mostly need the COFD book and I can work off the preview notes behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> I don't know if this has already been asked and answered, bit how compatible will the mortal remains content be? I imagine dread powers are pretty much a direct port - but what about the compacts or dare I ask conspiracys?<br /> <br /> Fortunately I see we are getting build your own conspiracy and compact rules, so I can't imagine porting will be that hard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mortal Remains itself does contain conversion rules to make it so that the old 1E system can function in 2E so the Compacts should be almost entirely fine. With Conspiracies, the main difference as we are going into official 2E territory is the gradual addition of Backlashes to the old Endowments, making it so that Endowments are much riskier to the hunter but feel like a worthwhile endeavor in the eyes of the Vigil. The Knights of St. Adrian and the Merrick Institute should be fine with a few homebrew changes thanks to the new Build-Your-Own system providing a skeleton for Endowment creation. However, the Faithful of Shulpae might be a slight issue as their Endowment is different from the others as they temporarily gain Dread Powers rather than having a list of powers to choose from (something that, I just realized, all official Endowments provide).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T06:42:48-08:00","id":1366961,"title":"","content":"Perispiritsm, the Council of Bones Endowment, just got publicly previewed.<br /> <br /> First of all: Aww, the Les Mysteres got dissolved? Bummer. I liked then, even if they weren't exactly bright. Still, instant story hook for rebuilding them.<br /> <br /> Second: Holy crap the Council is awesome. Also their powers are explicitly from a tattoo that enhances the link their life force has to their soul - that would be the perispirit. In the future, it's my canon soul-eating gets the perispirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T06:43:09-08:00","id":1366962,"title":"","content":"the Council of Bones seems very interesting, cant wait to see the full write up tomorrow<br /> <br /> and the Les Mysteres is apparently &quot;defunct&quot; now. I'm starting to get annoyed. it seems all those compacts and conspiracies were made just to be scrapped no matter what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T07:39:57-08:00","id":1366974,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone! Glad to see you're excited about the Kickstarter and are discussing the setting. Popping in briefly to mention that Hunter 2E does retain the toolkit mentality from First Edition. If you are interested in playing a 1E compact/conspiracy or want to create your own? You can do that with the rules in the Storyteller chapter. Ultimately, it's your decision what you're excited to play at your table. I do hope we blast through more stretch goals, because Tending the Flame has some awesome potential for Hunter 2E!<br /> <br /> I also wanted to talk about Mortal Remains. MR is considered a First Edition supplement. The patch provided does provide a rules update to 2E as it was designed. As I mentioned in The Story Told interview, Hunter 2E provides more rules that clearly distinguish the difference between someone who makes a commitment to the hunt versus their first brush with the supernatural. Besides the Endowments redesign, hunters also get a Tactics update, Teamwork, Touchstones, and more! As such, Hunter 2E is the current and most up-to-date iteration of the rules.<br /> <br /> Thanks! Enjoy the new conspiracy! We've also got two new compacts--one of which focuses on cryptids designed by Allen Turner!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T07:50:01-08:00","id":1366975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366974#post1366974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone! Glad to see you're excited about the Kickstarter and are discussing the setting. Popping in briefly to mention that Hunter 2E does retain the toolkit mentality from First Edition. If you are interested in playing a 1E compact/conspiracy or want to create your own? You can do that with the rules in the Storyteller chapter. Ultimately, it's your decision what you're excited to play at your table. I do hope we blast through more stretch goals, because Tending the Flame has some awesome potential for Hunter 2E!<br /> <br /> I also wanted to talk about Mortal Remains. MR is considered a First Edition supplement. The patch provided does provide a rules update to 2E as it was designed. As I mentioned in The Story Told interview, Hunter 2E provides more rules that clearly distinguish the difference between someone who makes a commitment to the hunt versus their first brush with the supernatural. Besides the Endowments redesign, hunters also get a Tactics update, Teamwork, Touchstones, and more! As such, Hunter 2E is the current and most up-to-date iteration of the rules.<br /> <br /> Thanks! Enjoy the new conspiracy! We've also got two new compacts--one of which focuses on cryptids designed by Allen Turner!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I assume it's the SWORN that focus on Cryptids. I admit that is actually REALLY awesome.<br /> <br /> If I may ask, and I'm sorry if I've been rude about it before, why are all the supplemental Hunter organizations being torn down? I understand it's to show the fragile nature of the Vigil, but all of those groups were made to be in the here and now and playable, and they were all quite popular. will we ever see them written up in any kinda future supplement?<br /> <br /> anyway, cant wait to see the full write-up on the Council of Bones, and I do like how every write-up so far introduces storyhooks from within the organizations. the Council especially seems to have many mysteries","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T08:16:11-08:00","id":1366980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366975#post1366975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume it's the SWORN that focus on Cryptids. I admit that is actually REALLY awesome.<br /> <br /> If I may ask, and I'm sorry if I've been rude about it before, why are all the supplemental Hunter organizations being torn down? I understand it's to show the fragile nature of the Vigil, but all of those groups were made to be in the here and now and playable, and they were all quite popular. will we ever see them written up in any kinda future supplement?<br /> <br /> anyway, cant wait to see the full write-up on the Council of Bones, and I do like how every write-up so far introduces storyhooks from within the organizations. the Council especially seems to have many mysteries</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, Primordial newcomer. The history of compacts and conspiracies began to change when the Dark Eras line was added, much like DE affected Geist, too. All of a sudden global conspiracies either needed to have more history than they did or they had to be newer; compacts could (but not always) be temporary due to historical events/tragedies and changes over time. Knowing this, I wanted Hunter 2E to be a corebook that reflected that change while not fixating on Dark Eras. There were tons of compacts/conspiracies created as First Edition progressed, and I felt it made sense they'd be absorbed or dissolved because there are more denizens now in the Chronicles of Darkness than there was when Hunter 1E debuted.<br /> <br /> I do want to reiterate that not all of the supplemental Hunter organizations are affected by this. I tried to be careful while also providing rules to create compacts and conspiracies in the Storyteller's chapter so you can play the group you want. The example compact, Ashwood Abbey, was re-introduced for this reason. If you want to play any compact or conspiracy, I absolutely encourage you to do so. At no point do I ever want to say: &quot;You can't play this!&quot; Or, &quot;Every group needs to resonate with you.&quot; Neither of those things are true. Hunter 2E is your game to use as you see fit.<br /> <br /> And yes, SWORN is the compact that deals with cryptids. We had fans who wanted Native compacts historically in Dark Eras, and I was lucky enough to find a Native designer who was excited to craft a modern compact. SWORN is Allen's vision. Compacts can be inspired by cultural needs--which is a very human thing to happen in a world full of shadows and darkness.<br /> <br /> I hope this helps and I appreciate the discussion. Not everyone is familiar with the Dark Eras line, I know, but as the developer I wanted to weigh my decisions for the new corebook. Thanks for listening!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T08:17:57-08:00","id":1366981,"title":"","content":"P.S. Thanks for catching on that the write-ups are full of story hooks--that was absolutely the intent! Should you want to hunt monsters every week? AWESOME. Should you want to delve deeper in hunter society? That's there, too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T10:07:28-08:00","id":1367021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366980#post1366980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, Primordial newcomer. The history of compacts and conspiracies began to change when the Dark Eras line was added, much like DE affected Geist, too. All of a sudden global conspiracies either needed to have more history than they did or they had to be newer; compacts could (but not always) be temporary due to historical events/tragedies and changes over time. Knowing this, I wanted Hunter 2E to be a corebook that reflected that change while not fixating on Dark Eras. There were tons of compacts/conspiracies created as First Edition progressed, and I felt it made sense they'd be absorbed or dissolved because there are more denizens now in the Chronicles of Darkness than there was when Hunter 1E debuted.<br /> <br /> I do want to reiterate that not all of the supplemental Hunter organizations are affected by this. I tried to be careful while also providing rules to create compacts and conspiracies in the Storyteller's chapter so you can play the group you want. The example compact, Ashwood Abbey, was re-introduced for this reason. If you want to play any compact or conspiracy, I absolutely encourage you to do so. At no point do I ever want to say: &amp;quot;You can't play this!&amp;quot; Or, &amp;quot;Every group needs to resonate with you.&amp;quot; Neither of those things are true. Hunter 2E is your game to use as you see fit.<br /> <br /> And yes, SWORN is the compact that deals with cryptids. We had fans who wanted Native compacts historically in Dark Eras, and I was lucky enough to find a Native designer who was excited to craft a modern compact. SWORN is Allen's vision. Compacts can be inspired by cultural needs--which is a very human thing to happen in a world full of shadows and darkness.<br /> <br /> I hope this helps and I appreciate the discussion. Not everyone is familiar with the Dark Eras line, I know, but as the developer I wanted to weigh my decisions for the new corebook. Thanks for listening!</div> </div> </div> </div>thanks for taking the time to answer! I can definitely see the reasoning for needing more history or being new. I will admit it does confuse me with the les mysteres, as they, to me at least, seem self propagating. but I'm still satisfied with the answer and have been more than happy with everything else in the book<br /> <br /> in the cryptids, that is awesome for Allen. to know the compact will have an authenticity to it is very reassuring. I've actually been looking forward to them more than the Council (which again, seems to be extremely cool)<br /> <br /> finally, yes, it all definitely helped. I'm sorry that I was so upset in my past posts, but the fact you took the time to address it gives me closure to it (and I do admit, only looking at Hunter groups coming apart would through Dark Eras would not really do the nature of them justice)<br /> <br /> and by the way, yup, to me hunting monsters AND learning the inner secrets of your own organization are what makes Hunter The Vigil fun to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T10:13:40-08:00","id":1367023,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the Les Mysteres were very fractured to begin with, and their complicated relationships with the spirits always put them on the verge of becoming their tools- and as such, rogue organization. While I sincerely liked them, it was only a matter of time before they'll dissolve- only for some more organized group rising from the wreckage.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Perispiritism looks very cool! And if SWORN will incorporate the believes and tools left behind by the Keepers of the Weave and the Wardens of Light it could be very cool to see. The Mark seems almost like a parasitic entity, something like a fragment of a geist which clutches to the living. Some really cool concept, IMO.<br /> <br /> Also, just something I have wondered about- does things like getting the Mark, the spiritual transformation of the Ascending Ones or gaining enough Taumatech should make someone considered a Sleepwalker/Kin? As hunter does have an high crossover potential, the answer for that question could impact the way the hunters would interact with their targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T10:34:04-08:00","id":1367030,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone! Allen wrote a design essay to talk about his deeply personal experiences and inspiration, but also to highlight why this particular compact is meaningful to a Native hunter and how they can work with other hunters. Authenticity was absolutely important, especially since there are over 550+ federally recognized tribes with their own, unique cultures and Native history is extremely complicated. I can't wait to share that with all of you; Allen is hoping you'll welcome him and his voice with open arms. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T10:55:18-08:00","id":1367036,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> while yes, the Les Mysteres could be used as tools, they were not ignorant of the fact, and managed to stay alive for quite a long time. I always thought they were like the Cainites in that you could never really get rid of em. all in all, I think the real reason I've been upset is because I really had it in my head that all organizations would get a short write-up and show up in a volume 2 C&amp;Cs. so really, it's all my fault for setting myself up for disappointment<br /> <br /> as for that design essay, is that something we will be able to read? I would really like to read it if that's ok. and I'm really looking forward to how Allen has the supernatural viewed from the perspective of the SWORN (while not a big focus of mine, I do like the different views and interpretations hunters groups have on the supernatural world and how they funnel it through their own beliefs)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T10:59:12-08:00","id":1367037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366980#post1366980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, SWORN is the compact that deals with cryptids. We had fans who wanted Native compacts historically in Dark Eras, and I was lucky enough to find a Native designer who was excited to craft a modern compact. SWORN is Allen's vision. Compacts can be inspired by cultural needs--which is a very human thing to happen in a world full of shadows and darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hearing this makes me so happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T11:03:22-08:00","id":1367039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367036#post1367036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>as for that design essay, is that something we will be able to read? I would really like to read it if that's ok. and I'm really looking forward to how Allen has the supernatural viewed from the perspective of the SWORN (while not a big focus of mine, I do like the different views and interpretations hunters groups have on the supernatural world and how they funnel it through their own beliefs)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I will be posting the essay on Sunday/Monday after SWORN is live. I've been posting interviews with willing team members on FlamesRising.com and there's two up already. I'm going to be traveling those days, so please be patient with me!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T11:03:47-08:00","id":1367040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367036#post1367036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> while yes, the Les Mysteres could be used as tools, they were not ignorant of the fact, and managed to stay alive for quite a long time. I always thought they were like the Cainites in that you could never really get rid of em. all in all, I think the real reason I've been upset is because I really had it in my head that all organizations would get a short write-up and show up in a volume 2 C&amp;Cs. so really, it's all my fault for setting myself up for disappointment</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, and I get where you are coming from- I too really wanted to see that &quot;short writeup for all!&quot; kind of section, but as it was for around 40 organizations, as time moved on I've started to understand how unrealistic it sounded for a core book. Just like you, I am too somewhat disappointed to see some old groups which I grew to love being dissolved, but I try to examine it well enough to see that at least non of those changes are too out of place (maybe Merrick, but again I think that it referenced to the original organization than the new one presented in Mortal Remains). So yeah, I too have hoped to see all of the groups presented in the core, but I steeled myself in case it wouldn't be the case (even though I have't expected the rote that 2e took for some of them, honestly)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T11:15:43-08:00","id":1367042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367040#post1367040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, and I get where you are coming from- I too really wanted to see that &amp;quot;short writeup for all!&amp;quot; kind of section, but as it was for around 40 organizations, as time moved on I've started to understand how unrealistic it sounded for a core book. Just like you, I am too somewhat disappointed to see some old groups which I grew to love being dissolved, but I try to examine it well enough to see that at least non of those changes are too out of place (maybe Merrick, but again I think that it referenced to the original organization than the new one presented in Mortal Remains). So yeah, I too have hoped to see all of the groups presented in the core, but I steeled myself in case it wouldn't be the case (even though I have't expected the rote that 2e took for some of them, honestly)</div> </div> </div> </div>well I should learn from you then, you have been much more mature about it than I have. and I'll be listening to those interviews <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1870_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1870\" data-vbnamecard=\"1870\">mlvalentine</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T11:25:04-08:00","id":1367043,"title":"","content":"The final chapter contains 'advice for creating player-facing compacts and conspiracies.' If you like a first edition compact or conspiracy, you now have the option of making a new one similar to it, having your players be vestiges of the last group and in control of the way it goes, or striving to regain relevancy, or have it never get dissolved in the first place.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I see this has been pointed out by now :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T12:07:56-08:00","id":1367055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367043#post1367043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The final chapter contains 'advice for creating player-facing compacts and conspiracies.' If you like a first edition compact or conspiracy, you now have the option of making a new one similar to it, having your players be vestiges of the last group and in control of the way it goes, or striving to regain relevancy, or have it never get dissolved in the first place.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I see this has been pointed out by now :P</div> </div> </div> </div>still appreciated. again, it's my fault for expecting things that were either purely wishful thinking or based on outdated (and not even official) info. besides, I'm a player, not a storyteller. while certainly some will just act like they never fell apart, the storytellers I know will also enjoy having them in a state of rebuilding or playing as a &quot;remnant&quot; like you said<br /> <br /> EDIT: CMON GET THAT STRETCH GOAL ALREADY","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-11-2020, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T12:23:46-08:00","id":1367062,"title":"","content":"I NO RITE! I know what the stretch goals are and it's killing me NOT to spoil the surprises in store!<br /> <br /> And Primordial newcomer, if it helps? I'm not offended at all. I can't expect everyone will be happy with the new edition or with changes. I can say a lot of thought went into each and every decision, but in the end it's a game that's meant to be played by you. You like what you like!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T12:31:11-08:00","id":1367063,"title":"","content":"Even without expectations of inclusion it's still valid to feel disappointed that they no longer canonically exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T12:50:26-08:00","id":1367067,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1870_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1870\" data-vbnamecard=\"1870\">mlvalentine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a>, thanks, but that does not excuse how I conducted myself. besides, as already proven, we may be canonically losing some groups (though I still hope in a idealistic and unrealistic way they all come back) we will be getting brand new groups to play with and enjoy. because of that, I'm slowly learning to accept it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T12:51:47-08:00","id":1367069,"title":"","content":"so since you are being so nice to talk to us. can you give us some hints on what future chapters of Tending the Flame will contain? like maybe more information on the core compacts and conspriacies or maybe new ones?<br /> <br /> So close to the next goal or like $30 more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T13:15:30-08:00","id":1367076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367069#post1367069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so since you are being so nice to talk to us. can you give us some hints on what future chapters of Tending the Flame will contain? like maybe more information on the core compacts and conspriacies or maybe new ones?<br /> <br /> So close to the next goal or like $30 more!</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, I'm reading all the comments and mentally saying &quot;BUT THAT... COULD BE...&quot; which is also why I've been refreshing the Kickstarter to make sure we hit more stretch goals. The corebook only gives us so much room!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T13:32:56-08:00","id":1367078,"title":"","content":"8 more dollars, we are so close its painful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer"