mordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-11-2020, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T16:23:13-08:00","id":1367118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367105#post1367105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont think hunter was as popular as Geist in first edition, but looking at its numbers, I think it's safe to assume we will get a tier 3 section<br /> <br /> EDIT: also, I like how the Council of Bones endowment is specifically tied to ghost. otherwise I, and i assume a good number of others, would of assumed spirits would be in effect too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter straight up was more popular than Geist. Mostly as a result of not having been screwed over by the circumstances of the time, but Geist was a cult hit where Hunter was more of a mainstream success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-11-2020, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T16:35:00-08:00","id":1367120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367118#post1367118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter straight up was more popular than Geist. Mostly as a result of not having been screwed over by the circumstances of the time, but Geist was a cult hit where Hunter was more of a mainstream success.</div> </div> </div> </div>ahh ok, thank you for the clarification (I was not around when Hunter the Vigil was a new gameline)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T00:07:47-08:00","id":1367173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367120#post1367120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ahh ok, thank you for the clarification (I was not around when Hunter the Vigil was a new gameline)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think hunter comes in 5th in general popularity behind the core 3 (vamp, wolf and mage) and then only beaten by changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T05:09:26-08:00","id":1367198,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/339646881/hunter-the-vigil-second-edition-tabletop-roleplaying-game/posts/2751716\" target=\"_blank\">Preview for Network Zero and the Council of Bones is up.</a><br /> <br /> The NetZos have been delayed in becoming a conspiracy due to internet trolls and fake news, which seems reasonable. Trolls will &quot;disprove&quot; things just to be jerks, when it's actually threatening their sense of security and pet politics I bet they'd turn outright vicious and borderline violent - to say nothing of the monsters manipulating them.<br /> <br /> The Council of Bones is awesome, as expected. They're apparently experts at surviving their own destruction, much to nobody's surprise given their Endowment; they just recovered from their latest mess. Also, nice contrast between being the most warlike on the concept of &quot;darkness&quot;, seeing it as an infection - and being the most pleasant and peaceful towards living monsters. If it's not undead and it doesn't kill people, it's not a threat and should be judged innocent until guilty. The writeup also outright calls ghosts &quot;people&quot; at one point, so the majority don't even view ghosts as monsters (the Diviners are an exception, but they're explicitly a minority and even then they're mostly trying to free ghosts from self-destructive undeath).<br /> <br /> This also means that Sin-Eaters (not Bound in general) are going to have an even split:<br /> <br /> &quot;I say it came back from the dead! It's obviously a monster!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;'<i>She </i>has a heartbeat, ages normally, and in the intervening time she was a ghost - you know, a person? This is obviously a lucky ghost and is doing our job for us!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T05:42:37-08:00","id":1367199,"title":"","content":"Add &quot;Probably Manipulated by a Number of Ghost Conspiracies(Council of Bones)&quot; to that Conspiracies Relationship list of mine, even if the Diviners have the good sense to keep their eyes wary and their knives sharp. Still, as THAT subject goes, this is actually a better balanced relationship than not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T05:47:57-08:00","id":1367200,"title":"","content":"Also, I have it that the Council of Bones became certain of the ability to see by staring into reflective surfaces from hearing the story told to them by the ghost of someone who made an incredibly accurate prediction by staring into the surface of a frozen lake. <br /> <br /> The vision being &quot;You will die of hypothermia after falling into a frozen lake.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T07:01:11-08:00","id":1367210,"title":"","content":"To me, Council of Bones is simply Sin-Eaters as hunters, 'stealing' idea of various interpretations of krewes around the world. For me, Council can easily take place of most Sin-Eaters in NPCs for various CoD stories - which have it's perks in prepering stories. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T07:22:20-08:00","id":1367215,"title":"","content":"I'm still not sure about how I feel about the Council. While the principle sounds great, some things about them feel a bit off- not that they are bad or something, just that I'm not sure they are for my liking.<br /> <br /> I did liked Network 0's writeup, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T07:30:48-08:00","id":1367217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367210#post1367210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, Council of Bones is simply Sin-Eaters as hunters, 'stealing' idea of various interpretations of krewes around the world. For me, Council can easily take place of most Sin-Eaters in NPCs for various CoD stories - which have it's perks in prepering stories. \ud83d\ude0e</div> </div> </div> </div>Watch for the Council of Bones appearance in the story I wrote for the Geist 2E anthology! Remember: hunters don't know bupkiss about what they're dealing with and many CoB hunters don't even know they have a mark or how their powers work. They're stumbling at shadows, whereas Sin-Eaters know quite a bit more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T10:22:44-08:00","id":1367256,"title":"","content":"surprised Netz0 is not close to a conspiracy, but the reasoning is very sound. love the whole write-up.<br /> <br /> The Council is very welcome, no surprise they resurrect every now and then due to being tied with ghost. I'm also very intrigued by the origins of their endowment. there must be some kinda catch to it. they seem to have a lot more freedom than other conspiracies, and decidedly arent, at least overtly, being influenced by ghosts or any other supernatural. perhaps when they die, does the mark take its share (perhaps turned into a reaper?). I also like how they seem to be one of the only conspiracies that can easily crossover with others. all in all, a lot of story-hooks can involve purely the past of this conspiracy and the Mark of the Scythe. Perspiritism itself is cool, though very niche for a corebook conspiracy. much like Les Mysteres aced the &quot;Shaman&quot; hunter, we finally have a conspiracy that let's us truly feel like ghostly occultists (yeah I know geist does it, but you know, council gives it that very &quot;otherworldly&quot; feel)<br /> <br /> so yeah, loved the two. I've also noticed that while in 1st edition, every group had its &quot;extremists who will risk everything morally&quot;, 2nd edition seems to be giving them more depth beyond that (sure the Faithful of the Long Night are quite brutal still, but I like their presentation in C&amp;Cs, which I think is still relevant to them here). the Diviners for example, while seeing ghosts as monsters too, arent going to just slaughter them, but rather be far less trusting (and for good reason).<br /> <br /> EDIT: also have to get the Geist Anthology now. love seeing how supernaturals react to Hunters that use endowments and what they get wrong. <br /> <br /> EDIT: also, would love to play the council during the Victorian era","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-12-2020, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T20:02:31-08:00","id":1367380,"title":"","content":"I had an idea a while ago for Doubting Souls (because Keepers of the Light read more like a snapshot of native Tier 1 Cells, than carrying any thematic niche as a Compact) of a Wampanoag Compact called Kakitonckqueban (\u201cThey are Dead and Gone\u201d) that was born out of the Great Dying of 1616-1619 to address the restless dead and help bring them peace and preserve their memory. I\u2019m now thinking of making them an an incarnation of what white Spiritualists would name the Council of Bones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T05:50:25-08:00","id":1367512,"title":"","content":"holy shit. that story was disgusting, in a good way of course. damn, how the fuck did sakamoto even survive that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-13-2020, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T12:22:04-08:00","id":1367578,"title":"","content":"Say, don't you think it would be cool if the numbers in the Mark of the Scythe represents something like the number of years taken as payment for the gift of Perispiritism? Or perhaps it is some sort of a doomsday clock, that every time it propagates to new hunters the number drops until reaching 0- which is when Reapers and ghosts and geists oh my come to destroy the conspiracy until it will be rebuilt once more?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T13:28:17-08:00","id":1367589,"title":"","content":"So what information do we have on the disbanding of Les Mysteres? Is it just being retconned or did something happen diegetically? Has there been any comment on why they were removed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T13:33:20-08:00","id":1367593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367589#post1367589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what information do we have on the disbanding of Les Mysteres? Is it just being retconned or did something happen diegetically? Has there been any comment on why they were removed?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were not retconned- there is one line in the Council's writeup which says that they are now defunct, and it seems to be tied to how they were treated by other hunters, which seems to be how they were so open about their Endowments. Not much, and most of its is my understanding due to context, but that's what we have.<br /> <br /> Also- another stretch goal slain!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T14:06:00-08:00","id":1367599,"title":"","content":"I wonder what the reason for that writing decision was? To much of a sense they were patsies of a greater threat being used to make humanity more vulnerable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T19:29:49-08:00","id":1367668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367599#post1367599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what the reason for that writing decision was? To much of a sense they were patsies of a greater threat being used to make humanity more vulnerable?</div> </div> </div> </div>while obviously I'm not a fan of it, I think the reason is less because they could be used as patsies (there are just as many savvy hunters who were not easily manipulated by spirits) and more because their powers were so blatantly in concert with the supernatural, supernatural creatures that were known drive good people to terrible things and Claim them.<br /> <br /> main reasoning for NOT being due to being patsies is since so many hunters suspect other conspiracies being used by the monsters (and while the Lucifuge are unpopular due to their supposed origins, their powers at least seem to control the supernatural, NOT form a symbiosis with it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T03:34:36-08:00","id":1367720,"title":"","content":"Les Mysteres felt far more like an NPC antagonist group for Werewolf than a Hunter conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T04:26:21-08:00","id":1367723,"title":"","content":"So it seems that Watt and Fielding have finally killed each other. Well, it had to happen eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T04:44:59-08:00","id":1367726,"title":"","content":"The lucifuge are BLOODY AMAZING! The write up is great. By far my favourite conspiracy and I am a big fan of the way castigation works. I like the addiction as an inherent downside, really should keep players on the edge of slipping to the dark side. <br /> <br /> Also we get clarification on Demons Vs Demons via the infernal dread power - looking forward to how that plays out in the antagonist chapter. <br /> <br /> Lastly, tid bits about Angels. I kinda hope we get some celestial Angels in the antagonist chapter. I believe the old Inferno had some? It has been a while (also inferno 2e when!) <br /> <br /> Otherwise I am tempted to now go convert all the old castigation rites to the new format, any interest in seeing that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T04:59:37-08:00","id":1367731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordofIron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367726#post1367726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise I am tempted to now go convert all the old castigation rites to the new format, any interest in seeing that?</div> </div> </div> </div>*raises hand*<br /> <br /> I like how the major Rites need a personal blood sacrifice too, it's both a good limiting factor and a major indication the Lucifuge is getting serious. LostLight had the best idea for why the Lucifuge can't bleed out others, though - that they're actually getting closer to victory and redeeming their blood, so it's lost the option for the selfish path that relies on victimizing others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T06:07:35-08:00","id":1367735,"title":"","content":"Yanluo Wang does NOT belong on that Satan figure list. He rules he\u2019ll and punishes the wicked to karmically cleanse them for reincarnation, but he is not seen as an incarnation of evil that is an \u201cadversary\u201d figure to Heaven or humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T06:20:35-08:00","id":1367737,"title":"","content":"I'm finding the frequent &quot;spellplage syndrome&quot;/&quot;plot progression&quot; in hunter 2e abit frustrating. I'd prefer if it was handled through retcons and just the way the setting was in 2e like the other CofD gamelines do rather than having the setting progress, and repeatedly bring up &quot;That thing you liked doesn't exist anymore&quot; to people who know of the group and &quot;Here is a sentence that wont make any sense to you if you didn't play 1e&quot; to those who don't know the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-14-2020, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T07:28:38-08:00","id":1367751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367720#post1367720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Les Mysteres felt far more like an NPC antagonist group for Werewolf than a Hunter conspiracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could say the same about almost every conspiracy, especially the cainites to vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T07:51:23-08:00","id":1367758,"title":"","content":"Also, because I don't think it was mentioned, on the subject of the secret goal of reaching 1692 backers- February 1692 was when the Salem Witch Trials has started. The Kicksarter launched on February, and Doubting Souls was the first Dark Era for Hunter.<br /> <br /> WHAT ARE YOU HIDING?!?!?!?!?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T07:57:50-08:00","id":1367761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367731#post1367731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *raises hand*<br /> <br /> I like how the major Rites need a personal blood sacrifice too, it's both a good limiting factor and a major indication the Lucifuge is getting serious. LostLight had the best idea for why the Lucifuge can't bleed out others, though - that they're actually getting closer to victory and redeeming their blood, so it's lost the option for the selfish path that relies on victimizing others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this too. I plan to run a 2e game as soon as we have all the rules, and I'm leaning towards running a historical lucifuge game. I remember the sidebar in c&amp;c exploring that members of the lucifuge can live for hundreds of years, so have characters being recruited in the 1400's and then working up to modern day. The change with the sacrifice already seems like a great plot hook as to introduce as time goes on where the players older methods stop working, as swapping the rites back to allowing external sacrifice seems trivial mechanically.<br /> <br /> I will definitely look into castigation conversion. I think most of mortal remains works as is with a few tweaks, a few should probably be dropped (the werewolf totem one feels redundant with the new calling forth the pit for example). I think the big one missing is shackles of pandemonium. <br /> <br /> I will wait until the merits are out from char gen. I don't want to redo anything that may be converted to a merit (I feel familiar would be a better merit than an endowment under the new rules) when it's only a week or two away.<br /> <br /> Edit: I will also make a new thread when I do to not clutter this thread up with reworked castigations <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:59:21-08:00","id":1367782,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty disappointed in the NM write-up honestly. I've never been able to understand the value of a (long-lived!) compact which is in open denial of what they deal with, and preferred as in Compacts and Conspiracies where they sound more like they just want to apply the scientific method to understanding the supernatural. But here we have a bunch of lines about we can prove everyone wrong and if NM succeeds than the Vigil can end (?!) and generally doubling down on the more ridiculous version of things.<br /> <br /> Is there some other way to see it? What am I missing? Is this just a fascinating satire of rationalism over empiricism or something that I keep not getting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T09:14:56-08:00","id":1367785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367782#post1367782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty disappointed in the NM write-up honestly. I've never been able to understand the value of a (long-lived!) compact which is in open denial of what they deal with, and preferred as in Compacts and Conspiracies where they sound more like they just want to apply the scientific method to understanding the supernatural. But here we have a bunch of lines about we can prove everyone wrong and if NM succeeds than the Vigil can end (?!) and generally doubling down on the more ridiculous version of things.<br /> <br /> Is there some other way to see it? What am I missing? Is this just a fascinating satire of rationalism over empiricism or something that I keep not getting?</div> </div> </div> </div>From my reading of it, it is not that they want to prove that supernatural beings do not exist- what they want to prove is that they are not supernatural. That there is some theory or system or scientific way to categorize the darkness, and explaining how those species (not monsters!) exist. That magic is just a form of energy, and could be described through formulas and laws just like any form of energy. That other worlds could be explained through a system of equations. That the scientific method could be used even for the occult world, and by doing so explain it. And once you explain the supernatural as just a part of the system, you could use technology in order to keep up with it. You can develop tools and apparatuses and simulations which don't only explain how the darkness works, but can also predict it and utilize it. The Vigil will end not by destroying all monsters, but by showing they are not monsters- they are just a part of the natural world, and could be studied like any other aspect of it. And once the fire of knowledge is ignited, the fear from the dark vanishes. Oh, sure, those things you used to be fearful from are still there, but before the light you can study them, understand them, and utilize them. Once, lions and wolves and bears were monsters and gods who preyed upon humanity. Now, they are just one more species we need to protect from ourselves, for not only we understood them, we have also developed the tools to kill them, and the fear subsides.<br /> <br /> That is the end of the Vigil. That is the end of the supernatural. Whatever you were afraid of is still there, but through rational thought and scientific tools, you can understand it, and knowledge is the one thing that the darkness fears the most.<br /> <br /> At least, that's my reading of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T10:19:52-08:00","id":1367801,"title":"","content":"You know, before Demon, there was something maybe a little absurd with Null Mysteriis's ethos, but now with the God-Machine's occult physics on the scene, there's a good chance they're actually onto something.<br /> <br /> Also, that Status 5 benefit is quite the doozy.<br /> <br /> I agree with glamourweaver that Yanluo Wang doesn't really fit into the tempter paradigm; the Buddhist demon Mara would work much better in that list (as one example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T10:37:04-08:00","id":1367810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367782#post1367782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty disappointed in the NM write-up honestly. I've never been able to understand the value of a (long-lived!) compact which is in open denial of what they deal with, and preferred as in Compacts and Conspiracies where they sound more like they just want to apply the scientific method to understanding the supernatural. But here we have a bunch of lines about we can prove everyone wrong and if NM succeeds than the Vigil can end (?!) and generally doubling down on the more ridiculous version of things.<br /> <br /> Is there some other way to see it? What am I missing? Is this just a fascinating satire of rationalism over empiricism or something that I keep not getting?</div> </div> </div> </div>err... I\u2019m not sure where you\u2019re getting that. They\u2019re not claiming the phenomena they\u2019re witnessing doesn\u2019t exist. They\u2019re asserting that all things are \u201cnatural\u201d, and the so called \u201csupernatural\u201d are governed by natural law that aren\u2019t understood yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-14-2020, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T11:00:51-08:00","id":1367813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367782#post1367782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty disappointed in the NM write-up honestly. I've never been able to understand the value of a (long-lived!) compact which is in open denial of what they deal with, and preferred as in Compacts and Conspiracies where they sound more like they just want to apply the scientific method to understanding the supernatural. But here we have a bunch of lines about we can prove everyone wrong and if NM succeeds than the Vigil can end (?!) and generally doubling down on the more ridiculous version of things.<br /> <br /> Is there some other way to see it? What am I missing? Is this just a fascinating satire of rationalism over empiricism or something that I keep not getting?</div> </div> </div> </div>like LostLight said, they still want to understand the supernatural. their new write-up is more like that speech in compacts and conspiracies. the supernatural does not exist. vampires and werewolves and all that do exist. but there is nothing supernatural about them. with science, they will make them understood by humanity, not to be feared.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T15:31:51-08:00","id":1367893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1366980#post1366980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, Primordial newcomer. The history of compacts and conspiracies began to change when the Dark Eras line was added, much like DE affected Geist, too. All of a sudden global conspiracies either needed to have more history than they did or they had to be newer; compacts could (but not always) be temporary due to historical events/tragedies and changes over time. Knowing this, I wanted Hunter 2E to be a corebook that reflected that change while not fixating on Dark Eras. There were tons of compacts/conspiracies created as First Edition progressed, and I felt it made sense they'd be absorbed or dissolved because there are more denizens now in the Chronicles of Darkness than there was when Hunter 1E debuted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is not only have you thereby created a metaplot consisting mostly of \u201cYour fave is canonically gone now,\u201d but one that, without the benefit of this post to know the actual reasoning, reads (IMO) a lot like someone got it in their head somehow that any compact/conspiracy without a 2e corebook writeup has to have an in-universe reason why it didn\u2019t get one.<br /> <br /> How much consideration was given to the option of instead making up new compact/conspiracy names to drop as the examples of ones that have come and gone over time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 02-14-2020, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T15:43:21-08:00","id":1367897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367893#post1367893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Problem is not only have you thereby created a metaplot consisting mostly of \u201cYour fave is canonically gone now,\u201d but one that, without the benefit of this post to know the actual reasoning, reads (IMO) a lot like someone got it in their head somehow that any compact/conspiracy without a 2e corebook writeup has to have an in-universe reason why it didn\u2019t get one.<br /> <br /> How much consideration was given to the option of instead making up new compact/conspiracy names to drop as the examples of ones that have come and gone over time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the book does name drops a few new groups which have died out through the ages and refers to a number of supplementary organizations outside those in the book which are stated to still exist, I assume that the team have invested a lot of time and reasoning in those choices?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:34:56-08:00","id":1367915,"title":"","content":"I am guessing they are getting rid of and consolidating groups that have too much overlap? I mean while The Barret Comission and Division 6 are extra governmental they both kinda do the same thing for their chosen monster. So it makes a kinda sense to just fold them into TFV?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:40:44-08:00","id":1367916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367720#post1367720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Les Mysteres felt far more like an NPC antagonist group for Werewolf than a Hunter conspiracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>THis line bugs me, and I think I can illustrate why.<br /> <br /> Firstly-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, Valkyrie being <i>funded </i>by vampires(and that's important to distinguish, they are funded by vamps and expected to act in response to that rather than simply being run by them) is small potatoes compared to<br /> <br /> Actively Act In the Abyss's Favor to Keep It Quiet(Knights of St. George),<br /> Act as the Spirit's Ambassadors and Soldiers in the Conflict over the Border(Les Mysteres),<br /> Probably a Puppet for VII[Whatever the fuck they are](Cainite Heresy),<br /> Pretty Much Absolutely the Result of Shuankhsen Efforts(Feast of Shulpae),<br /> Has a God-Machine Angel as Their Driving Client(Knights of St. Adrian),<br /> Posers as Government Agents for the Panopticon(Division Six[compact, but worth mentioning]),<br /> Run by Extra-Dimensional Entities who Either Have Odd Ideas About Fighting the Apocalypse or Terrifying Ideas About Causing the Apocalypse and Oh By The Way Are Capitalist Fucks(Cheiron Group),<br /> Actively Serve an Actively Angry and Gluttonous Ghoul and are Possibly Powered by Really Warped Imitator of a God Who Is Already A Fuck(Malleus Maleficarum),<br /> Operate Under Probable-Metaphysical Gunpoint of a Woman of Indeterminate Origin(Lucifuge),<br /> [Probably Manipulated by a Number of Ghost Conspiracies(Council of Bone)]<br /> and Might Probably be Manipulated by the Most Judgmental Morally Grey Folks in Mage's Setup(Aegis Kai Doru).</div> </div> </div> </div>You might notice a trend here where Hunter Conspiracies are also shaped up to be in alignment with the enemies of their enemies, which means a default is that they naturally look like antagonist groups.<br /> <br /> Second:<br /> <br /> Hunters hunt monsters. Hunter are inherently fodder for NPC antagonist groups for any of the other gamelines. That's kind of the point.<br /> <br /> Anyways, nothing against youMorty, it's just the line itself pricks at my brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T18:23:50-08:00","id":1367944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367915#post1367915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am guessing they are getting rid of and consolidating groups that have too much overlap? I mean while The Barret Comission and Division 6 are extra governmental they both kinda do the same thing for their chosen monster. So it makes a kinda sense to just fold them into TFV?</div> </div> </div> </div>division 6 is not extra governmental, not initially. they certainly THOUGHT they were, but ultimately they were pawns tricked by a Panopticon Seer named Mr Jones. he showed them Panopticon &quot;tech&quot;, gave funding and badges in such a way that seemed straight of a government conspiracy, and gave hit lists. they dont do politics, they get training in suppressing magic (unwittingly utilizing paradox by focusing on mages using even subtle magic) and go to KILL mages.<br /> <br /> Barret Commission stayed on the political, military, and corporate business fronts. they did not kill (normally) vampires, but fought there very influence on the aforementioned 3 fronts. they were kept decentralized so vampires couldn't infiltrate them easily or just kill the leaders. that, and I think they didnt even know TFV existed.<br /> <br /> so two very different groups. while I disagree with getting rid of them, it's to show the Vigil is not something you just expect any compact to last a long time on, normally it's very short, with the ones we get being exceptions. considering we will have a dedicated DIY chapter for making our own groups, I think you will find it pretty difficult if not impossible that your DIT groups will have SUPERFICIAL similarities with already existing groups","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T18:33:15-08:00","id":1367946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1367893#post1367893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Problem is not only have you thereby created a metaplot consisting mostly of \u201cYour fave is canonically gone now,\u201d but one that, without the benefit of this post to know the actual reasoning, reads (IMO) a lot like someone got it in their head somehow that any compact/conspiracy without a 2e corebook writeup has to have an in-universe reason why it didn\u2019t get one.<br /> <br /> How much consideration was given to the option of instead making up new compact/conspiracy names to drop as the examples of ones that have come and gone over time?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But there ARE still non-core organizations that still exist within the Hunter 2niversE that haven't been consolidated or defunct. Both the Promethean Brotherhood and the Faithful of Shulpae exist (as examples of hunters that may have jumped off the deep end) as well as the Knights of Saint Adrian , Knights of Saint George, and Utopia Now. Some organizations were subsumed by the more influential organizations (&quot;Why does Ross, the largest friend, simply not eat the other five?&quot;) or eventually developed into a more modern-esque organization. I think that, of the organizations still unmentioned, there are:<br /> -Night Watch<br /> -Maiden's Blood Sisterhood<br /> -The Cainite Heresy<br /> -The Illuminated Brotherhood<br /> -The Talbot Group<br /> -Keepers of the Source<br /> -Habibti Ma<br /> -Yuri's Group<br /> -The Reckoning<br /> -Some of the Dark Era organizations<br /> <br /> Some of the above organizations, while good concepts, I can see being absorbed into pre-existing organizations (Night Watch into The Union or a consolidation of Yuri's Group, The Talbot Group, and Maiden's Blood into a support group) or would probably collapse (Keepers of the Source, almost hands down for me). However, they still had existed in some shape or form and may even still have some surviving hunters or even cells that made it out. Ahl al-Jabal is stated to have a very vague fate (which I assume is intentional by writing), having either disappeared in time, endured throughout the centuries, or have been co-opted by a different hunter group.<br /> <br /> I would like to say that the writing does not seem to be an attempt to justify anything. Rather, the writing is showing that the nature of Hunter organizations and the Vigil is fragile and subject to the whims of time. Some organizations stay, some organizations go, some organizations dig in their nails into the group and are dragged into other organizations in order to stay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T14:44:49-08:00","id":1368138,"title":"","content":"so less then $100 till our next goal and then on to Tending the Flames Compacts in another four grand! I know it seems hard but we can do it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T15:06:38-08:00","id":1368141,"title":"","content":"We're also about 350 backers away from getting the secret stretch goal. If even half those backers each pledge the $25 to get a copy of the PDF, we'll hit both goals. 18 days left, so I'm in high hopes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T15:13:36-08:00","id":1368145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368138#post1368138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so less then $100 till our next goal and then on to Tending the Flames Compacts in another four grand! I know it seems hard but we can do it!</div> </div> </div> </div>trust me, we will make that one. you will be most likely surprised to see how far we go by the end of this kickstarter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T15:32:17-08:00","id":1368148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368145#post1368145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> trust me, we will make that one. you will be most likely surprised to see how far we go by the end of this kickstarter</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm all hopes that we will smash through the stretch goals, at least until the third part of the Player's Guide! We can't let the Mummy incident return itself..<br /> <br /> Also, one stretch goal down!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T15:34:32-08:00","id":1368150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368148#post1368148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all hopes that we will smash through the stretch goals, at least until the third part of the Player's Guide! We can't let the Mummy incident return itself..<br /> <br /> Also, one stretch goal down!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more confident for this one simply because hunter is not as a niche as mummy (damn was I still sad by that though. still, I will be content with getting the section on conspiracies...until we see an epic stretch goal next)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T00:46:39-08:00","id":1368238,"title":"","content":"Wait what compacts and conspiracies did they cut?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T02:06:35-08:00","id":1368251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368238#post1368238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait what compacts and conspiracies did they cut?</div> </div> </div> </div>All the corebook organizations are represented in some way, with Ashwood Abbey and Aegis Kai Doru being deconstructed to explain the Compact/Conspiracy creation rules.<br /> <br /> Currently, we know that Barrett Commission and Division Six were absorbed by VALKYRIE while the Merrick Institute was disbanded in some way by VALKYRIE. Les Mysteres are defunct as well. The Bear Lodge was absorbed by Ashwood Abbey. Some of the Dark Era organizations had a mention as well but, as they are built within their time, they eventually evolved or disbanded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T05:38:36-08:00","id":1368284,"title":"","content":"Merrick Institute? Do they mean the secret government Faculty that tested on Teenagers got disbanded? <br /> <br /> And not the dream hunting conspiracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T08:48:07-08:00","id":1368304,"title":"","content":"damn, really hoping we can get that secret stretch goal revealed to us, freaking killing me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T09:08:48-08:00","id":1368307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368284#post1368284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merrick Institute? Do they mean the secret government Faculty that tested on Teenagers got disbanded?<br /> <br /> And not the dream hunting conspiracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>That looks like the consensus among those forums, at the very least. The other option makes a little sense in the context. On the other hand, we don't know what was the intention of the writer- but that would be how I'll use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T09:25:28-08:00","id":1368309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368307#post1368307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That looks like the consensus among those forums, at the very least. The other option makes a little sense in the context. On the other hand, we don't know what was the intention of the writer- but that would be how I'll use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>the most I can take from if it's the hunters that were absorbed, is if it was that faction that wanted to centralize managed to gain enough influence. otherwise, they are too unwilling to gain some organization, with a 3rd of them being extremists against it (the firebrands)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T10:26:31-08:00","id":1368320,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m still not clear on how the SWORN differ from the Union except in demographic. I love having a native group, but I hope they aren\u2019t just another example of the infinitely reskinnable \u201ccommunity defenders\u201d Compact archetype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T10:48:55-08:00","id":1368326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368307#post1368307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That looks like the consensus among those forums, at the very least. The other option makes a little sense in the context. On the other hand, we don't know what was the intention of the writer- but that would be how I'll use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, it refers to the 'Merrick Institute', which is specifically the name of the Hunter conspiracy. The researchers group were 'Merrick Research'. Also, the researchers weren't really hunters, which is the focus of the paragraph.<br /> <br /> I mean seeing as the same paragraph refers to both Division VI and the Barrett Commission as 'government sanctioned'; maybe the author was going off of memory and got confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T10:53:32-08:00","id":1368328,"title":"","content":"Currently, I am too feel a bit not too drawn to SWORN- even though I assume that most of its history is outside of my culture. While I can see how I could reskin it for a different population, currently they see much like the Union, but for Native Americans. I can understand the compel it may offer for Native Americans, as it draws directly from their history, however. Perhaps the full writeup would offer more ways to connect to it. I have hoped to see some mention to the Keepers of the Weave (or even the Wardens of Light), but I can understand why there wasn't, as the writeup details how much of their traditions were lost through the actions of the US government. Still, I kind of hope that we'll see how they differ from the Union in terms of their methods and themes. They were, after all, said to be focused around Cryptids- which could give the needed twist to differ them from other similar groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T10:54:53-08:00","id":1368330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368326#post1368326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, it refers to the 'Merrick Institute', which is specifically the name of the Hunter conspiracy. The researchers group were 'Merrick Research'. Also, the researchers weren't really hunters, which is the focus of the paragraph.<br /> <br /> I mean seeing as the same paragraph refers to both Division VI and the Barrett Commission as 'government sanctioned'; maybe the author was going off of memory and got confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>true. still, I have too much of a soft spot for the Merrick kids to be lost. cool powers and already had conflict within the group","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-16-2020, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T11:18:54-08:00","id":1368334,"title":"","content":"If it\u2019s still in the final text preview during the errata phase I\u2019m reporting it. I really think the author misunderstood what those groups were. The only true US government backed hunters besides TFV are VASCU, who specifically DIDN\u2019T get absorbed!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key"