>?</div> </div> </div> </div>The history section- the part that details how the Barrette Commission and Division VI were folded into VALKYRIE, while Merrick was dissolved after the congressional inquiry. Reading the reference to Merrick as the &quot;children conspiracy&quot; doesn't make much sense, IMO, while as the original organization which did the experiment makes a lot of sense. Because there is a lack of clarity about which organization is referred in that line, people are confused about whether or not that line makes sense, especially in the context of Division VI which was never a part of the government. And if you were to talk about the &quot;children conspiracy&quot;, people wonder what happened to them, and for some reason, TFV murdering them all was suggested.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T15:49:28-08:00","id":1368424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368420#post1368420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The history section- the part that details how the Barrette Commission and Division VI were folded into VALKYRIE, while Merrick was dissolved after the congressional inquiry. Reading the reference to Merrick as the &amp;quot;children conspiracy&amp;quot; doesn't make much sense, IMO, while as the original organization which did the experiment makes a lot of sense. Because there is a lack of clarity about which organization is referred in that line, people are confused about whether or not that line makes sense, especially in the context of Division VI which was never a part of the government. And if you were to talk about the &amp;quot;children conspiracy&amp;quot;, people wonder what happened to them, and for some reason, TFV murdering them all was suggested.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>all I can see now is TFV killing kids Anakin style lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T15:58:13-08:00","id":1368425,"title":"","content":"shit the text preview supposedly says that TFV Dissolved the Merrick institute.another user says it probably refers to the Conspiracy of Experimented on Kids with ties to the primdiol dream and not the secret Government Research lab experimented on the Kids. and after what they went through it\u2019s not like TFV can be hey kids sorry about that gross violation of human rights and tourture want john TFV?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T16:17:31-08:00","id":1368426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368425#post1368425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">shit the text preview supposedly says that TFV Dissolved the Merrick institute.another user says it probably refers to the Conspiracy of Experimented on Kids with ties to the primdiol dream and not the secret Government Research lab experimented on the Kids. and after what they went through it\u2019s not like TFV can be hey kids sorry about that gross violation of human rights and tourture want john TFV?</div> </div> </div> </div>still a huge leap to assume that they just straight up killed everyone though.<br /> also it wasn't even TFV that did it. It says the Merrick Institute couldn't survive a congressional inquiry and was shut down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","user":"Grimmi05","date":". 02-16-2020, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T16:20:11-08:00","id":1368427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368424#post1368424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> all I can see now is TFV killing kids Anakin style lol</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Agent Kender, there are too many of them, what are we gonna do?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, I've always wondered what this angel gun does.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T16:27:31-08:00","id":1368429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368425#post1368425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">shit the text preview supposedly says that TFV Dissolved the Merrick institute.another user says it probably refers to the Conspiracy of Experimented on Kids with ties to the primdiol dream and not the secret Government Research lab experimented on the Kids. and after what they went through it\u2019s not like TFV can be hey kids sorry about that gross violation of human rights and tourture want john TFV?</div> </div> </div> </div>The text says a <b><i>congressional inquiry </i></b>dissolved the Merrick Institute. TFV is referenced as an alternative option for the Barrett Commission and Division Six (being absorbed), which were seen as more salvageable. The confusion stems from two sources. Three if we count an assumption.<ul><li>The Merrick Institute is used as one of the names for the research group and the runaway test subjects that formed the playable hunter group.</li> <li>People conflating Taskforce Valkyrie with Congress.</li> <li>The assumption that 'dissolved' means killed, arrested or otherwise dealt with in a permanent manner.</li> </ul><br /> Honestly I would have thought that the Barrett Commission would have been better suited to be folded into VASCU given their (Barrett's) nonviolent methods dealing with supernaturals. Likewise, some of those researchers from Merrick could've been 'reallocated' to refining/improving the Wintergreen process.<br /> <br /> It makes little sense that the runaway children would have any meaningful connection to the government, so it is <b><i>incredibly </i></b>unlikely that the official dissolution of the Merrick Institute would have any effect on them whatsoever, in and of itself. So the alternative (that this use of the Merrick Institute refers to the researchers) is more likely correct. Now this does raise some interesting questions, such as:<ul><li>What did the government do to the test subjects the Institute still had in custody?</li> <li>Are the runaway test subjects/hunters still being hunted?</li> <li>How do the hunters resupply/recruit when the facilities they used to raid are all shut down?</li> <li>What happened to the research?</li> </ul><br /> None of which imply that Hunter 2e removed them as a playable faction, let alone <b>MURDERED THEM.</b><br /> We haven't gotten a full book yet, could we not jump to conclusions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T19:19:35-08:00","id":1368447,"title":"","content":"I do want to say that, of the organizations that have been previewed, both the Ascending Ones and the Cheiron Group have an implicit threat to their organization or their hunters: the Ascending Ones are being infiltrated as the Cult of Set did centuries ago and the Cheiron Group are dealing with Sweetwater and a sudden influx of reportedly rogue agents. The Lucifuge now have to answer to the Lady, who is much more active in directing the hunters with the Will of the Lucifuge, which checks out and is less of a threat and more of an agreement. I wonder if this will follow into Malleus Malificarum, VALKYRIE, and VASCU and have them dealing with more internal issues and conflicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T21:28:57-08:00","id":1368457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368420#post1368420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">especially in the context of Division VI which was never a part of the government. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Div6 obviously <i>wanted </i>to be &quot;absorbed&quot; in TFV. The Seers were sick of the vampires controlling TFV, and decided it was time to move in-house.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T02:05:06-08:00","id":1368493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368457#post1368457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Div6 obviously <i>wanted </i>to be &quot;absorbed&quot; in TFV. The Seers were sick of the vampires controlling TFV, and decided it was time to move in-house.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I personally have no issue with that change (I can rationalize it easily, like how you suggested, and I was never a fan of the group so I don't care very much about them). However, some people think that unexplained changes like that makes them feel that the writer have not done their research properly. I can understand where they are coming from, and it won't be the first time a writer for 2e misunderstands the original material, but in the case of Division VI I don't think it was the case- it is just that without any further clarification, it could look odd to those who know the source material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T02:16:06-08:00","id":1368497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368493#post1368493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I personally have no issue with that change (I can rationalize it easily, like how you suggested, and I was never a fan of the group so I don't care very much about them). However, some people think that unexplained changes like that makes them feel that the writer have not done their research properly. I can understand where they are coming from, and it won't be the first time a writer for 2e misunderstands the original material, but in the case of Division VI I don't think it was the case- it is just that without any further clarification, it could look odd to those who know the source material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Division 6's change felt natural. Personally I thought Merrick Institute/Research being being shut down the instance there was a through check on them was also a comfortable and predictable alteration; no one wants their name stamped on child torture after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T03:08:42-08:00","id":1368500,"title":"","content":"There is only question how children from Merrick program should be called now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T03:16:13-08:00","id":1368502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368500#post1368500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is only question how children from Merrick program should be called now...</div> </div> </div> </div>Survivors, dreamers and independents...the Children of Merrick were never numerous. Honestly, they felt like a Compact with an Endowment to me.<br /> But then again, those same Children have had time to grow up now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T03:23:28-08:00","id":1368503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368502#post1368502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Survivors, dreamers and independents...the Children of Merrick were never numerous. Honestly, they felt like a Compact with an Endowment to me.<br /> But then again, those same Children have had time to grow up now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly the answer is probably \u201cRenegades\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T04:12:06-08:00","id":1368509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368503#post1368503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly the answer is probably \u201cRenegades\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>But would they be Deviants then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T04:12:51-08:00","id":1368510,"title":"","content":"Is new previe a bit late? Last four come up about hour before..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T04:26:44-08:00","id":1368512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368509#post1368509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But would they be Deviants then?</div> </div> </div> </div>yes, that was my point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T05:15:52-08:00","id":1368514,"title":"","content":"The preview is up and I'm pleasantly surprised by both SWORN and Malleus Malificarum for two separate reasons.<br /> <br /> It's so interesting that SWORN categorizes monsters into things that should exist and are okay to live and things to eradicate. Guess now that Promethean has an organization that would be specifically eyeing them down. It's also very interesting to see that SWORN has an explicitly cloistered faction within them that are, let's say unpleasant to deal with. It seems like it will be a divisive addition, but I can understand the implications as to why that faction exists.<br /> <br /> Seeing that Benedictions have a new rule and way to actually activate them makes me excited. I'm very happy to see that the writers are experimenting with Endowments and making them feel even more unique and keyed to a specific Conspiracy. Additionally, the sister getting ready to throw hands is possibly my favorite piece of artwork I've seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T09:13:01-08:00","id":1368543,"title":"","content":"On Flames Rising, we have another designers write up on <b>HtV </b>2E - This time, about new organisations - <a href=\"http://www.flamesrising.com/htv2e-introducing-the-new-hunter-compact-sworn/\" target=\"_blank\">Nine Stars, Council of Bones - and mainly, SWORN</a>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-17-2020, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T16:29:38-08:00","id":1368642,"title":"","content":"This is a preview ago now, but thank you for good and clear responses to my flailing about the NM. I was reacting to keywords and old associations more than I was the overall thrust of the write-up. My problems are really disliking a couple sentences more than the thing I loved about the NM disappearing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T23:32:51-08:00","id":1368691,"title":"","content":"Just asking but isn't the benefit of having Rank 3 Status in the Malleus Maleficarum...kind of useless. I mean everyone else gets an actual benefit at the odd levels but this just gives you the 4th Rank for free, which has little value since your going to want to get to Rank 5 eventually and you're going to have less than the other factions to show for it.<br /> <br /> ...and why did the Wrathful Sword of St. Michael the Archangel get such as MASSIVE nerf?!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24424-magus-black","name":"Magus Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T00:14:57-08:00","id":1368695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368691#post1368691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just asking but isn't the benefit of having Rank 3 Status in the Malleus Maleficarum...kind of useless. I mean everyone else gets an actual benefit at the odd levels but this just gives you the 4th Rank for free, which has little value since your going to want to get to Rank 5 eventually and you're going to have less than the other factions to show for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm almost willing to bet that the extra rank in MM is an oversight considering that Status 3 in 1E MM grants you a dot in Status (The Church).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T01:45:42-08:00","id":1368700,"title":"","content":"Hope so, but still I'm worried about Wrathful Sword being made totally useless against their primary foes (Vampires). I mean it was suppose to be a somewhat hazardous but useful tool to slay vampires that didn't require you to chain them to a chair and stake `em. But now...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24424-magus-black","name":"Magus Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T03:27:45-08:00","id":1368707,"title":"","content":"Vampires are arguably the thing Wrathful Sword is the <i>most </i>useful against, because it lets you deal lethal damage to an enemy that otherwise downgrades all damage from mundane weapons to bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T05:44:27-08:00","id":1368718,"title":"","content":"Less than 2000$ till Compacts chapter in Companion book!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T05:58:20-08:00","id":1368724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368707#post1368707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are arguably the thing Wrathful Sword is the <i>most </i>useful against, because it lets you deal lethal damage to an enemy that otherwise downgrades all damage from mundane weapons to bashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that's true. but damn was aggravated damage so satisfying","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T07:00:57-08:00","id":1368738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368724#post1368724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that's true. but damn was aggravated damage so satisfying</div> </div> </div> </div>2e in general has made aggravated damage a fair bit rarer as well as making weapon damage higher at base.<br /> <br /> 1e's version of Wrathful Sword had a set <i>total amount</i> of aggravated damage it could inflict, cost two Willpower to use, lasted a scene or less, destroyed the weapon after its effects ended, and rolled Strength + Benediction alone as an instant with the +5 dice if you used it on Michaelmas.<br /> <br /> The previewed version of Wrathful Sword gives the weapon a consistently lethal damage modifier against a set of entities that include many with &quot;this thing doesn't have organs, so weapons deal bashing damage against it&quot; as an innate quality, costs one Willpower to use, lasts for a day, makes no mention of destroying the blessed weapon, and rolls Intelligence + Occult + Benediction as an extended action.<br /> <br /> Bumping the latter up to full aggravated damage changes the power dramatically more than giving it a utility bump; there's &quot;satisfying&quot; and then there's &quot;giving a level of access to aggravated damage that amounts to casual vaporization to people who are still supposed to be relative underdogs among the supernatural.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T07:17:52-08:00","id":1368742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368738#post1368738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e in general has made aggravated damage a fair bit rarer as well as making weapon damage higher at base.<br /> <br /> 1e's version of Wrathful Sword had a set <i>total amount</i> of aggravated damage it could inflict, cost two Willpower to use, lasted a scene or less, destroyed the weapon after its effects ended, and rolled Strength + Benediction alone as an instant with the +5 dice if you used it on Michaelmas.<br /> <br /> The previewed version of Wrathful Sword gives the weapon a consistently lethal damage modifier against a set of entities that include many with &amp;quot;this thing doesn't have organs, so weapons deal bashing damage against it&amp;quot; as an innate quality, costs one Willpower to use, lasts for a day, makes no mention of destroying the blessed weapon, and rolls Intelligence + Occult + Benediction as an extended action.<br /> <br /> Bumping the latter up to full aggravated damage changes the power dramatically more than giving it a utility bump; there's &amp;quot;satisfying&amp;quot; and then there's &amp;quot;giving a level of access to aggravated damage that amounts to casual vaporization to people who are still supposed to be relative underdogs among the supernatural.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, that makes sense. the utility is pretty good. huh, now that I think about it, while it does cost a dot, the boon of Lazarus has gotten a buff if you ask me. no more persistent condition (sure 5 minutes or less, but still)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T14:46:29-08:00","id":1368801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368707#post1368707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are arguably the thing Wrathful Sword is the <i>most </i>useful against, because it lets you deal lethal damage to an enemy that otherwise downgrades all damage from mundane weapons to bashing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hate to break it to but that isn't what it says at all.<br /> <br /> All the ability says is that it REPLACES your Weapons normal Damage with your Benedicition Ranking...nothing more, it doesn't grant you the ability to ignore defensive abilities or acts like Bane to the creatures your attack. So a vampire will still reduce ALL Damage to Bashing.<br /> <br /> That's why the ability is useless as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24424-magus-black","name":"Magus Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T15:12:16-08:00","id":1368806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368801#post1368801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hate to break it to but that isn't what it says at all.<br /> <br /> All the ability says is that it REPLACES your Weapons normal Damage with your Benedicition Ranking...nothing more, it doesn't grant you the ability to ignore defensive abilities or acts like Bane to the creatures your attack. So a vampire will still reduce ALL Damage to Bashing.<br /> <br /> That's why the ability is useless as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>it does specify that the lethal damage applies to monsters. at the very least, that implies its lethal to vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T15:24:06-08:00","id":1368809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368801#post1368801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hate to break it to but that isn't what it says at all.<br /> <br /> All the ability says is that it REPLACES your Weapons normal Damage with your Benedicition Ranking...nothing more, it doesn't grant you the ability to ignore defensive abilities or acts like Bane to the creatures your attack. So a vampire will still reduce ALL Damage to Bashing.<br /> <br /> That's why the ability is useless as written.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Vampire: the Requiem 2E, pg. 90</b>, bold emphasis mine. &quot;Kindred take only bashing damage from <b>many sources</b> that would normally cause lethal damage to humans. This includes most <b>non-supernatural weapons</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> The 2E version of Wrathful Sword states that the weapon is imbued with divine power. I would like to argue that the weapon would be considered supernatural and would bypass a Vampire's ability to reduce lethal damage to bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T15:35:53-08:00","id":1368811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368801#post1368801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hate to break it to but that isn't what it says at all.<br /> <br /> All the ability says is that it REPLACES your Weapons normal Damage with your Benedicition Ranking...nothing more, it doesn't grant you the ability to ignore defensive abilities or acts like Bane to the creatures your attack. So a vampire will still reduce ALL Damage to Bashing.<br /> <br /> That's why the ability is useless as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to be sorry about it, because you're not actually &quot;breaking&quot; anything to me. Here's what the Benediction's text says:<br /> <br /> &quot;When wielded against a monster, the weapon has a lethal damage rating equal to the hunter\u2019s Benediction rating.&quot;<br /> <br /> This means it specifically deals lethal damage to monsters. It would be rather redundant against mortals, who take lethal damage from all weapons anyhow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T16:40:31-08:00","id":1368821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368809#post1368809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Vampire: the Requiem 2E, pg. 90</b>, bold emphasis mine. &quot;Kindred take only bashing damage from <b>many sources</b> that would normally cause lethal damage to humans. This includes most <b>non-supernatural weapons</b>.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The 2E version of Wrathful Sword states that the weapon is imbued with divine power. I would like to argue that the weapon would be considered supernatural and would bypass a Vampire's ability to reduce lethal damage to bashing.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Perhaps that's my problem here 'argue' would imply that there is a bit </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">ambiguousness to that the old didn't have...perhaps they could put a bit in to clarify that. Most 'supernatural weapons' are of the more...permanent variety after all.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368811#post1368811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No need to be sorry about it, because you're not actually &quot;breaking&quot; anything to me. Here's what the Benediction's text says:<br /> <br /> &quot;When wielded against a monster, the weapon has a lethal damage rating equal to the hunter\u2019s Benediction rating.&quot;<br /> <br /> This means it specifically deals lethal damage to monsters. It would be rather redundant against mortals, who take lethal damage from all weapons anyhow.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand the (as written) benefit to this is taking a small (Damage 0) weapon and making it a Damage 5 Pen-knife of Doom, which is how I see the point of the ability as its currently written. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24424-magus-black","name":"Magus Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T17:31:12-08:00","id":1368825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368821#post1368821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Perhaps that's my problem here 'argue' would imply that there is a bit </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">ambiguousness to that the old didn't have...perhaps they could put a bit in to clarify that. Most 'supernatural weapons' are of the more...permanent variety after all.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand the (as written) benefit to this is taking a small (Damage 0) weapon and making it a Damage 5 Pen-knife of Doom, which is how I see the point of the ability as its currently written. <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>as it's currently written, is to allow truly meaningful damage to a monster who normally would just downgrade the damage. the fact it makes a weapon inherently Lethal to monsters is a bonus (and it make it impossible for them to take the blessed wooden bat from you and deal lethal damage with it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T21:11:17-08:00","id":1368852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368821#post1368821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Perhaps that's my problem here 'argue' would imply that there is a bit </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">ambiguousness to that the old didn't have...perhaps they could put a bit in to clarify that. Most 'supernatural weapons' are of the more...permanent variety after all.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The 1E iteration of Wrathful Sword explicitly did aggravated damage, which in general nothing resists. That's probably why there's ambiguity now that wasn't there. Additionally, the Endowments in 2E are explicitly stated to be supernatural (&quot;Hunters are not supernatural, but the Endowments they use are.&quot; Under 'Using Endowments', Manuscript Preview #1 and Ascending Ones), so the 2E iteration of Wrathful Sword should affect Vampires and creatures that resist lethal damage from mundane weapons. I do agree that stating in plain words that Wrathful Sword either does or does not bypass resistances would clarify the issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> In other news, we have $71 dollars to go before we clear the $70k marker. The writing has yet to be set in stone, I presume, but I'm excited to hear about the 8 new Compacts we will be getting. I enjoy SWORN and while I'm not 100% sold on the Council of Bones, I acknowledge that they fulfill a missing niche in Hunter, which helps flesh it out as a fuller universe. I'm excited to know more about Nine Stars know that we know that the Compact was directly inspired by crime dramas and I'm in high hopes for the rest of the 2E Hunter manuscript.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T21:30:35-08:00","id":1368853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368852#post1368852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The 1E iteration of Wrathful Sword explicitly did aggravated damage, which in general nothing resists. That's probably why there's ambiguity now that wasn't there. Additionally, the Endowments in 2E are explicitly stated to be supernatural (&amp;quot;Hunters are not supernatural, but the Endowments they use are.&amp;quot; Under 'Using Endowments', Manuscript Preview #1 and Ascending Ones), so the 2E iteration of Wrathful Sword should affect Vampires and creatures that resist lethal damage from mundane weapons. I do agree that stating in plain words that Wrathful Sword either does or does not bypass resistances would clarify the issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> In other news, we have $71 dollars to go before we clear the $70k marker. The writing has yet to be set in stone, I presume, but I'm excited to hear about the 8 new Compacts we will be getting. I enjoy SWORN and while I'm not 100% sold on the Council of Bones, I acknowledge that they fulfill a missing niche in Hunter, which helps flesh it out as a fuller universe. I'm excited to know more about Nine Stars know that we know that the Compact was directly inspired by crime dramas and I'm in high hopes for the rest of the 2E Hunter manuscript.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its expanded write ups on the 7 we have, PLUS one new compact and conspiracy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T21:35:38-08:00","id":1368854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368853#post1368853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think its expanded write ups on the 7 we have, PLUS one new compact and conspiracy</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Huh. The Update #10 and the interpretations of others seems to make it out as it being more, specifically the quick mention of &quot;New Compacts, baby! So excited!&quot; I might be overhyping myself. But hey, more information and at least one more organization. :V","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T21:40:03-08:00","id":1368855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368854#post1368854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Huh. The Update #10 and the interpretations of others seems to make it out as it being more, specifically the quick mention of &amp;quot;New Compacts, baby! So excited!&amp;quot; I might be overhyping myself. But hey, more information and at least one more organization. :V</div> </div> </div> </div>welp, reading it again, I have no idea. I'm going to sleep on it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T23:32:26-08:00","id":1368862,"title":"","content":"70,000$! New Compacts, baby! :P<br /> <br /> And now to get the Third Tier expansion and the secret stretch goal and I could sleep well at night","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T04:03:17-08:00","id":1368883,"title":"","content":"Union and TF: V are out! Being the chump I am I have skipped the compact straight to the Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> I have not read much/ Any TF:V stuff from 1e but I like the feel of the write up here. The twisted self-eating conspiracy theories is a fun angle, the suspicions as to why they don\u2019t work outside the US and the scope of Antagonists is nice compared to some of the more focused conspiracy\u2019s.<br /> <br /> Their write up I like, but I have some issues with Advanced Armoury. To start positive, the general idea of monster hunting tech that, in contrast to the other conspiracies, is completely mundane is badass. I also really like the RFID feature as a reason the weapons cannot go walkabout easily and another layer of Military Industrial complex control. Plus, most of the items I think do a really cool effect. As endowments go, flavour is on point.<br /> <br /> My issue is the mechanics feel really, really, dissonant from the flavour. Mainly in 2 areas:<br /> <br /> Loadout: This mechanic feels like it has an Identity crisis? Some items like the Grenades or Serum give the user a direct number of uses (6 and 1 respectively) but still have the caveat that they cease working after X sessions \u2013 a purely out of game measure. What if I am running some really slow paced sessions running at near real time, and then RAW my goggles fail between sessions, or my grenades just \u201cstop\u201d even though only a day has passed in game, but in another session 2 months could pass and the goggles are working fine. I feel like loadout should be tied to an in game measure either uses (Grenades have 6 per loadout, ammo for Mjolnir) or an in game measure before the item needs to be checked in (3 weeks or the goggles are remotely deactivated for instance). I know this is super easy to homebrew, but I want that feedback in now if possible <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Further thought: having them tied to in game measures can be used for extra tension, either as your hunt goes poorly and your up against the clock, or the vampire you were trailing has skipped the border to Canada and you need to negotiate with your handler an extension to the loadout time to hunt it down. <br /> <br /> Using Advanced Armoury in a roll: This is mostly on the Equaliser Grenade and the Odin Reticule, It feels weird that AA is used in die rolls for this equipment when much was made of these weapons being Mundane in the write up for AA. Even if they are supposed to be supernatural and scale with AA \u2013 AA is just level of trust with TF:V, not an inherent trait. I suppose the Odin Reticule could be covered by \u201ctraining\u201d in how the AA rating helps, but the roll for the grenade is used as a effect of the grenade which feels \u2013 disconnected.<br /> <br /> I know that\u2019s a little negative \u2013 but this is probably my favourite write up so far except maybe Lucifuge! Just the above two bugged me as they are out of game mechanics effecting in game which I feel should be avoided whenever possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":24597,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","user":"LordofIron","date":".  Idea on loadout 02-19-2020, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T04:41:55-08:00","id":1368892,"title":"","content":"Electricity typically does bashing damage. Does the Mjolnir Cannon do bashing damage because it is a giant taser? Or does it do lethal damage because it is a weapon? Or does the low-powered version do bashing and the high-powered version do lethal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T05:37:48-08:00","id":1368897,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24597_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24597\" data-vbnamecard=\"24597\">LordofIron</a> The way I look at it, most stories run with investigation first, to figure out what kind of monster you're dealing with, then the hunt, then the confrontation. So, you're probably going to choose things like the Etheric Goggles first, which have a long loadout time, and then when you know what you're dealing with, you go check-in with your field office and load up for bear with those one session loadout weapons. This lets the ST build up some tension first since they can throw a monster at you for which you do not have proper equipment putting you on your back foot, but when you're ready to go after it, you stand a chance against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T05:52:04-08:00","id":1368899,"title":"","content":"Reading through new previews, I focused on Union. A bit weird is that proper Compact was created at year 1999, in Internet age, mentioning that 'work parties' ( i.e. hunter cells ) were created for whole 20th century. Even in <i>Supernatural </i>TV show, it was pointed that Roadhouse Compact started in 70s-80s and survived to modern times by using simple telephone lines and common meeting grounds. Why Union as organisation could not start in at least mid 30s-40s is really beyond my imagination. It's not like Labour Movement representatives did not meet at the start of 20th century, right?<br /> <br /> In my own games, I would probably set the start of Union in late 1940s, just after World War 2, where USA industry started to kick in en masse - and 'American Dream' truly begun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-19-2020, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T06:23:40-08:00","id":1368905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368821#post1368821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand the (as written) benefit to this is taking a small (Damage 0) weapon and making it a Damage 5 Pen-knife of Doom, which is how I see the point of the ability as its currently written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to turn a kitchen knife or baseball bat into a deadly weapon, even against the undead, seems pretty useful to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T06:34:20-08:00","id":1368909,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8719\" data-vbnamecard=\"8719\">Florin</a> I understand where you are coming from but personally don\u2019t see how tying the metric to sessions though helps this in a way that a more measurable in game time factor wouldn\u2019t. For example my group has quite short sessions, normally 2-3 hours long. An investigation arc could more than 3 sessions, especially if we are layering in downtime, sub plots and personal stories with touchstones \u2013 we could easily make 1 in game week stretch for months\u2019 worth of play, and I know I can, I\u2019ve done it! (Had a 1 year irl long vampire game that took place over 2 in game weeks!) So in those situations in game players may need to check in to their handler with the goggles every day in game? This just feels unintuitive.<br /> <br /> Now, the text does also say: \u201cInstead of purchasing each Endowment separately, the hunter simply picks a number of Endowments at the beginning of each session based on her Advanced Armory rating, and that is what she has.\u201d Which kind of reads that you can just refresh your gear every single session at the start? So why have loadout at all be session based at all? Or, why not add a time limit in game or a usage count to add that extra tension.<br /> Lastly is that the rule makes these\u2026 assumptions, it assumes that final confrontations will be over in a session which RAW restricts the ability to use cliff-hangers or \u201cYes, but\u2026. Find out next time\u201d and the like. It also assumes that sessions always start at a point of downtime where people are able to make such decisions and characters can \u201cPop off to grab a Mjolnir\u201d when I find most games more run as a continuous narrative, not a collection of isolated scenes. (And it should be noted, Session limits hurt a continuous narrative, but setting in game limits works fine for both play styles.)<br /> <br /> Once again, I know this is all super easy to homebrew and house rule for individual tables. It just reads as being so dissonant from how these games can be played and reads like \u201cPlay games X way or the mechanics won\u2019t work\u201d.<br /> <br /> Ill proably stop harping on about this now - TF:V is a very cool write up and this just bugs me becasue it seems so easy to tweak to make this 10/10.<br /> <br /> Ill save this feedback for the official feedback channels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T06:46:06-08:00","id":1368915,"title":"","content":"I don't expect to convince you, but I can see the reasoning behind doing the timing the way they did. CoD has always used &quot;dramatic&quot; time. A scene is as long as it needs to be, a chapter is a collection of scenes played in one session, etc. It make sense for them to continue that instead of trying to say a loadout lasts for 1 day or 3 days or whatever. I think of it this way: if you only play one day in a session, you're probably doing a lot of stuff and therefore wearing out your equipment quicker than if you did the same number of scenes over the course of three days. So, more wear and tear quicker. Still the same number of sessions, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T07:05:08-08:00","id":1368920,"title":"","content":"Supervisors are fickle creatures, you never know if it\u2019s going to be two days or two months until the next time they suddenly hit the remote killswitch on your gear and demand a progress report before they\u2019ll turn it back on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T07:09:33-08:00","id":1368921,"title":"","content":"Weirdly I would be fine if the limit was say &quot;1 Story&quot; or &quot;1 scene of use&quot; as those are flexible and can fit into how a ST runs things. I just find &quot;session&quot; arbitrary and restrictive. <br /> <br /> I get where you are coming from, just different styles for different groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T09:27:12-08:00","id":1368951,"title":"","content":"Hiya, everyone! I mentioned this on the Kickstarter page but wanted to repeat it here. The reason why we're not announcing specifics for tier two support (and, by extension, other Tending the Flame chapters) is because a lot depends upon how the rest of the book shapes up. Once we're clear on what chapters were funded via stretch goals, the outline will be further plotted to ensure we're giving you the best value within that space. Yes, there is a plan and I would LOVE for the entirety of Tending the Flame to be funded. I also want to have the freedom to make adjustments so you are happy with the book. Keep your fingers crossed! And, as always, appreciate the enthusiasm and conversations you're having. Yay, hunters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T09:43:14-08:00","id":1368953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368951#post1368951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hiya, everyone! I mentioned this on the Kickstarter page but wanted to repeat it here. The reason why we're not announcing specifics for tier two support (and, by extension, other Tending the Flame chapters) is because a lot depends upon how the rest of the book shapes up. Once we're clear on what chapters were funded via stretch goals, the outline will be further plotted to ensure we're giving you the best value within that space. Yes, there is a plan and I would LOVE for the entirety of Tending the Flame to be funded. I also want to have the freedom to make adjustments so you are happy with the book. Keep your fingers crossed! And, as always, appreciate the enthusiasm and conversations you're having. Yay, hunters!</div> </div> </div> </div>companions are usually 4 chapters correct? I do wonder what that 4th chapter could be","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T09:47:49-08:00","id":1368955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1368953#post1368953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> companions are usually 4 chapters correct? I do wonder what that 4th chapter could be</div> </div> </div> </div> Four doesn't give us the space for a game about hunting monsters. There are a LOT more chapters planned for Tending the Flame--three of which I'm dying to reveal right now because they're SO cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"