<strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369022#post1369022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me or are the stats for the Mjolnir Cannon kind of anemic compared to the description?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mechanically, the Mjolnir Cannon is comparable to a rifle in terms of damage with the added bonus of forcing the target to be Knocked Down. Strangely, the range doesn't seem to change between its two settings. Notably, a change-up from 1E to 2E is that Endowments are no longer limited by your dots in the Endowment, meaning that, in theory, a low-rank member of VALKYRIE may gain access to a previously 4-5 dot weapon which necessitates the slight downgrade. It's now less of a BFG railgun fantasy and more of an experimental weapon that does what it needs to without drawing too much attention. Additionally, the 1E iteration of the Mjolnir Cannon dealt either bashing, more bashing, or lethal depending on which mode it was set to. The 2E iteration is either lethal or more lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T05:40:38-08:00","id":1369337,"title":"","content":"Its a shame what happened to VASCU -- going from cops that were unusually principled by conspiracy standards to just another private mercenary organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T05:44:42-08:00","id":1369342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369337#post1369337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a shame what happened to VASCU -- going from cops that were unusually principled by conspiracy standards to just another private mercenary organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>You meant a private investigation office, and they are still bound by the local laws of the countries they operate in.<br /> <br /> Sure, it is a different experience, but it is still not a mercenary group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T06:31:50-08:00","id":1369353,"title":"","content":"And opens up more story locations and options. I don't see how this is a loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T07:35:31-08:00","id":1369366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369337#post1369337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a shame what happened to VASCU -- going from cops that were unusually principled by conspiracy standards to just another private mercenary organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure being a private consulting firm makes them inherently less ethical than federal law enforcement, given all the baggage there too.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m surprised by the change given the main source material for VASCU agents are overwhelmingly FBI profilers, but there\u2019s a Sherlock Holmes Consulting Detective angle to play up now I suppose.<br /> <br /> Speaking of source material, Postcognition should really put the agent in the eyes of the killer, not the victim. Beside genre emulation, it also avoids the issue of them solving the case too easily by just seeing the killer\u2019s face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T07:44:45-08:00","id":1369369,"title":"","content":"so, what's some good movies and games to watch to see how to play a hong kong police force and ge t a proper feel for them?<br /> <br /> the only game i have (and still am playing) is Sleeping Dogs. that's all i have for inspiration<br /> <br /> EDIT: also, like what would separate how the kong kong police operates to the NYPD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-21-2020, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T08:45:23-08:00","id":1369383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369353#post1369353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And opens up more story locations and options. I don't see how this is a loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO there\u2019s a certain coolness factor to \u201cpsychic FBI\u201d that \u201cpsychic PI agency\u201d doesn\u2019t nearly match, but that\u2019s it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T08:56:46-08:00","id":1369387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369366#post1369366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> but there\u2019s a Sherlock Holmes Consulting Detective angle to play up now I suppose.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really a thing IRL with respect to actual police investigations. VASCU are now just high-end private investigators, without the hook, baggage, authority and duty of being an actual law enforcement officer.<br /> <br /> I believe the change was to make VASCU more open to non-American characters, but I think they really lost a lot of what was great about them in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T09:00:16-08:00","id":1369390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369383#post1369383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IMO there\u2019s a certain coolness factor to \u201cpsychic FBI\u201d that \u201cpsychic PI agency\u201d doesn\u2019t nearly match, but that\u2019s it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, you can still play the &quot;psychic FBI&quot; agent with VASCU's 2e version- the writeup outright states that VASCU still has a few members in the FBI, the Status 3 benefit includes the FBI, and the US government (as well as the FBI) are said to be some of VASCU's more prominent clients. You could play an hunter who work with the FBI as a freelancer, and you could play as an agent or a contact. Going private opens more concepts, but still allows the original one, if I understand correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T09:07:22-08:00","id":1369391,"title":"","content":"The CIA actually already has guidelines on employing psychics for aiding law enforcement. <a href=\"https://www.cia.gov/library/readingroom/docs/CIA-RDP96-00788R000100280009-3.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.cia.gov/library/readingr...00280009-3.pdf</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T11:46:37-08:00","id":1369415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369390#post1369390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, you can still play the &quot;psychic FBI&quot; agent with VASCU's 2e version- the writeup outright states that VASCU still has a few members in the FBI, the Status 3 benefit includes the FBI, and the US government (as well as the FBI) are said to be some of VASCU's more prominent clients. You could play an hunter who work with the FBI as a freelancer, and you could play as an agent or a contact. Going private opens more concepts, but still allows the original one, if I understand correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> VASCU agents are not FBI, and FBI agents really can't moonlight with an international detective agency.<br /> <br /> The VASCU Status 3 bonus is supposed to represent good relationships, respect and contacts with a specific government agency, and should be reflected as dots in Allies or Contacts, not Status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T12:10:45-08:00","id":1369420,"title":"","content":"Page 6 paragraph 4 of the preview says that there are a few VASCU agents still in the FBI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T12:40:38-08:00","id":1369425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369420#post1369420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 6 paragraph 4 of the preview says that there are a few VASCU agents still in the FBI.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using a bioengineering research group called the Vanguard Initiative as a front, VASCU remains<br /> headquartered in Philadelphia, and continues to work with US government interests as a<br /> contractor \u2014 including, upon occasion, with the few VASCU agents who remained in the FBI.<br /> However, as word of the institute\u2019s talents worm their way through the dark underside of<br /> international law enforcement, VASCU increasingly sees profitable opportunities overseas. </div> </div> </div>No, some old VASCU agents stayed with the FBI or other government agencies and didn't move Vanguard Institute in Philadelphia, and old and new VASCU agents still cross paths on occasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T13:18:09-08:00","id":1369431,"title":"","content":"Rereading it, I can see it that way now. Really, though I am not especially tied to VASCU being a FBI group or anything, the section doesn't read super interestingly to me overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T13:20:10-08:00","id":1369432,"title":"","content":"Idea - instead of Vanguard Initiative being private investigators, they\u2019re a \u201cprofiling training institute\u201d that takes law enforcement trainees from all over the world. So you end up with VASCU \u201cprofilers\u201d In law enforcement agencies around the world, with the Vanguard Initiative providing the information sharing network between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T13:55:32-08:00","id":1369438,"title":"","content":"I wont be surprised if VASCU gets some minor re-write. it being more tied to law enforcement definitely brought them in to people (oh, and the extensive write-up). part of me wonders if they did this due to the 9 stars police force. still, they still seem as bound to the law as they were in Slasher, it's just the word count cant go into that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T13:57:53-08:00","id":1369439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369369#post1369369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so, what's some good movies and games to watch to see how to play a hong kong police force and ge t a proper feel for them?<br /> <br /> the only game i have (and still am playing) is Sleeping Dogs. that's all i have for inspiration<br /> <br /> EDIT: also, like what would separate how the kong kong police operates to the NYPD</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard Boiled is a good movie. most of John Woo's early films and stuff that deal with the police and the triads are great inspiration for Nine Stars. Also Internal Affairs?(the movie the Departed was based off of.) Young and Dangerous(about the triads) all really good fodder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T14:00:23-08:00","id":1369440,"title":"","content":"I like them being tied to the FBI because I think a hunter group that has to follow the law for both good(gives you something to hold onto when the vigil gets rough) and bad(that monster will get away if you don't do something about him but the law can't touch them) is a good hook to based a lot of stories off of. That being said I don't mind their change a whole lot because it does open stuff to new places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T14:04:57-08:00","id":1369443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369439#post1369439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hard Boiled is a good movie. most of John Woo's early films and stuff that deal with the police and the triads are great inspiration for Nine Stars. Also Internal Affairs?(the movie the Departed was based off of.) Young and Dangerous(about the triads) all really good fodder.</div> </div> </div> </div>thank you! considering they are based on pop culture depictions, I want to mix those with real life traits in order to differentiate them from other famed police departments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T14:32:37-08:00","id":1369449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369439#post1369439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hard Boiled is a good movie. most of John Woo's early films and stuff that deal with the police and the triads are great inspiration for Nine Stars. Also Internal Affairs?(the movie the Departed was based off of.) Young and Dangerous(about the triads) all really good fodder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Infernal Affairs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T15:26:07-08:00","id":1369458,"title":"","content":"The VASCU writeup refers to both a Vanguard Institute and a Vanguard Initiative and I don't know if they are two separate things or a mistake but it's kind of confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T16:11:41-08:00","id":1369467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I like them being tied to the FBI because I think a hunter group that has to follow the law for both good(gives you something to hold onto when the vigil gets rough) and bad(that monster will get away if you don't do something about him but the law can't touch them) is a good hook to based a lot of stories off of. That being said I don't mind their change a whole lot because it does open stuff to new places.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">VASCU is still bound to the law of the country they are operating in. While they are no longer a secret-but-officially-sanctioned investigative bureau, VASCU does not have the level of carte-blanche that they did before their re-restructuring and &quot;</span>their actions are restricted by the laws and regulations of the countries in which they operate.&quot; Additionally, their main headquarters is located in the USA and they are implicitly still under scrutiny by and answer to the FBI considering that some agents allege that they are only still operating because there is a search out for Dr. Wintergreen.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The VASCU writeup refers to both a Vanguard Institute and a Vanguard Initiative and I don't know if they are two separate things or a mistake but it's kind of confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the public face of VASCU is a &quot;bioengineering research group&quot; called the Vanguard Initiative while the actual core to VASCU is known as the Vanguard Institute. The Initiative is mentioned three times in the write-up and is referred to as a &quot;front&quot; while the Institute is mentioned several times and seems to refer to the hunter organization that is VASCU. I do agree that it is confusing, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So with the final organizations previewed (barring the Ashwood Abbey and Aegis Kai Doru create-your-own-organization examples), I can confirm some of my own suspicions and predictions about the Compacts and Conspiracies. Close to all of the 1E organizations are dealing with some sort of upheaval or crisis of their own that is threatening the stability of their organization (with the only groups that have little to no internal uproar being the Union and, surprisingly to me, the Long Night. In contrast, SWORN, Nine Stars, and the Council of Bones seem rather stable in comparison (which I'd attribute to word count). The Endowments are what really caught my attention as there is no longer a power hierarchy or division in certain Endowments like Elixirs, Advanced Armory, Teleinformatics, etc. The number of powers are also rather scant, sitting in the range of 7-9 powers per Endowment whereas 1E averaged somewhere of 9-12 for each organization barring additions from other sourcebooks. I do hope that the final adds a few more powers to help offer more diversity for these organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1417,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","user":"Reaper Verse","date":".  Formatting 02-21-2020, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T17:33:11-08:00","id":1369476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369467#post1369467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">VASCU is still bound to the law of the country they are operating in. While they are no longer a secret-but-officially-sanctioned investigative bureau, VASCU does not have the level of carte-blanche that they did before their re-restructuring and &quot;</span>their actions are restricted by the laws and regulations of the countries in which they operate.&quot; Additionally, their main headquarters is located in the USA and they are implicitly still under scrutiny by and answer to the FBI considering that some agents allege that they are only still operating because there is a search out for Dr. Wintergreen.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>However...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, when it comes to dealing with monsters, the rules don\u2019t apply. New VASCU recruits are even taking their cues from other agencies such as Task Force: VALKYRIE or the Cheiron Group. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T18:09:47-08:00","id":1369478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369476#post1369476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However...<br /> <br /> [<i>Of course, when it comes to dealing with monsters, the rules don\u2019t apply. New VASCU recruits are even taking their cues from other agencies such as Task Force: VALKYRIE or the Cheiron Group.]</i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was a part of VASCU's 1E iteration as well, only expanded upon. VASCU is almost entirely involved in examining the Slashers as supernaturally-enhanced serial killers, who would need to be process and tried as any serial killer would in normal circumstances. VASCU agents that pursue the explicitly supernatural non-humans do it without official VASCU sanction and cannot be use their association with VASCU for it. Implicitly, rogue VASCU agents hunting down the supernatural tend to do so violently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other cases concern killers who appear to be creatures from folklore. Some agents think it\u2019s their job to bring such beasts to trial, but when a killer grows into a nine-foot tall monster (...), arraignment might be the last thing on most agents\u2019 minds. If a monster can\u2019t pass for human, (...) it\u2019s up to the chain of command to decide whether to destroy the creature or lock it in Lansing.<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> An agent who wants to turn \u201cmonster hunter\u201d has to do it in her own time, and be very careful that her extracurricular activities don\u2019t dump the unit in a whole bunch of trouble. (...) Vanguard has common psychological profiles for the most populous supernatural creatures, but that\u2019s it. Because their cases often end with the death of the monster, Vanguard agents believe that each is unique.<br /> </div> </div> </div>It reads as if the &quot;rules don't apply&quot; line is more of a Hunter mindset rather than an organizational mindset, especially as the line comes after bemoaning the fact that VASCU needs to follow legal channels for their cases with non-monsters. An agent can go ahead and chase down a vampire bleeding victims dry in a backalley but it would be close to impossible to guarantee that the vampire would be able to be brought to legal justice via the system. VASCU won't reprimand a specific agent should that agent take justice into their own hands against something that isn't human but they are not going to officially support their actions. There are some instances of VASCU managing to contain a non-human supernatural (specifically the one vampire in Lansang which is, in and of itself, noted as an exception) but VASCU aims more towards instances of spree or serial murders, which is why their attention is more on Slashers and mundane serial killers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T03:16:24-08:00","id":1369543,"title":"","content":"So, which group or groups are attacking nuVASCU?, Vampires, mages, other Hunters, the US government,etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T08:30:34-08:00","id":1369587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369543#post1369543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, which group or groups are attacking nuVASCU?, Vampires, mages, other Hunters, the US government,etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think VASCU is really under attack by anything. I can only really think of the Hunt Club","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T11:52:32-08:00","id":1369612,"title":"","content":"Did Heritage House and the Ahl al-Jabal make it to the list of Compacts? Wondering if some of the more obscure ones got lost in the shuffle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T12:02:05-08:00","id":1369618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369612#post1369612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Heritage House and the Ahl al-Jabal make it to the list of Compacts? Wondering if some of the more obscure ones got lost in the shuffle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahl al-Jabal gets a historic mention. I don\u2019t think Heritage House does, but they don\u2019t really have any defining traits I can recall to make them worth using word count on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T12:03:52-08:00","id":1369619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369618#post1369618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahl al-Jabal gets a historic mention. I don\u2019t think Heritage House does, but they don\u2019t really have any defining traits I can recall to make them worth using word count on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aww, I liked 'em. There's a classic New England ghost story vibe to them I liked quite a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T13:28:41-08:00","id":1369633,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>, I'm just wondering, you liking the game so far?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T23:16:16-08:00","id":1369769,"title":"","content":"With the newest Kickstarter update expanding on Bygones, I wonder how different Aegis Kai Doru's Relics Endowment will be. AKD has already been confirmed as the Build-Your-Own example for Conspiracies, so I assume their Endowment will be deconstructed for Build-Your-Own Endowments. Their 1E iteration seems to run the gamut due to the power ranking but it seems like their iconic Relics float around the semi-to-truly permanent Bygones.<br /> <br /> Actually, now I'm kinda sad that Aegis Kai Doru isn't an official splat. I kinda want to see how they would hypothetically develop through the transition into 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T23:58:40-08:00","id":1369779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369633#post1369633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>, I'm just wondering, you liking the game so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>-Ish?<br /> <br /> The thing of the matter is that it hits a lot of the major notes that I wanted it to hit-Hunter has not changed it's fundamental nature-but there's a lot of details that are not quite there.<br /> <br /> The two big details I can name that hit my (personal) dissonance with it are the much more definitive nature of the Lucifuge's origins and VASCU's move over into private investigator against them as FBI, and these are equal and opposite directions-the former moving away from the murkier, mixed, complicated, and ultimately unanswerable metaphysics that is one of the things I love most about Chronicles (And Also Beast, because that game starts off Definite and Ends Strange, but that's a side tangent), and the latter for moving away from the real world deep criticism that was cleverly and subversively baked into the presentation of material. Hunter Second, on both counts, does move away from the elements of monstrosity that I feel make it fascinating, and I do personally feel like this version is actually legitimately weaker against it's predecessor for both it's weirdness and potential in terms of the supernatural, and it's critical examination of human nature in groups in a way that is better understood than simply saying &quot;herd mentality&quot;.<br /> <br /> I list those two as my Major Points, but it honestly is just emblematic of concerns that I'm seeing baked across the text, a distancing from that willingness to be murky and messy, and at the same time a distancing from a willingness to be really sharply critical. It rounds it's edges, so to speak.<br /> <br /> Now this all amounts to <i>basically</i> a personal bitching. Hunter Second, so far, is still really good, delivering a lot of what is to like about Hunter on the whole. It is solid and cohesive, it is willing to promote itself while still solidly alluding to the flaws of the splat in the same way any of the Second Editions have been, and in particular while it has not gotten as critical as, say, C&amp;C could get at times, or even the original core, it still is very good at looking at human nature on various levels and balancing human awfulness with human heroism and the fact that <i>that's</i> a complicated balance.<br /> <br /> There's also a part of me that is both grateful and bummed out that it's basically not #iHunt, because on the one hand I want it to be more like #iHunt, but on the other hand, if it was, then I wouldn't have #iHunt.<br /> <br /> So, I mean, so far? Yeah, it's solid, and I'm very 'kay with it.<br /> <br /> But I'm not going to deny it's also <i>not quite</i> the Hunter I fell in love with.<br /> <br /> Best thing about me though, and this Hunter, is that is a <i>very workable problem</i>. We can disagree, but baby we can work things out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T09:41:40-08:00","id":1369850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369449#post1369449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Infernal Affairs</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you I knew it was something along those lines. been awhile since I had seen it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T10:55:18-08:00","id":1369867,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> got it. ok, I'll be honest, the only reason I was wondering, was because I'd be very sad if you didnt like it, because that would likely mean you would have no essays or discussions about thematic aspects of the game once it comes out (and I do enjoy reading those very much)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T11:09:28-08:00","id":1369873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369867#post1369867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> got it. ok, I'll be honest, the only reason I was wondering, was because I'd be very sad if you didnt like it, because that would likely mean you would have no essays or discussions about thematic aspects of the game once it comes out (and I do enjoy reading those very much)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage the Awakening is my second least favorite Chronicles game. (Which should not be understood as me not liking it, I just like everything else a lot more)<br /> <br /> It has, like, three major essays and a lot of big posts having me talk metaphysics, morals, ethics, and philosophy.<br /> <br /> I go where the fight is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T11:23:45-08:00","id":1369879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1369873#post1369873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage the Awakening is my second least favorite Chronicles game. (Which should not be understood as me not liking it, I just like everything else a lot more)<br /> <br /> It has, like, three major essays and a lot of big posts having me talk metaphysics, morals, ethics, and philosophy.<br /> <br /> I go where the fight is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>oh, so I have nothing to worry about. well then, I feel a lot better, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T04:18:10-08:00","id":1370027,"title":"","content":"&quot;If a hunter believes that a kind zombie who chooses not to eat brains is not a monster, that\u2019s fine&quot;<br /> &quot;From an out-of-character perspective, Code breaking points consider any creature that wields Dread Powers or Numina a monster \u2014 as long as the hunters know it is such a creature&quot;<br /> &quot;Actively and willingly helping a monster -3&quot;<br /> <br /> So, can the hunter designate the non brain eating zombie as a non monster or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T05:12:50-08:00","id":1370036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370027#post1370027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;If a hunter believes that a kind zombie who chooses not to eat brains is not a monster, that\u2019s fine&quot;<br /> &quot;From an out-of-character perspective, Code breaking points consider any creature that wields Dread Powers or Numina a monster \u2014 as long as the hunters know it is such a creature&quot;<br /> &quot;Actively and willingly helping a monster -3&quot;<br /> <br /> So, can the hunter designate the non brain eating zombie as a non monster or not?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It reads like a Hunter can justify whether a given creature is a monster (supernatural, non-human/mortal, and possible threat to normal humanity) or not and it reflects on their Breaking Point. A section below mentions a Hunter that sees a member of the Lucifuge performing a Castigation and presuming that the Lucifuge member is a monster if they had no knowledge beforehand of what the Lucifuge is or does and says that it is effectively up to the Hunter to make a judgment call on whether that Lucifuge member is a monster or not.<br /> <br /> I think the whole &quot;monster&quot; thing, outside of the meta definition of &quot;Dread Power/Numina-using creature&quot;, is a semantics thing. A Hunter can deem a zombie to be a non-monster for a number of reasons ranging from trust in the zombie's actions to underestimating the dangers of it and that would be entirely fine and dandy. Once that zombie crosses the fine-line, chows down on an unsuspecting person, and demonstrates that, no, they actually ARE a monster, is when the definition of monster starts coming into play and the Hunter has to figure out how they would respond. Likewise, with the Lucifuge member, the Hunter in question may just straight-up murder what they consider a demon-summoning monster and they would be entirely in their right in accordance to the Code; after all, the Hunter didn't kill a person, they killed a monster. However, if they were to discover that the Lucifuge member was, for all intents and purposes, a fellow Hunter who simply used their power to uphold the Vigil, the Hunter might need to reflect on their actions if they consider the Lucifuge to be a person. And that's not including whether or not the Hunter believes that &quot;I had no idea&quot; is enough of an excuse.<br /> <br /> So I would say that the answer would be: the zombie is still identifiably a monster but a Hunter is allowed to consider them to be a non-monster. However, in the context of pertinent moral quandaries, the Hunter would need to understand that there is a distinct different between a human person and a zombie and that they may have prioritized the zombie's needs over a fellow person's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T05:40:52-08:00","id":1370040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370027#post1370027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;If a hunter believes that a kind zombie who chooses not to eat brains is not a monster, that\u2019s fine&quot;<br /> &quot;From an out-of-character perspective, Code breaking points consider any creature that wields Dread Powers or Numina a monster \u2014 as long as the hunters know it is such a creature&quot;<br /> &quot;Actively and willingly helping a monster -3&quot;<br /> <br /> So, can the hunter designate the non brain eating zombie as a non monster or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding of the subject is that in order for a being to be considered as a &quot;monster&quot;, it has to answer the following criteria- <br /> <br /> a) they must have access to supernatural powers (generally, Dread Powers or Numina, but at certain cases Supernatural Merits and Endowments could also qualify)<br /> <br /> b) they must use those powers outside of the service of the Vigil (so you can't use them for personal gain or harm other people)<br /> <br /> c) they must hurt people (that is, anyone who is not a monster)<br /> <br /> And all of that under the assumption that the hunter must <i>believe </i>them to answer those criteria.<br /> <br /> So an hunter witnessing a member of a conspiracy using supernatural powers and believing them to be outside of the use of the Vigil, or not understanding that they are used in the context of the Vigil, would identify those hunters as &quot;monsters&quot;. People who are not slashers and yet kill others are terrible people, but they are still people and not monsters. A monster which hides its true nature, or disguise/use its abilities in the service of the Vigil and nothing beside it, could be registered as a &quot;person&quot;. A regular mortal who the hunter believes to be a monster, either because of a mistake in identity, failed research or them being used as a scapegoat by a monster, could be registered as a &quot;monster&quot;. The Code is not an Unseen Senses merit- it relays on the perception of the hunter and how they understand the situation. What is the difference between a psychic who reads fortunes and a VASCU agents which use them to track down murderers beside their commitment for the Vigil? The definition for a monster is objective- but in the sense of how the hunter understands the situation. That's my reading of the text, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T08:05:36-08:00","id":1370054,"title":"","content":"The intent of the rules as would regard a non-brain eating zombie would basically be under the area of the zombie not being an issue for Integrity breaking points until you're in a situation where it's the humans or the zombie, and you choose the zombie.<br /> <br /> Pretty much everything else is just &quot;Welp, they're not doing anything, so&quot;<br /> <br /> A hunter can personally decide something is not a monster, particular if it's not acting like one, but for the purposes of Hunter if it falls under the criteria of Dread Powers and/or Numina and is known to be what you would conventionally call a monster, they're a monster in a such a way that the Hunter always knows (in their own terms) that it would be a monster and therefore subject to the Code.<br /> <br /> Like, they can use whatever words or avoid labelling how they will, but there's always gonna be that tickle, barely concious or subconcious, that their not-brain-eating friend is also being held in a different category from his beer hall buddies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T08:47:59-08:00","id":1370064,"title":"","content":"I'm also reading that penalty and breaking point as &quot;helping monster over a human&quot; - which is to say actively feeding people to Steve McZombie. Which is a major betrayal of the Code.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T10:34:45-08:00","id":1370091,"title":"","content":"So should I assume that a crossover chronicle is going to almost necessarily entail a -3 to the hunter's breaking points forever or no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T10:39:01-08:00","id":1370093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370091#post1370091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So should I assume that a crossover chronicle is going to almost necessarily entail a -3 to the hunter's breaking points forever or no?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you start a Crossover Chronicle you wouldn't have already sacrificed Breaking Points for Code, so not until you decided to screw your crossover pals over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T10:43:36-08:00","id":1370094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370091#post1370091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So should I assume that a crossover chronicle is going to almost necessarily entail a -3 to the hunter's breaking points forever or no?</div> </div> </div> </div>The table for breaking point modifiers is for your <i>roll.</i> You roll dice to see if your hunter suffers a loss of Integrity and it is not a guarantee. The fiction is going to vary widely depending upon your hunter's view of the Code and who/what they encounter and when--even in a crossover chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T10:49:37-08:00","id":1370096,"title":"","content":"Hey folks, there are additional rules present in The Slasher Chronicle presented as an alternative to fit the sample setting. Slashers are the primary monster type and hunters are at risk of being turned into them. You're encouraged to take a close look at those rules, especially since there's some edge cases or clarity we may not have anticipated especially because 2E hunters are more capable than their 1E counterparts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1870,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","user":"mlvalentine","date":". 02-24-2020, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T10:55:39-08:00","id":1370097,"title":"","content":"So I have a quick question about Long-Term Modifications for equipment. It mentions availability and what sort of equipment penalty it is to alter an item. But some items have variable equipment penalty, do you raise the cost of the item for each -1 you take or is the cost flat?<br /> For example would you raise the cost of giving a weapon +3, 6 higher availability. Or is it only 2 higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T11:02:00-08:00","id":1370099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370091#post1370091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So should I assume that a crossover chronicle is going to almost necessarily entail a -3 to the hunter's breaking points forever or no?</div> </div> </div> </div>The book says breaking point modifiers are at the ST's discretion. As an ST, I'd feel like a bit of a heel if I applied that -3 to all of your breaking point checks in a crossover game I am running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T11:07:27-08:00","id":1370101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370093#post1370093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you start a Crossover Chronicle you wouldn't have already sacrificed Breaking Points for Code, so not until you decided to screw your crossover pals over.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and as noted, the protagonists of other gamelines aren't generally the targets. One could say that a hunter who's Sworn thinks of their faction as being &quot;the good ones&quot; and is able to ignore them being technically monsters if everyone is facing the real adversary, the Contagion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T12:05:50-08:00","id":1370112,"title":"","content":"I certainly appreciate the changes to Tactics, which should be a far more robust tool now. But I was really hoping for more universal hunter mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T15:31:48-08:00","id":1370162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370101#post1370101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That, and as noted, the protagonists of other gamelines aren't generally the targets. One could say that a hunter who's Sworn thinks of their faction as being &quot;the good ones&quot; and is able to ignore them being technically monsters if everyone is facing the real adversary, the Contagion.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in a Crossover/Contagion game, it's reasonable the monster being their monstrous selves is something is not going to be something the Hunter is openly subject to at all times. The Hunter in a Crossover Game is neccesarily going to act as the angel on the shoulder that is also the canary to wound for everyone else, which is really something that should only be a matter of concern in dramatic moments.<br /> <br /> A Hunter can function in a crossover game, and even avoid the Really Bad Integrity Hits (by their lonesome) so long as everyone minds their p's and q's and plays to a heroic standard-but their role in such a game is to be an additional stressor on the (human vs monster) vs (self vs service) structures of such a game, with themselves as stake. The fun is also part of the risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T15:32:21-08:00","id":1370163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370112#post1370112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly appreciate the changes to Tactics, which should be a far more robust tool now. But I was really hoping for more universal hunter mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T18:11:16-08:00","id":1370200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370091#post1370091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So should I assume that a crossover chronicle is going to almost necessarily entail a -3 to the hunter's breaking points forever or no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely not. The penalty comes from choosing to aid a 'monster' over a 'person'. Setting aside the fact that the text makes it clear those are variable terms, there will be times in a crossover game where siding with 'monsters' does not come at the expense of 'people'. Helping a vampire fight off a strix wouldn't trigger it, as an example. Nor would helping a pack of werewolves fight off a plague of hosts. Heck, taking sides in a changeling gang war might be ok, as long as the hunter's 'allies' don't get caught harming people.<br /> <br /> The Code might compel the hunter to deal with them after the fact, but 'good zombie' analogy still applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T19:24:56-08:00","id":1370210,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... would it be a problem then to take the side of a non-predatory supernatural against a \u201ckill them all and ask questions later!\u201d Hunter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T19:47:37-08:00","id":1370214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370210#post1370210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... would it be a problem then to take the side of a non-predatory supernatural against a \u201ckill them all and ask questions later!\u201d Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like it would depend on you, your compact or conspiracy (if any), and your definition of a problem. And also the level of 'take the side of.' If you aren't harming them, letting them come to harm, refusing them in a time of need, torturing or betraying them, then it wouldn't have any impact at all. But if the murderous hunter was going to go kill a bunch of vampire babies and called you for help because he got ambushed by teenage Frankensteins and you refused to help then you could have a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> Though the same thing stands since the first part of second edition, where facing a Breaking Point usually doesn't mean game over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T21:48:08-08:00","id":1370231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370210#post1370210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... would it be a problem then to take the side of a non-predatory supernatural against a \u201ckill them all and ask questions later!\u201d Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you see still see them as a hunter? Or as a slasher targeting supernaturals?<br /> If you think of them as a monster, it should be fine. And honestly, that question is one of the major themes of the game. The answer should always vary and making the roll should be something people are worried about. Are they monsters, or people? Am I hero or a psychopath? It is all in the eye of the beholder.<br /> <br /> An unfortunate consequence of this is that it implies if you truly believe the hateful rhetoric of racists, seeing another subsect of people as 'subhuman, parasites or an infestation' might let you hunt them. Personally I'd say that is slasher territory, and will wait til we get the slasher chronicle chapter for judgement, but right now I consider the issue of what constitutes person vs monster to be rather subjective. Yet another reason not to have those kinds of groups among hunters; the Vigil cannot hold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T23:13:55-08:00","id":1370255,"title":"","content":"So\u2026 Integrity and the Code. Mechanically, I'm getting the feeling that a Hunter's Integrity has more in common with a Mage's Wisdom than with a corebook mortal's Integrity. You have none of the \u201cfive questions\u201d thing that the corebook uses to establish Breaking Points (or if you do, I've missed them); you have a ladder of Breaking Points set up in such a way that the lower your Integrity, the fewer of them you have to work about. And so on. <br /> <br /> Also, I find it interesting that nearly all of the Innate Breaking Points are \u201cFirst Time X happens\u201d. Only torturing a person or suffering a significant loss due to the supernatural or the Vigil aren't \u201cfirst time\u201d Breaking Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T03:34:49-08:00","id":1370290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370162#post1370162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in a Crossover/Contagion game, it's reasonable the monster being their monstrous selves is something is not going to be something the Hunter is openly subject to at all times. The Hunter in a Crossover Game is neccesarily going to act as the angel on the shoulder that is also the canary to wound for everyone else, which is really something that should only be a matter of concern in dramatic moments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which leads the rather hilarious image of a member of a literal killer cult suddenly realizing she's the conscience of the rest.<br /> <br /> And then screaming into the void for a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T03:58:46-08:00","id":1370293,"title":"","content":"One of the very few things that survived from the playtest were the integrity mechanics of hunters, which I rather like, particularly formalized high/medium/low integrity 'sins' and conditions that differ on a pass vs fail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T04:19:30-08:00","id":1370303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370290#post1370290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which leads the rather hilarious image of a member of a literal killer cult suddenly realizing she's the conscience of the rest.<br /> <br /> And then screaming into the void for a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact: Beast and Hunter are sister games.<br /> <br /> So, very much so, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-25-2020, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T04:40:01-08:00","id":1370306,"title":"","content":"Hi,<br /> how do you feel about Tactics? Mainly the fact that every hunter can use every tactic (which imho contradicts the idea of tactics being &quot;drilled down to muscle memory&quot; group actions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25828-aegnor","name":"Aegnor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T04:56:14-08:00","id":1370307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370303#post1370303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact: Beast and Hunter are sister games.<br /> <br /> So, very much so, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that supposed to be a secret? They are the two gamelines most likely to crossover with other gameline.<br /> That alone should have had people looking at the parallels. And once you see Heroes and C&amp;C...well, you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T08:51:58-08:00","id":1370368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aegnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370306#post1370306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi,<br /> how do you feel about Tactics? Mainly the fact that every hunter can use every tactic (which imho contradicts the idea of tactics being &quot;drilled down to muscle memory&quot; group actions).</div> </div> </div> </div>Huge improvement. 1e tactics struck me as extremely unfun, and I've been STing hunter for years and years and never seen players willingly take them. You also had to coordinate across the entire cell, ooc-wise, in character planning, and a lot of people already had ideas of what they wanted to do. Then there was the fact that so many are so niche, and you get a cumulative -3 penalty per additional tactic you used in a day. Simply put: you are already paying for tactics in terms of assigning the right attributes and abilities, and in using up your wp risking.<br /> <br /> Though here's a question: why does Adrenaline Surge only help on resisted fear and doubt powers and not contested? I can't think of all that many outside of Demon and Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T09:09:26-08:00","id":1370373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370368#post1370368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huge improvement. 1e tactics struck me as extremely unfun, and I've been STing hunter for years and years and never seen players willingly take them. You also had to coordinate across the entire cell, ooc-wise, in character planning, and a lot of people already had ideas of what they wanted to do. Then there was the fact that so many are so niche, and you get a cumulative -3 penalty per additional tactic you used in a day. Simply put: you are already paying for tactics in terms of assigning the right attributes and abilities, and in using up your wp risking.<br /> <br /> Though here's a question: why does Adrenaline Surge only help on resisted fear and doubt powers and not contested? I can't think of all that many outside of Demon and Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Super agreed, and I love the narrative conceit that a lot of them are ways of speeding up certain processes (namely investigatory ones), but at the cost of making them very high-risk, high-reward. Yes, Identification will get you answers much faster, but man, you better hope no one screws up, or things are going to go BAD. It turns Hunter into a very fast-moving, action-packed, high drama game, which I like.<br /> <br /> Re: Adrenaline Surge -- I suspect most of the Tactics are written based on the theory that you'll be building monsters based on the Dread Powers system we're getting tomorrow, instead of any of the powers of the existing splats. Those might have more powers that fit that bill.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T09:59:38-08:00","id":1370390,"title":"","content":"not gonna lie. kinda worried we may need the final 2 days just to get to conspiracies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T14:34:01-08:00","id":1370446,"title":"","content":"Heya, thanks so much for sticking with the Kickstarter for the final stretch! My team is really excited and we're all hoping to hit more stretch goals. We've still got a lot more previews to go, but if you can help spread the word by sharing what you love about the new edition that'd be super awesome! Thanks, hunters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T14:51:18-08:00","id":1370451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370446#post1370446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heya, thanks so much for sticking with the Kickstarter for the final stretch! My team is really excited and we're all hoping to hit more stretch goals. We've still got a lot more previews to go, but if you can help spread the word by sharing what you love about the new edition that'd be super awesome! Thanks, hunters!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You should join the CofD and official OPP Discords to help talk up Hunter 2e.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://discord.me/cofd\" target=\"_blank\">http://discord.me/cofd</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T16:17:50-08:00","id":1370467,"title":"","content":"ok, I realize now that it's pretty obvious, but what if one of the Flame stretch goals is about the process of becoming a slasher (and maybe involvement of the Hunt Club)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T01:41:24-08:00","id":1370516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370163#post1370163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like what?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Something like Conviction, or other hacks from Mirrors/Armory Revised, presumably optional for people who would rather not use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T01:53:21-08:00","id":1370517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370516#post1370516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Something like Conviction, or other hacks from Mirrors/Armory Revised, presumably optional for people who would rather not use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conviction and/or Skill Tricks could have been a nice addition to the game. I mean, I can get why they aren't here, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T02:01:06-08:00","id":1370518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370517#post1370517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conviction and/or Skill Tricks could have been a nice addition to the game. I mean, I can get why they aren't here, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, there is still chance they put these into the ST chapter. Werewolf have some &quot;hack ideas&quot; in that part of the book, if I remember correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25828-aegnor","name":"Aegnor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T04:28:10-08:00","id":1370528,"title":"","content":"So. The Slender Man's apparently real, and he's attracted to people who experiment with magic.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of information, look under Network Zero's files, search code &quot;FUUUUUUUU--&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, the Devalpa, given how his Virtue is Altruistic and Vice is Petulant, sounds like a potential major character of a sitcom - the Cranky Tentacle Iranian Grandpa Who's Good With Kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 02-26-2020, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T04:55:08-08:00","id":1370532,"title":"","content":"Raise Dead could probably create a rank 1 horror (or a &quot;Minion&quot; if those were used) or something along those lines, instead of requiring each zombie to have its own stat block that is in turn modified by how old it is.<br /> There needs to be some kind of Dread Power numen so that ephemera can take Infernal -- its hard to buy that these are &quot;real&quot; demons from Hell if they cannot possess people and if exorcism never has a role with them.<br /> Discorporate could use some sort of guideline (swarm rules?) as to how hard/easy it is to kill the creepy crawlies. Does a frag grenade automatically work, etc.?<br /> Finally, I noticed that none of the powers that cause doubt/fear/etc. (Dement, Madness and Terror, Awe) in this section actually would be affected by the Adrenaline Surge tactic. Is the Adrenaline Surge tactic's fear protection clause only meant to be useful in crossover?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T05:55:55-08:00","id":1370537,"title":"","content":"the interpretation of slender man is interesting. while I will always see him as an Incarnate Inguma, slender man as a magic searching stalker is quite good for story hooks (but, perhaps having him as both is a possibility)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T05:57:27-08:00","id":1370538,"title":"","content":"Hm. Already thinking of how to make a kuda-gitsune: <a href=\"http://yokai.com/kudagitsune/\" target=\"_blank\">http://yokai.com/kudagitsune/</a><br /> <br /> They seem like perfect Hunter cryptids, since they possess people and are horny little bastards who breed rapidly and so pose a threat to the ecology if not reined in, but they're pets. They don't show up unless a sorcerer is keeping them, and they are a potential resource to a hunter who thinks they can keep ahead of the population of ferret-foxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T06:18:57-08:00","id":1370542,"title":"","content":"I'm very surprised that Slender Man made a pass-through, considering that the Slender Man is copywritten. The entire write-up in that section is also very on the nose, so I am a bit concerned over the Slender Man's inclusion and not a lawyer-friendly facsimile.<br /> <br /> The wide range of monsters is something very enjoyable and I have to say that this section is possibly my favorite so far. It definitely helps flesh out the 2E world as significantly more-packed with inexplicable and bizarre creatures that aren't as clearly-defineable. The focus on environments being a factor on the type of monsters that exist and how Hunters and mortals in general deal with that horror is excellent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T06:22:37-08:00","id":1370543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aegnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370518#post1370518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, there is still chance they put these into the ST chapter. Werewolf have some &quot;hack ideas&quot; in that part of the book, if I remember correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not impossible, but I doubt it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T07:10:11-08:00","id":1370547,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1870_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1870\" data-vbnamecard=\"1870\">mlvalentine</a> I have a concern. As far as I know, the Slender Man is copyrighted. Won't there be any problems on that front?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T07:27:59-08:00","id":1370549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370543#post1370543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's not impossible, but I doubt it.</div> </div> </div> </div>while I'll be honest that i dont really like Conviction as it takes away from the underdog feel and starts to make hunters feel like a supernatural template, it may not be THAT small of a possibility. wasnt the Code just an optional mechanic in 1st edition, after all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T07:43:30-08:00","id":1370552,"title":"","content":"Phew! Lots of excited chatter. Let me address some stuff in one go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370467#post1370467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok, I realize now that it's pretty obvious, but what if one of the Flame stretch goals is about the process of becoming a slasher (and maybe involvement of the Hunt Club)?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Hiya, I have good news for you! This is all in The Slasher Chronicle. In true Hunter fashion, we cooked up alternate rules for you to add to your toolkit.<br /> <br /> 2. @Aegnor: The creative &quot;hack&quot; ideas are part of The Slasher Chronicle. The ST chapter has information to create your own compact, conspiracy, and Endowments to facilitate new groups or additional powers.<br /> <br /> 3. I need to check, but I'm pretty sure the character first appeared in the Chronicles of Darkness rulebook. The character concept is Hunter's version, but I will raise it just to be sure. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T07:51:46-08:00","id":1370553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370549#post1370549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> while I'll be honest that i dont really like Conviction as it takes away from the underdog feel and starts to make hunters feel like a supernatural template, it may not be THAT small of a possibility. wasnt the Code just an optional mechanic in 1st edition, after all?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is why it should be optional. I personally don't see Conviction as being at odds with Hunter. It won't fit every game, but it gives hunters an edge without making them not fundamentally underdogs. But again, I don't see it happening here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 02-26-2020, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T07:58:40-08:00","id":1370554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370549#post1370549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> while I'll be honest that i dont really like Conviction as it takes away from the underdog feel and starts to make hunters feel like a supernatural template</div> </div> </div> </div>It would kind of fit if hunters were defined as that portion of the populace that can't be hoovered up by the monster mind control squad. Nothing really stops vampires as is from chilling out in the hunter safehouse with their oblivious patsies, and that was the beauty of Second Sight: you aren't guaranteed to win, but at least you can't just be dominated and blood bonded and that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T07:59:26-08:00","id":1370555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370552#post1370552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. I need to check, but I'm pretty sure the character first appeared in the Chronicles of Darkness rulebook. The character concept is Hunter's version, but I will raise it just to be sure. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for the quick response about this particular issue.<br /> <br /> The concept of tall, skinny humanoid that does horrible things to people is a universal concept but, as far as I understand, the specific idea of the Slender Man, white featureless being in a black suit, was conceived or at least can be traced back to Eric Knudsen of the Something Awful forums. The specific copyright information is something I don't know but he has given a yes/no to some depictions of Slender Man. I do hope this issue is clarified as he has exercised his copyright before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T08:14:23-08:00","id":1370559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370549#post1370549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> while I'll be honest that i dont really like Conviction as it takes away from the underdog feel and starts to make hunters feel like a supernatural template, it may not be THAT small of a possibility. wasnt the Code just an optional mechanic in 1st edition, after all?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Code was optional. I felt it was an important addition to Second Edition--especially given the fact there's more monsters than ever before. Conviction is present for Deviant and makes sense for that game. With The Cheiron Group present in Deviant, well... I'll let you draw your own conclusions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1870,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","user":"mlvalentine","date":". 02-26-2020, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T08:16:29-08:00","id":1370562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370555#post1370555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you for the quick response about this particular issue.<br /> <br /> The concept of tall, skinny humanoid that does horrible things to people is a universal concept but, as far as I understand, the specific idea of the Slender Man, white featureless being in a black suit, was conceived or at least can be traced back to Eric Knudsen of the Something Awful forums. The specific copyright information is something I don't know but he has given a yes/no to some depictions of Slender Man. I do hope this issue is clarified as he has exercised his copyright before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've raised it with The Powers That BeTM and linked to legal sources for it. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T08:23:15-08:00","id":1370564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370559#post1370559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Code was optional. I felt it was an important addition to Second Edition--especially given the fact there's more monsters than ever before. Conviction is present for Deviant and makes sense for that game. With The Cheiron Group present in Deviant, well... I'll let you draw your own conclusions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could this be clarified for people who have neither played nor read Deviant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T08:24:54-08:00","id":1370565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370564#post1370564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Could this be clarified for people who have neither played nor read Deviant?</div> </div> </div> </div>In what context?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T08:25:48-08:00","id":1370566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370565#post1370565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In what context?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How does the Conviction from Deviant relate to the system that appeared in Mirrors back in 1E nWoD and that I would like to see in Hunter? Why is it important that Cheiron also appears in Deviant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T08:28:31-08:00","id":1370568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370566#post1370566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How does the Conviction from Deviant relate to the system that appeared in Mirrors back in 1E nWoD? Why is it relevant that Cheiron also appears in Deviant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, okay. I cannot speak to how Conviction works in Deviant as its related to Mirrors back in 1E nWoD. The rule for &quot;Conviction&quot; shows up in Deviant and the system is related to your Touchstone. The Cheiron Group is one of the conspiracies that is believed to create the Renegades.<br /> <br /> I might not be thinking the same thing you are, and if I'm not I deeply apologize. I'm trying to get Discord open and haven't had enough caffeine. Blargh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T08:44:15-08:00","id":1370571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370568#post1370568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool, okay. I cannot speak to how Conviction works in Deviant as its related to Mirrors back in 1E nWoD. The rule for &quot;Conviction&quot; shows up in Deviant and the system is related to your Touchstone. The Cheiron Group is one of the conspiracies that is believed to create the Renegades.<br /> <br /> I might not be thinking the same thing you are, and if I'm not I deeply apologize. I'm trying to get Discord open and haven't had enough caffeine. Blargh.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does seem like we're talking about something entirely different. Conviction was a rules hack in Mirrors that gave mortals some minor supernatural tolerance and enhanced Willpower expenditure. The second half is kind of redundant with Willpower risking, I realize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T08:49:26-08:00","id":1370572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370568#post1370568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, okay. I cannot speak to how Conviction works in Deviant as its related to Mirrors back in 1E nWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a system introduced in 1e's World of Darkness: Mirrors (p32-33) as a &quot;power stat&quot; (Supernatural Potency/Tolerance) for normal human characters, providing a handful of additional options for spending Willpower and gradually increasing their supernatural resistance and the amount of Willpower they can spend per turn. It has basically nothing to do with the Touchstone track in Deviant aside from sharing a name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T08:49:43-08:00","id":1370573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370571#post1370571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does seem like we're talking about something entirely different. Conviction was a rules hack in Mirrors that gave mortals some minor supernatural tolerance and enhanced Willpower expenditure. The second half is kind of redundant with Willpower risking, I realize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah-HAH! Gotcha. Thanks for clarifying. Yeah, we are talking about something different. At the same time, you could create an Endowment that performs that function. It'd also be neat if folks expanded on Tactics and leaned into the occult a bit. If an exorcism is a Tactic, why wouldn't a blessing be one as well? :-) Hmmm... Might have to mark that down for the companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T08:57:31-08:00","id":1370579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370554#post1370554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would kind of fit if hunters were defined as that portion of the populace that can't be hoovered up by the monster mind control squad. Nothing really stops vampires as is from chilling out in the hunter safehouse with their oblivious patsies, and that was the beauty of Second Sight: you aren't guaranteed to win, but at least you can't just be dominated and blood bonded and that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, hunters wont just not notice any suspicious activities from fellow hunters, and experienced ones will start to notice that some powers are akin to mental manipulation, and do their best to stop it<br /> <br /> anyway, it would be fine as an optional mechanic. even then though, I feel it pushes hunters to too even ground against monsters. I just find it ridiculous for a hunter to be on even physical grounds against an elder Gangrel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T10:09:07-08:00","id":1370592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370579#post1370579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just find it ridiculous for a hunter to be on even physical grounds against an elder Gangrel</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't even remotely in the ballpark of what Conviction or similar rules hacks permit mortals to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T10:34:52-08:00","id":1370596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370571#post1370571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does seem like we're talking about something entirely different. Conviction was a rules hack in Mirrors that gave mortals some minor supernatural tolerance and enhanced Willpower expenditure. The second half is kind of redundant with Willpower risking, I realize.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the first part is also a bit redundant, as second edition has the Supernatural Tolerance merit (or something of that name), even though it requires have a Supernatural Merit as requierment, IIRC. It still could have been a nice addition to the core, with perhaps some variation to include Endowments (unless it is already there and I missed it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T10:40:21-08:00","id":1370598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370592#post1370592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't even remotely in the ballpark of what Conviction or similar rules hacks permit mortals to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh, well in that case, what does conviction do exactly,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T10:45:48-08:00","id":1370600,"title":"","content":"Thing is, much of what the Conviction hack in Mirrors was designed to do is handled by the Code in H2e. If I were to do a rules hack for incorporating some sort of Conviction-like mechanic into H2e, I'd tie it into the Code by having it represent a given Hunter's dedication to the tenets of monster hunting. I might even link it to the business in the Code about trading out Breaking Points, possibly even making that a prerequisite for Conviction. <br /> <br /> That is, I wouldn't portray Hunter Conviction as an unalloyed good; it would give the hunter extra protection from supernatural influences at the cost of the hunter's own mindset becoming gradually more extreme. <br /> <br /> It would be an \u201coptional trait\u201d not only in that no gaming group would be required to use it if they don't want to, but also in that hunters themselves would see it as a two edged sword, with players of moderate to high Conviction hunters potentially working toward <i>reducing</i> it.<br /> <br /> in the context of the Slasher Chronicle, it might even be that the more Conviction you have, the more likely you are to go Slasher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-26-2020, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T10:48:48-08:00","id":1370602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370598#post1370598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> oh, well in that case, what does conviction do exactly,</div> </div> </div> </div>The version in Mirrors is basically a Power Stat for mortals.<br /> <br /> Active benefits (usable once per chapter): Concentration (mitigate environmental penalties on one skill roll), Drive (boost one Attribute for one roll), Endurance (ignore wounds for a few turns), Perception (spend Willpower to recognize monsters as monsters). <br /> <br /> Passive benefits: lets the character expend multiple Willpower per turn; acts as Supernatural Tolerance. <br /> <br /> Note that the section on Conviction in Mirrors is immediately followed by a section on Expanded Willpower. These are two separate sections; though given their common nature, it's <i>really</i> easy to make the mistake of thinking that Expanded Willpower is part of Conviction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-26-2020, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T11:14:59-08:00","id":1370606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370602#post1370602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Passive benefits: lets the character expend multiple Willpower per turn</div> </div> </div> </div>Did Conviction allow the character to expend multiple Willpower <i>per action</i>? If not, then that's already a core rule in second edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T11:16:43-08:00","id":1370607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370602#post1370602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The version in Mirrors is basically a Power Stat for mortals.<br /> <br /> Active benefits (usable once per chapter): Concentration (mitigate environmental penalties on one skill roll), Drive (boost one Attribute for one roll), Endurance (ignore wounds for a few turns), Perception (spend Willpower to recognize monsters as monsters). <br /> <br /> Passive benefits: lets the character expend multiple Willpower per turn; acts as Supernatural Tolerance. <br /> <br /> Note that the section on Conviction in Mirrors is immediately followed by a section on Expanded Willpower. These are two separate sections; though given their common nature, it's <i>really</i> easy to make the mistake of thinking that Expanded Willpower is part of Conviction.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh, so it did not take attributes above 5 dots? well ok, I can see Conviction in a better light then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T11:24:45-08:00","id":1370610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370607#post1370607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh, so it did not take attributes above 5 dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>It didn't even provide a one-to-one Supernatural Tolerance boost. The bulk of its power came from the active benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T12:32:35-08:00","id":1370623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370606#post1370606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did Conviction allow the character to expend multiple Willpower <i>per action</i>? If not, then that's already a core rule in second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div> Obviously, it would require changes for 2e. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370610#post1370610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It didn't even provide a one-to-one Supernatural Tolerance boost. The bulk of its power came from the active benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Willpower/Turn ranged from 1 at Conviction 1 to 4 at Conviction 10, and Resistance ranged from +0 at Conviction 1 to +6 at Conviction 10. But again, a 2e version wouldn't work precisely the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T13:31:22-08:00","id":1370634,"title":"","content":"I have an idea for a 2e update for Conviction I might write up with some some setting tweaks/expansions for the Vault.<br /> <br /> Rather than tie it to the Code though, my idea was to play up that Conviction reflects an inhuman dedication to the mission, as opposed to the Code which often sets boundaries on the mission. One negative side effect of Conviction will be lowering max Integrity. Too much Conviction basically makes you into a an HtR Wayward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T13:32:02-08:00","id":1370635,"title":"","content":"Setting aside the Conviction discussion for a moment, one other hack I'm thinking of implementing involving the Code is to give even tier one hunters an opportunity to trade out Breaking Points. That is, rather than a Hunter Org being a <i>requirement</i> for doing this, I'd rather it be a, what, enabler? No, that's not quite right either: a sort of \u201cpath of least resistance\u201d. Making Code changes that conform to your Compact or Conspiracy is either easier to do than making Code changes without such guidance or is more advantageous. The existing rule that social penalties coming from such changes don't apply to other hunters in that Org <i>might</i> be enough if modified with something like \u201c\u2026if the change is in keeping with that org's worldview\u201d. <br /> <br /> It's something to look into, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T13:46:37-08:00","id":1370639,"title":"","content":"On the Ephemeral Entities rules: is there a way we could get something resembling <b>World of Darkness: Inferno</b>'s demons as a third variety of Ephemeral Entity? Given both the Lucifuge and the Malleus Maleficatorum, having a particular category that more or less conforms to their notions of what a demon is would seem to be appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-26-2020, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T14:22:22-08:00","id":1370648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370639#post1370639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Ephemeral Entities rules: is there a way we could get something resembling <b>World of Darkness: Inferno</b>'s demons as a third variety of Ephemeral Entity? Given both the Lucifuge and the Malleus Maleficatorum, having a particular category that more or less conforms to their notions of what a demon is would seem to be appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that that's the goal of the Infernal Dread Power- sure, Ephemerals should generally have Numen, so maybe there could be a note or something on the subject, but the idea is to use it as a &quot;marker&quot; for anything which is connected to Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T15:01:17-08:00","id":1370662,"title":"","content":"As you say, that's a Dread Power. It's also not terribly appropriate for a WoDI-style ephemeral demon: the creature is immune to fire, and can set its surroundings on fire. A WoDI-style demon isn't about fire; it's about corruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T15:43:52-08:00","id":1370670,"title":"","content":"I imagine Hunter second edition was not really built off of first edition's Inferno. If we get a second edition of Inferno, it would probably be built off of this.<br /> <br /> I figure someone would try to homebrew an Inferno demon (I believe others have already done so) for second edition but already existing ephemera seem to fit the niche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T15:47:06-08:00","id":1370672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370538#post1370538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Already thinking of how to make a kuda-gitsune: <a href=\"http://yokai.com/kudagitsune/\" target=\"_blank\">http://yokai.com/kudagitsune/</a><br /> <br /> They seem like perfect Hunter cryptids, since they possess people and are horny little bastards who breed rapidly and so pose a threat to the ecology if not reined in, but they're pets. They don't show up unless a sorcerer is keeping them, and they are a potential resource to a hunter who thinks they can keep ahead of the population of ferret-foxes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Let's start on that, work on my writing a but too:<br /> <br /> <b>Kuda-gitsune</b><br /> <br /> <i>You are a Japanese-American cop in San Francisco, and you are sure the Yakuza are muscling in on your home. Normally they keep to Hawaii, but one of the families of Japanese mob is growing aggressive - extremely, unhealthily so. Your captain thinks they're feeling confident and have had a crop of new recruits full of piss, vinegar, and dreams of making it big, but you'd expect </i>some <i>caution. They're reckless, with the younger thugs being confused and almost relieved to be arrested and put away from their bosses for a bit, and said bosses look haggard, tired, and desperate. They aren't acting like people who are feeling especially confident, which is why you're tailing a known accountant through their turf, relying on your ethnicity to blend in as the furtive-looking man checks into a nearly empty warehouse with a few other expensive cars up front. Through your binoculars, you see him gather with other men in fine suits in front of delicious - and expensive - looking food, bow to each other, and calmly take out a few dozen bamboo pipes from their suits, and lay them down. From the pipes issues a tide of tiny, orange and yellow forms, somewhere between fox, ferret, and snake, which descend on the table like furry locusts, as their keepers look on in forlorn resignation.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Location: </b>Japan. However, as Japan's people have emigrated to other countries, so have kuda mochi families, and so they are possibly found wherever significant Japanese-speaking populations are, if not farther due to the technique not being exclusive to the culture.<br /> <br /> Kuda-gitsune - literally, &quot;tube fox&quot; - are as to Japan's witches as black cats are stereotyped as being to the European variety. They are <i>yokai, </i>but are unique for being almost always being only involved with humans at the behest of an ostensibly human master. Technically closer to polecats (hence the less popular name, <i>izuna </i>- &quot;least weasel&quot;) biologically, tube foxes are intelligent, trainable, and small beasts drawn to magic in order to help their interesting reproductive process. A lineage of Japanese sorcerers, now known as &quot;kuda mochi&quot; as a whole, soon learned how to mystically bind kuda-gitsune to a family's lineage, becoming a combination of household familiar and pet genie; tube foxes have the ability to possess humans, foretell the future, and hex rivals, meaning a clan of kuda mochi has a perfect way to leverage their kuda-gitsune into wealth and power. What's more, the name comes from their more obvious attribute, their size - more specifically, the lack thereof. A mated pair of tube foxes can easily fit in a short bamboo tubs and is quite happy to do so, while an entire family can grow in a large matchbox, making them easy to hide.<br /> <br /> Which is convenient for the kuda mochi, because one literally cannot have<i> one</i> kuda-gitsune. The yokai ferrets are friendly and tame towards their masters, but this is because they are already incorrigibly social with their own kind. And due to their less-known ability to open doors through invisible worlds, a kuda-gitsune fed with enough magic to the point where it doesn't run away to more fertile grounds invariably summons a mate from the strange, possibly otherworldly place they come from. Much like polecats, they are also capable of breeding year-round, and often do, frequently growing uncooperative and moody if kept isolated from their mates to prevent breeding. Their gestation time can also be ridiculously fast, especially since they can feed on magic to speed development; a well-fed female tube fox can deliver a litter of three-to-seven kits in a week, all of which become independent and sexually mature in three months, and their mother can start working on another litter as soon as her kits are weaned. A few return to the wild, but about one out of every three stay and call in their own mates, leading to a geometric growth in familiars, all of which are magic hungry and are also still animals who need proper care and feeding (and being highly intelligent, kuda-gitsune can grow quite picky). As a result, a kuda mochi needs to have enough mystical strength to command her familiars not to make more familiars, or resign herself of a life of eternally running faster just to stay still, and that her own source of wealth and power doesn't eat her out of house and home with their ever-hungry bellies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T16:38:39-08:00","id":1370681,"title":"","content":"Only in the sense that H2e's Ephemeral Entities come in two flavors: ghosts and not-ghosts. That is, it broadens \u201cspirits\u201d to mean \u201cany Ephemeral Entities that aren't ghosts\u201d. <br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I'm not talking about having H2e reproduce everything about WoDI's demons; I agree that the full treatment of them should be its own book, what with the business of Testaments and True Names and the taxonomy of Whisperers, Diaboli (Deceptors, Immundi, and Larvals), Dominions, Malus Loci, and Archdemons, and Infernal Pacts and the Possessed, etc. <br /> <br /> For H2e, all I'm looking for would be an extension of the Ephemeral Beings section to include the bulk of the Principalities and Powers section of WoDI, beginning in p.47 and ending on p.54. It pretty much has most of it already; the needed additions would boil down to adding demons as a third type of Ephemeral Entity, and differentiating them from ghosts and spirits through a 2e adaptation of Malapraxis and Infernal Influence (the former let's them regain Essence and Willpower from the actions of nearby humans, and the latter is basically a summary of what constitutes the demonic equivalent to the Anchor/Resonance Condition) \u2014 and <i>possibly</i> adding 2e versions of some of the Universal Abilities of the Inferno's demons (Aura of Corruption, The Dragon's Tongue, Soul of Sin, Lord of Lies, and Keeper of Secrets).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T01:22:43-08:00","id":1370714,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there being no way to have a &quot;demon&quot; include &quot;thingies that can possess people and be exorcised&quot; strikes me as a major missing opportunity, as long as one is bothering with the setting having &quot;thingies that can possess people and be exorcised&quot; at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T02:03:32-08:00","id":1370723,"title":"","content":"They might not have had enough room in the corebook. Honestly i think extra monsters and dreadtc powers/numen will be the forth section of the stretch goal book. If nothing else, it is more likely to include demons now.<br /> <br /> Heck, Hunter has never gotten an official Night Horrors book and I can see 'demons' being it's own chapter there, a couple of infernal demons (one material, one emphermeral), an unchained lookalike, etc.<br /> <br /> Give them a little time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T04:39:02-08:00","id":1370733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370723#post1370723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, Hunter has never gotten an official Night Horrors book and I can see 'demons' being it's own chapter there, a couple of infernal demons (one material, one emphermeral), an unchained lookalike, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no point to releasing Night Horrors for Hunter since most of its regular supplements fulfil the same role of supplying new antagonists. But a supplement that focuses on ephemeral and pseudo-ephemeral entities could very well have Hunter-ified rules for infernal demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T04:52:33-08:00","id":1370734,"title":"","content":"Oh I don't know, a &quot;Night Horrors: Threats Unknown&quot; book focusing on all kinds of strangeness not otherwise covered in other core books could be fun. Like the ghouls from the 1e fiction. Plus you fill it with slashers, rogue and corrupted hunters, maybe a sentient infectious Endowment that is itself an antagonist, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T09:17:50-08:00","id":1370776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370723#post1370723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might not have had enough room in the corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div> How much room do you think they'd need? I mean, it's not like I'm asking for a whole new entry: you'd need a paragraph about demons under Crossing Over, a bullet point about how demons regain Essence under Essence, a paragraph about Malapraxis under Advantages (the section that talks about the Integrity, Virtue, and Vice of Ephemeral Entities), a sentence or two about the Dragon's Tongue under the Language entry of Other Traits, a Corrupt Condition in the Manifestation section, and a few odds and ends here and there where mention of \u201cghosts and spirits\u201d would become \u201cghosts, spirits, and demons\u201d. That's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T09:28:46-08:00","id":1370781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370776#post1370776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How much room do you think they'd need? I mean, it's not like I'm asking for a whole new entry: you'd need a paragraph about demons under Crossing Over, a bullet point about how demons regain Essence under Essence, a paragraph about Malapraxis under Advantages (the section that talks about the Integrity, Virtue, and Vice of Ephemeral Entities), a sentence or two about the Dragon's Tongue under the Language entry of Other Traits, a Corrupt Condition in the Manifestation section, and a few odds and ends here and there where mention of \u201cghosts and spirits\u201d would become \u201cghosts, spirits, and demons\u201d. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, after how it felt when Immortals was updated in Mummy 2e (that is, squeezed and unsatisfying), I think that updating a 2e Blue Book splat would be something better to do in a supplement of some kind than in the Core. It may work, but if it won't it could make those who are Inferno fans feel cheated in some way. The Infernal Dread Power is a much safer path, as Dread Powers are gross simplifications by definition.<br /> <br /> Like, I would really want an Inferno 2e update, and I do think that it could be presented as an Hunter supplement (like a Night Horrors book of some kind), but I prefer to not have it than to have it in a way that feels incomplete or too forced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T09:59:12-08:00","id":1370786,"title":"","content":"The difference here is that, despite my mention of WoDI-style demons, these wouldn't be \u201cthe 2e update of WoDI\u201d so much as they'd be \u201chow to do demons as Ephemeral Entities\u201d. The only WoDI connection would be that the additions would be inspired by WoDI and thus compatible with a proper 2e update of WoDI (which I definitely want to see, too; but that's something for a separate post). <br /> <br /> That, and being in H2e means that you're getting \u201cdemons in the context of hunters\u201d; so the fact that it's \u201cincomplete\u201d isn't a problem: H2e's treatment of vampires, werewolves, witches, etc. is awfully \u201cincomplete\u201d, far moreso than this would be. <br /> <br /> As for being forced: as I said initially, we have both the Lucifuge and the Malleus Maleficatorum who in one way or another would benefit from the inclusion of ephemeral demons. I'd also add that the Long Night would be big on fighting these kinds of demons. It's not forced at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T10:31:22-08:00","id":1370791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370786#post1370786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for being forced: as I said initially, we have both the Lucifuge and the Malleus Maleficatorum who in one way or another would benefit from the inclusion of ephemeral demons. I'd also add that the Long Night would be big on fighting these kinds of demons. It's not forced at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant &quot;forced&quot; in terms of wordcount, not themes. Like, forcing something which deserves its share of words into a much smaller format due to wordcount and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T11:17:29-08:00","id":1370800,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. And as I just said, I don't see that as an issue here, either. <br /> <br /> I will say that I'd love to get a \u201cChronicles of Darkness: Inferno\u201d book that gives Infernal demons their due; <i>and</i> I'd like a \u201cFiend Fighters\u201d supplement for H2e that tackles demons in the same way that Night Stalkers tackled vampires, with an emphasis on the \u201cThere are more things in Heaven and on Earth, Horatio, than are dreamt of in your philosophy\u201d notion that Night Stalkers took with regard to vampires, rather than the paint-by-the-numbers approach that Mortal Remains took. But before I get off track, none of that lessens my interest in having a third, demonic, type of ephemeral entity in H2e core. <br /> <br /> Now, getting off track (in a manner of speaking): the original H1e supplements (Witch Finders, Spirit Slayers, and Night Stalkers) addressed mages, werewolves, and vampires in the context of Hunter; but they didn't limit themselves to \u201chow to replicate the Awakened, Uratha, and Kindred using Dread Powers\u201d. I single out Night Stalkers because it tackled its subject matter better IMHO: it actually had a section in it about how to build vampires that are distinctly <i>not</i> Kindred in it, allowing Hunter to \u201csurprise\u201d players who think they know everything about what the monsters in the setting are like and to reinforce the notion that the Darkness in \u201cChronicles of Darkness\u201d is much deeper, diverse, mysterious, and unknown (and possibly even <i>unknowable</i>) than anything else. By contrast, Mortal Remains was basically \u201chow to recreate Prometheans, the Lost, Sin-Eaters, the Arisen, and the Unchained with Dread Powers\u201d: it stuck too closely to the conceptual templates provided by the gamelines in question. I'm hoping that the H2e gameline goes back to its roots in that regard and aims for more diversity in its antagonists rather than conforming to what the other gamelines have done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T11:52:28-08:00","id":1370808,"title":"","content":"Point of confusion on my part: is being a primary actor on a tactic an exception to the way risking willpower normally collapses the difference between normal and dramatic failure? Because all of these tactics have different writeups for failure and dramatic failure, but as far as I can see in a straight read of risking WP (and of the Tactics section!) all of their failures should be dramatic failures. Is that the only exception it makes to normal risking willpower mechanics? I feel like I'm missing something. Why are those normal failure writeups there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","user":"Nicias","date":".  edit: clarifying 02-27-2020, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T11:55:07-08:00","id":1370811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370723#post1370723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might not have had enough room in the corebook. Honestly i think extra monsters and dreadtc powers/numen will be the forth section of the stretch goal book. If nothing else, it is more likely to include demons now.<br /> <br /> Heck, Hunter has never gotten an official Night Horrors book and I can see 'demons' being it's own chapter there, a couple of infernal demons (one material, one emphermeral), an unchained lookalike, etc.<br /> <br /> Give them a little time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't... Reveal... What... GAH!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T11:56:19-08:00","id":1370812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370808#post1370808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point of confusion on my part: is being a primary actor on a tactic an exception to the way risking willpower normally collapses the difference between normal and dramatic failure? Because all of these tactics have different writeups for failure and dramatic failure, but as far as I can see in a straight read of risking WP, all of their failures should be dramatic failures. Is that the only exception it makes to normal risking willpower mechanics? I feel like I'm missing something.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, failure and dramatic failures are not the same thing. The Willpower cost is the same to the primary actor, however, but the fiction does not represent the same result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T12:18:21-08:00","id":1370814,"title":"","content":"All of the information given after the Failure section of a Tactic is a variation on &quot;This tactic does not work&quot; while a Dramatic Failure is &quot;This tactic does not work and additionally (...)&quot;. Because Risking Willpower converts all Failures into Dramatic Failures, there is no mechanical difference. However, the fact that the roll results for Tactics are structured to include both a Failure and a Dramatic Failure is rather confusing to read and misleading as it implies there is the possibility of attaining a mundane Failure result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T12:27:31-08:00","id":1370816,"title":"","content":"I also was confused about the failure effects of Tactics with the required risking of willpower. I think that's probably a section which could use some clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T12:28:47-08:00","id":1370817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370814#post1370814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the information given after the Failure section of a Tactic is a variation on &quot;This tactic does not work&quot; while a Dramatic Failure is &quot;This tactic does not work and additionally (...)&quot;. Because Risking Willpower converts all Failures into Dramatic Failures, there is no mechanical difference. However, the fact that the roll results for Tactics are structured to include both a Failure and a Dramatic Failure is rather confusing to read and misleading as it implies there is the possibility of attaining a mundane Failure result.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of where the clarification needs to be made, and have made a note of it. Risking Willpower does not convert all Failures into Dramatic Failures. That is a verbage error as opposed to a design wrinkle. You can simply fail the Tactic and not have it be a Dramatic Failure. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T12:31:56-08:00","id":1370818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370817#post1370817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm aware of where the clarification needs to be made, and have made a note of it. Risking Willpower does not convert all Failures into Dramatic Failures. That is a verbage error as opposed to a design wrinkle. You can simply fail the Tactic and not have it be a Dramatic Failure. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, is the Failure and Dramatic Failure section in Risking Willpower supposed to read &quot;as the action's usual Failure or Dramatic Failure&quot; rather than just &quot;the action's usual Dramatic Failure&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T12:53:29-08:00","id":1370820,"title":"","content":"I'll be making the clarification in a few places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T12:58:47-08:00","id":1370825,"title":"","content":"Do we know if Contagion Chronicles address Hunters in 2e and Lunacy/Disbelief?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m inclined to rule that with the ability to Risk Willpower comes greater ability to mentally adapt to the supernatural (hence Code modification), and other than the initial breaking point for witnessing a never before encountered supernatural force, Hunters do not experience Lunacy, or the breaking-point/memory edit of Quiessence. This is adaptation protects only the Hunter\u2019s own mind however, and the enhancement to Paradox and Dissonance as a Sleeper witness to Supernal Magic still occur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-27-2020, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T13:34:42-08:00","id":1370834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370825#post1370825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if Contagion Chronicles address Hunters in 2e and Lunacy/Disbelief?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m inclined to rule that with the ability to Risk Willpower comes greater ability to mentally adapt to the supernatural (hence Code modification), and other the initial breaking point for witnessing a never before encountered supernatural force, Hunters do not experience Lunacy, or the breaking-point/memory edit of Quiessence. This is adaptation protects only the Hunter\u2019s own mind however, and the enhancement to Paradox and Dissonance as a Sleeper witness to Supernal Magic still occur.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe it does, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T13:43:42-08:00","id":1370838,"title":"","content":"Okay, folks. I need your help for the last few chapter reveals. Mysterious Places and the Slasher Chronicle will be the newest content added; the ST chapter will also have new &quot;how-to&quot; rules, too. I am stepping back intentionally from commenting on them, because I want to review your thoughts to weigh them for post-development. This doesn't mean I'm not paying attention! This is a good time for me to sit back and let you have fun chatting about the new stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you're out and about, please feel free to let other players know this is intentional and not an oversight. It's important to our team as we move in the last stages. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T13:44:29-08:00","id":1370839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370834#post1370834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't believe it does, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, definitely leaning into my houserule rather than have Hunters constantly forgetting certain foes (or allies) then. I think it\u2019s consistent with how Hunters mentally differ from baseline mortals.<br /> <br /> As a side note, one definite downside of the external aspects of the Lie still applying to Hunters - they HEAL ABYSSAL ENTITIES!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-27-2020, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T13:49:00-08:00","id":1370840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370839#post1370839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, definitely leaning into my houserule rather than have Hunters constantly forgetting certain foes then. I think it\u2019s consistent with how Hunters mentally differ from baseline mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say &quot;same here&quot;, only I'm not terribly likely to run a crossover of Hunter with either of those games, on account of not having them... but it's the principle of the thing, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T16:45:51-08:00","id":1370878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370839#post1370839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, definitely leaning into my houserule rather than have Hunters constantly forgetting certain foes (or allies) then. I think it\u2019s consistent with how Hunters mentally differ from baseline mortals.<br /> <br /> As a side note, one definite downside of the external aspects of the Lie still applying to Hunters - they HEAL ABYSSAL ENTITIES!</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, M2e includes a Merit that's tailor-made for hunters: basically, it's a variant of Sleepwalker that's acquired through exposure to the Supernal. Basically, if your hunter sides a Breaking Point sure to the Quiescence and the player is willing and able to spend the experience to acquire the Merit, the character will be a Sleepwalker from that point on and thus immune to the forgetfulness that Sleepers experience. <br /> <br /> Most Sleepers don't acquire it because it requires a hunter-like mindset of standing up to the supernatural rather than shying away from it; but by the same token, I expect that it would be quite common among hunters who have confronted Supernal menaces. Not <i>universal</i>, mind you; but common enough. (When I can, I'll post a page reference.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T17:09:32-08:00","id":1370882,"title":"","content":"I had a complex house rule about the Sleeping Curse/Lunacy etc that attempted to model the &quot;deeply held taboo&quot; idea in horror fiction, that talking about the supernatural is somehow embarrassing or shameful and people are highly reluctant to do it. My model was the novel &quot;Declare&quot; by Tim Powers, where people would talk themselves out of believing what they'd seen and wouldn't want to talk about it, but wouldn't necessarily just get auto-amnesia'd a la the existing rules for the Sleeping Curse (which close off too many story hooks for my taste).<br /> <br /> Then I just threw up my hands making a complicated rule to handle non-player characters, and just merged &quot;Sleepwalker&quot;, &quot;Fitful Sleeper&quot;, and the 1e merit &quot;A Little Knowledge&quot; into a one-dot version of Unseen Sense and gave it to all hunters/slashers for free while they had taken up the Vigil or an Undertaking.<br /> <br /> Unseen Sense 1 offers a +2 to parsing out supernatural involvement from forensic evidence, newspapers, local gossip, and other forms of indirect evidence. It signified freedom from the invisible shadows of the mind that prevented most regular people from remembering what they've seen, or repressing/denying supernatural encounters. It's the &quot;Sam Winchester uses Google to find this week's episode&quot; merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 02-27-2020, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T17:14:56-08:00","id":1370884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370825#post1370825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if Contagion Chronicles address Hunters in 2e and Lunacy/Disbelief?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m inclined to rule that with the ability to Risk Willpower comes greater ability to mentally adapt to the supernatural (hence Code modification), and other than the initial breaking point for witnessing a never before encountered supernatural force, Hunters do not experience Lunacy, or the breaking-point/memory edit of Quiessence. This is adaptation protects only the Hunter\u2019s own mind however, and the enhancement to Paradox and Dissonance as a Sleeper witness to Supernal Magic still occur.</div> </div> </div> </div>One day, Hunter fans are going to come to terms with this argument.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, Nope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T18:09:22-08:00","id":1370892,"title":"","content":"Fitful Slumber, M2e p.306: if you suffer three or more Breaking Points due to exposure to the Supernal or Abyssal, you're eligible to acquire this one-dot Merit which not only grants you the benefits of being a Sleepwalker, but also grants a +2 to resist further Breaking Points caused by the Supernal or Abyssal. <br /> <br /> There! A fully RAW-based solution for hunters of Supernal or Abyssal prey. <br /> <br /> It doesn't help against Lunacy, Disquiet, or Sybaris; but that's not as much of a problem, and there are other ways of dealing with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T18:27:45-08:00","id":1370894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370892#post1370892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fitful Slumber, M2e p.306: if you suffer three or more Breaking Points due to exposure to the Supernal or Abyssal, you're eligible to acquire this one-dot Merit which not only grants you the benefits of being a Sleepwalker, but also grants a +2 to resist further Breaking Points caused by the Supernal or Abyssal.<br /> <br /> There! A fully RAW-based solution for hunters of Supernal or Abyssal prey.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help against Lunacy, Disquiet, or Sybaris; but that's not as much of a problem, and there are other ways of dealing with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It just feels grossly overpriced to me. It's a full one dot for...permission to participate in the game? Marginal resistance against one effect by one kind of thing? This is the kind of thing I'd hand out for free or expect the core playable template to handle already.<br /> <br /> Mage could have easily solved this problem with a more interesting Sleeping Curse mechanic, the same way Werewolf 2E solved the main issue with Lunacy by making it a roll with a variety of possible outcomes, broadening the story possibilities, but Mage went with a linear kludge rule that created more edge cases than it served a gameplay need. Hunter could have solved it too by just having the template provide the general supernatural hall pass, but none of the specific resistances you need to go past the surface encounter level.<br /> <br /> I don't know, it's a minor issue, but it's a sticking point for me. I get wanting to keep the &quot;magic that is invisible to the uninitiated&quot; trope for Mage purposes, but surely some sort of difference could have been split. Spellcasting you can remember, Mysteries you cannot, something like that. Demon form stuff isn't auto-forgotten by witnesses, Demons still have to be careful, but God-Machine infrastructure is still generally imperceptible. That would have been fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 02-27-2020, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T19:20:39-08:00","id":1370910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370894#post1370894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It just feels grossly overpriced to me. It's a full one dot for...permission to participate in the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Different definitions of Participation.<br /> <br /> Without adjusting anything, Hunters interested in the Awakened are kind of fucked with a Catch-22. They can be a)Sleepers, and therefore fucked over by the Sleeping Curse in terms of Integrity damage and also non-meaningful interaction with their prey in all but the most narrow of circumstances, but also benefit from Quiescience and the ability for spells to eventually slough off, or b) Sleepwalkers, which means they can TRY and interact meaningfully, but any and everything that an Awakened can do to them <i>sticks</i>. Both options suck ass and really don't empower Hunter.<br /> <br /> But that's <i>kind of the point of Awakening</i>.<br /> <br /> Mages are monsters, and one of those ways is as acting as the metaphysical 1%. Hunters, by contrast, aren't anywhere near their game, and at some point the sheer world reinforcing that divide helps with the metaphors at work for Mage, that upper-class elitism creating an untouchable chasm that divides mages from their former humanity, and keeps the &quot;lower classes&quot; in despair of affecting them, to the point their only real hope affecting change on that level is getting advocates on the other side.<br /> <br /> BUT BUT BUT<br /> <br /> <i>THE BIG THING MISSED OFTEN IN THIS CONVERSATION</i><br /> <br /> is that it's <i>kind of the point of Vigil too.</i><br /> <br /> I have argued before that part of the reason Masquerades of various sorts are in place is of course the Vigil-but a really big part of the themes of Vigil is the despair over where humanity <i>just can't do anything</i>. The ignorance, the capacity to grasp the world as it is without the neccesary tools, the impossibility of wrangling nature, human or otherwise-all of that's <i>there. </i>Vigil <i>never promises</i> that Humanity Wins, only that it <i>tries</i>, and <i>often</i> ineffectually, because human fallibility is as important, if not more so, as human empowerment to Hunter the Vigil. Vigil, as SEIZE THE NIGHT as it is, is actually really bleak and pessimistic. <i>BEAST</i> is more optimistic about humanity, on the whole.<br /> <br /> And in this way, Hunters being basically powerless to their most human and most personally inhuman opponents is powerful commentary...that admittedly sucks if you want to play the Knights of Saint Adrian punching out a Seer of the Throne. But it plays <i>perfectly</i> into the themes of both games for that divide between hunter and mages to not only be present, but honestly kind of impassable. And honestly?<br /> <br /> I mean, this is me, but I'll take that kind of thematic honesty over &quot;And then I punch the Praetorian though his Force Field&quot; any day of the week.<br /> <br /> I have no commentary on Lunacy, I feel like everything Hunter fans could want came in with the changes to Lunacy in Second Editon Forsaken. But Awakening versus Vigil? Kids, you don't like it, but it's perfect the way it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-13-2021, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T20:01:47-08:00","id":1370919,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d still apply Fitful Slumber automatically rather than have players repeatedly stuck with PCs forgetting the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T20:12:06-08:00","id":1370922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370919#post1370919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d still apply Fitful Slumber automatically rather than have players repeatedly stuck with PCs forgetting the experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather avoid the situation entirely if I care enough to go into it.<br /> <br /> I am not compromised by the way Hunter and Mage operate this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T20:24:40-08:00","id":1370926,"title":"","content":"Minor reminder that Quiescence more commonly works by self-editing encounters with the Supernal and the Abyssal toward the mundane, which does not do terribly much to retroactively remove a Hunter's suspicion at a mage's involvement in a lot of weird coincidences. You may not remember that that wizard called up the walking dead to assault you and your cell, but you're less likely to forget that they were there and you had a confrontation with them that ended with you having a lot of upsetting bite wounds than you are to think it was weird how quickly they were able to get a pack of wild dogs onto the scene.<br /> <br /> Being constitutionally incapable of safely recalling the details of a scene where the immanent magic of the universe's raw substrata was visibly engaged just means going after the Awakened \u2014 who frequently deal with things that are esoteric even by the standards of most supernatural communities \u2014 is more of a witch hunt based on things not adding up than a guns-blazing showdown with Count Dracula VII. This is, after all, a game where most of the monsters you'll be going after are the ones careless enough to get caught.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T20:43:31-08:00","id":1370927,"title":"","content":"I have no problem with Fitful Slumber costing that exorbitant quantity of\u2026 a single Experience, literally the cheapest that anything in the game can cost. And in a game where Breaking Points from exposure to Supernal and/or Abyssal sources are frequent enough to warrant protection from them, a +2 to the rolls to resist them along with immunity to the memory loss is certainly worth such a meager expenditure. <br /> <br /> Especially for hunters: I would argue that the way Integrity works for them, a Sleepwalking hunter should treat Supernal/Abyssal Breaking Points just like any other supernatural Breaking Point: and <i>that</i> means that repeated exposure to the same kind of Supernal phenomenon won't subject him to multiple Breaking Points. So a hunter with Fitful Slumber gets a +2 against said Breaking Points when they happen; but they tend not to happen after a while. <br /> <br /> If you think it's too expensive, then house rule it. But I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> on this: the existing rules are fine as is; H2e doesn't need to do anything more than it's already doing, and the Contagion Chronicle companion doesn't need to address anything here, either. <br /> <br /> (Note: back when M2e was in production, I fought vociferously for the likes of hunters to have a way to achieve Sleepwalker status on their own. I'm very much with you on that score. But I got what I wanted: Fitful Slumber, as written, does everything I need it to. I'm not going to be house ruling it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T20:46:17-08:00","id":1370929,"title":"","content":"You are also far from obligated to use metaphysics designed to center another game entirely in Hunter, which has different goals, assumptions, and protagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T20:51:42-08:00","id":1370930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370926#post1370926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor reminder that Quiescence more commonly works by self-editing encounters with the Supernal and the Abyssal toward the mundane, which does not do terribly much to retroactively remove a Hunter's suspicion at a mage's involvement in a lot of weird coincidences. You may not remember that that wizard called up the walking dead to assault you and your cell, but you're less likely to forget that they were there and you had a confrontation with them that ended with you having a lot of upsetting bite wounds than you are to think it was weird how quickly they were able to get a pack of wild dogs onto the scene.<br /> <br /> Being constitutionally incapable of safely recalling the details of a scene where the immanent magic of the universe's raw substrata was visibly engaged just means going after the Awakened \u2014 who frequently deal with things that are esoteric even by the standards of most supernatural communities \u2014 is more of a witch hunt based on things not adding up than a guns-blazing showdown with Count Dracula VII. This is, after all, a game where most of the monsters you'll be going after are the ones careless enough to get caught.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as that goes, I still like the idea of an \u201cAfter-Action Report\u201d Tactic developed largely to cope with the memory-altering effects of Quiescence and more generally with memory-altering supernatural phenomena, where the team gets together afterward and forensically pieces together what <i>actually</i> happened. They don't regain their true memories of the event; but they can accept the truth of the AAR without actually remembering the truth. <br /> <br /> The biggest argument I see against an After Action Report Tactic is that it would be cheaper for everyone to acquire Fitful Slumber, rendering the point moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T20:56:32-08:00","id":1370932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370929#post1370929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are also far from obligated to use metaphysics designed to center another game entirely in Hunter, which has different goals, assumptions, and protagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. For what it's worth, the bulk of the argument here has to do with what happens of you choose to do so; and despite ArcaneArts' statement, the existing rules do <i>not</i> say \u201cyou're screwed\u201d if you do. <br /> <br /> Bottom line where I'm concerned is that H2e doesn't need to do anything here; the matter is adequately addressed in M2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T01:20:26-08:00","id":1370947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370930#post1370930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest argument I see against an After Action Report Tactic is that it would be cheaper for everyone to acquire Fitful Slumber, rendering the point moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Fitful Slumber only protects against Quiescence. After-Action Report would broaden that to all sorts of hallucinations and memory manipulation - whether coming from a Vampire, Changeling, Beast or a gas leak. It could even be used to reroll mundane Perception rolls, when Cell members pool their observations together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T02:02:24-08:00","id":1370956,"title":"","content":"Hunter is about some of the huddled mortal masses trying to do something about the messed-up world they live in. Mage is a game where those huddled masses are even more powerless and irrelevant than in the CofD at large - more like unusually talkative furniture.<br /> <br /> They might be the most diametrically opposed games of the franchise - one says &quot;sometimes mortals can matter, at great cost&quot;. The other says &quot;no, they never will and they won't even know they can try&quot;. Trying to reconcile that is probably doomed and I don't see much of a point in trying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T02:06:17-08:00","id":1370958,"title":"","content":"I will probably just give any Hunter for free release from Quiescence, Lunacy, etc. after making this 'first time encounter' Breaking Point. Being hunter itself mean you changed your psyche to accommodate to existence of monsters, in the end - and that goes on territory of the Truth in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-28-2020, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T02:10:39-08:00","id":1370959,"title":"","content":"&quot;Marginal resistance against one effect by one kind of thing?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's just against one kind of thing (if we lump Supernal and Abyssal, but they kinda go hand-in-hand) which kinda sucks if mages were to be a one time antagonist in a longer game*. But it's not &quot;marginal resistance&quot; when it completely removes the Sleeping Curse, along with a bonus to regular breaking points surrounding Supernal/Abyssal. You can't ask for more complete coverage.<br /> <br /> And if you really do think the players in your game should have that Merit, just grant it to them. If you have a game that more or less require a thing or a stat, just have the characters start with it. In our newest game, Deviant set in Bangkok, we get Language or Multilingual (our choice) for Thai for free because that's pretty important for our Russian and Japanese catgirls, cyborg ninjas and walking grey goo scenarios.<br /> <br /> *Which I wouldn't recommend using any of the big splats. If they're not the focus of a game or at least a recurring feature, I'd recommend using the abridged HtV version instead. They're there for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T04:00:49-08:00","id":1370972,"title":"","content":"Well, this was helpful. At some point you have to realize that if brussel sprouts taste like soap to you, you can't house rule them to your taste. I think it's a bad rule in Mage, it's kludgy fail-backwards design, and that's that. So clearly Hunter isn't for me, Mage wasn't for me, and there's no fixing it. I'm not going to &quot;come to terms' with the argument, but that's okay. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 02-28-2020, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T04:39:43-08:00","id":1370978,"title":"","content":"Looking on the bright side of life.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For anyone wondering what the larger conversation of this all is, check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil\">The Lie and The Vigil</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages\">Hunters vs mages</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-28-2020, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T04:58:42-08:00","id":1370981,"title":"","content":"I love Nautilus so much out even though they only have a three-paragraph sidebar mention in the Mysterious Places preview. They sound so menacingly benign, especially considering that they're a seemingly-omnipresent <i>real estate mogul hunter organization</i> that have a sitcom antagonist relationship with the other compacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T05:55:53-08:00","id":1370993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370972#post1370972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So clearly Hunter isn't for me,</div> </div> </div> </div>How does a rule in Mage, a different game, result in you losing interest in HtV?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, why couldn't you just house rule away the &quot;brussel sprouts&quot; completely if you don't like them? It would have a lot of consequences in a Mage game, but almost none of them would impact a Hunter game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-28-2020, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T06:01:09-08:00","id":1370995,"title":"","content":"I must say that I find it weird that there are no examples for Bygones in the preview (unless I am somehow blind and missed them). While I did enjoy the mysterious places, the lack of Bygones disappoints me a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T06:06:29-08:00","id":1370997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370995#post1370995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say that I find it weird that there are no examples for Bygones in the preview (unless I am somehow blind and missed them). While I did enjoy the mysterious places, the lack of Bygones disappoints me a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure this will come up other places, but I need to monitor responses to this chapter (and the Storyteller chapter) before committing to Bygones additions in the corebook. There is a plan that includes *sooper sekrit stretch goals* but I wanted some flexibility.<br /> <br /> I also want to point out that the new Bygones definitions are to specifically avoid having *one* group of hunters hoard all the relics to use for themselves. It's implicit, but I think I need to make it explicit that any tier 3 hunter could find a true Bygone and, with time and study, could unlock it as a new Endowment for *any* conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T06:11:13-08:00","id":1370998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370997#post1370997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure this will come up other places, but I need to monitor responses to this chapter (and the Storyteller chapter) before committing to Bygones additions in the corebook. There is a plan that includes *sooper sekrit stretch goals* but I wanted some flexibility.<br /> <br /> I also want to point out that the new Bygones definitions are to specifically avoid having *one* group of hunters hoard all the relics to use for themselves. It's implicit, but I think I need to make it explicit that any tier 3 hunter could find a true Bygone and, with time and study, could unlock it as a new Endowment for *any* conspiracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much for the response! It indeed clarify the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T06:12:34-08:00","id":1370999,"title":"","content":"Also, less than 11K for the conspiracy stretch goal! *fingers crossed*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T06:28:57-08:00","id":1371005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370999#post1370999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, less than 11K for the conspiracy stretch goal! *fingers crossed*</div> </div> </div> </div>YESSSSSSSSSSSSSSS!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T07:48:43-08:00","id":1371015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370972#post1370972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this was helpful. At some point you have to realize that if brussel sprouts taste like soap to you, you can't house rule them to your taste. I think it's a bad rule in Mage, it's kludgy fail-backwards design, and that's that. So clearly Hunter isn't for me, Mage wasn't for me, and there's no fixing it. I'm not going to &amp;quot;come to terms' with the argument, but that's okay. </div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter doesn\u2019t even assume this comes up. Kind of silly to write off the whole game because you don\u2019t like one crossover dynamic that is easy to ignore, especially with Hunter\u2019s ability to support it\u2019s own witch npcs without Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T07:55:19-08:00","id":1371016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1371015#post1371015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hunter doesn\u2019t even assume this comes up. Kind of silly to write off the whole game because you don\u2019t like one crossover dynamic that is easy to ignore, especially with Hunter\u2019s ability to support it\u2019s own witch npcs without Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially given how easy it is to be a Sleepwalker. I'd argue that hunters invariably are or are charging at top speed towards it given their self-chosen mission being something that rhymes with Awakened Obsessions. Hell, if I wanted to go balls-to-the-wall, I'd say any hunter who has suffered a Breaking Point due to the Code is a Sleepwalker, because they've accepted that they need to be a personal arbiter of what they can and cannot know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T08:21:04-08:00","id":1371020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1370993#post1370993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does a rule in Mage, a different game, result in you losing interest in HtV?</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of my position in the context of being increasingly disappointed with design choices made by the 2nd ed books. So what I\u2019ve come to realize in this discussion is that while I\u2019ve been forgiving so far because I love the settings and flavor, the rules design is always going to taste like soap to me. Since it tastes like cilantro to everyone else, I can only conclude this is a problem on my end.<br /> <br /> Hunter\u2019s been on my campaign bucket list for years but the CofD just generally does not work for me anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 02-28-2020, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T10:35:15-08:00","id":1371043,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who thinks the current scaling of Dread Powers to Rank is a little silly, especially compared to CofD core? Rank 10 Horrors have access to 8 Dread Powers in CofD, but in the Hunter pdfs a Rank 4 Horror has access to 9, and it only scales harder past Rank 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T11:04:07-08:00","id":1371050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1371043#post1371043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who thinks the current scaling of Dread Powers to Rank is a little silly, especially compared to CofD core? Rank 10 Horrors have access to 8 Dread Powers in CofD, but in the Hunter pdfs a Rank 4 Horror has access to 9, and it only scales harder past Rank 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>CofD core is overly stingy on the dread powers (compare how many a rank 1 claimed gets in WtF!) plus the dread powers in Hunter are usually weaker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T15:39:21-08:00","id":1371102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1371043#post1371043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who thinks the current scaling of Dread Powers to Rank is a little silly, especially compared to CofD core? Rank 10 Horrors have access to 8 Dread Powers in CofD, but in the Hunter pdfs a Rank 4 Horror has access to 9, and it only scales harder past Rank 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters are also more capable than blue book characters. That was a factor in power level decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T09:14:02-08:00","id":1371990,"title":"","content":"Hi, at the moment I am not sure, whether I should back the Kickstarter or not. Since the shipping cost to Europe got insane, I was thinking about the &quot;AT COST&quot; PoD VERSION. But the pledge costs 30$ (27 \u20ac) and the &quot;AT COST&quot; price for the Premium Hardcover Version of Changeling was around 50$ (45\u20ac). Furthermore all the other rewards are only discounts, as far as I can see. <br /> Therefore I believe it is cheaper to wait and buy it for the \u201enormal\u201c price at DriveThruRPG. Or did I miss something?<br /> <br /> (The statement on the kickstarter side is, that the 30$ do not include the print cost.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 02-29-2020, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T10:40:05-08:00","id":1371994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1371990#post1371990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, at the moment I am not sure, whether I should back the Kickstarter or not. Since the shipping cost to Europe got insane, I was thinking about the &quot;AT COST&quot; PoD VERSION. But the pledge costs 30$ (27 \u20ac) and the &quot;AT COST&quot; price for the Premium Hardcover Version of Changeling was around 50$ (45\u20ac). Furthermore all the other rewards are only discounts, as far as I can see.<br /> Therefore I believe it is cheaper to wait and buy it for the \u201enormal\u201c price at DriveThruRPG. Or did I miss something?<br /> <br /> (The statement on the kickstarter side is, that the 30$ do not include the print cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, while I am not sure how the sipping cost works within the Kickstarter vs after it, at the very least you could gain the pdf AND the companion's pdf copies for 25$, or at the very least gain early access to the manuscript for 5$, so while you are waiting for the PoD version you would already have access to Hunter 2e.<br /> <br /> Also, less than 8k for conspiracies!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T11:59:33-08:00","id":1372010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1371994#post1371994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, while I am not sure how the sipping cost works within the Kickstarter vs after it [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hardcover version of the Kickstarter campaign is delivered from the USA for 50$. DriveThruRPG ships the POD version from the UK. Therefore it\u2019s much cheaper (9$). <br /> <br /> \u201e(Premium) Hardcover + PDF\u201c comparison<br /> Kickstarter Hardcover version = 50 $ (pledge) + 50 $ (shipping) = 100 $ (based on the current Kickstarter)<br /> Kickstarter POD version = 30 $ (pledge) + 45 $ (POD) + 9 $ (shipping) = 89 $ (based on an old Kickstarter)<br /> DriveThruRPG POD version = 70 $ (POD) + 9 $ (shipping) = 79 $ (based on a similar product)<br /> <br /> Edit: <br /> I am also interested in a real storyteller screen, but this seems to be a difference of 41$ compared to the third option. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (Kickstarter Hardcover + Storyteller Screen = 120 $)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 03-03-2020, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T11:59:44-08:00","id":1372011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1371990#post1371990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, at the moment I am not sure, whether I should back the Kickstarter or not. Since the shipping cost to Europe got insane, I was thinking about the &quot;AT COST&quot; PoD VERSION. But the pledge costs 30$ (27 \u20ac) and the &quot;AT COST&quot; price for the Premium Hardcover Version of Changeling was around 50$ (45\u20ac). Furthermore all the other rewards are only discounts, as far as I can see.<br /> Therefore I believe it is cheaper to wait and buy it for the \u201enormal\u201c price at DriveThruRPG. Or did I miss something?<br /> <br /> (The statement on the kickstarter side is, that the 30$ do not include the print cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I put a note in with the Operations Manager, Matt. He's at a convention this weekend, but will be checking back on Monday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T12:01:38-08:00","id":1372012,"title":"","content":"Heya, I have a question for you to dissect. Elsewhere, some players wanted to know what happened when/if a romantic interest turned out to be supernatural, and how that factored into breaking points/The Code. Is this something that a) comes up in your games and b) something you'd want clarity on besides &quot;at the Storyteller's discretion&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T12:05:16-08:00","id":1372013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372012#post1372012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heya, I have a question for you to dissect. Elsewhere, some players wanted to know what happened when/if a romantic interest turned out to be supernatural, and how that factored into breaking points/The Code. Is this something that a) comes up in your games and b) something you'd want clarity on besides &quot;at the Storyteller's discretion&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, while I am not sure how much of &quot;romantic conflict&quot; comes in my games, the possibility of discovering that one of your Touchstones has became/always been a &quot;monster&quot; (as dictated by the Code) and its implications could be interesting, to me at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T12:31:13-08:00","id":1372015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372012#post1372012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heya, I have a question for you to dissect. Elsewhere, some players wanted to know what happened when/if a romantic interest turned out to be supernatural, and how that factored into breaking points/The Code. Is this something that a) comes up in your games and b) something you'd want clarity on besides &quot;at the Storyteller's discretion&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember to be glad to see some advises on this subjects in <b>Forsaken Chronicler's Guide </b>- and I was glad to see those. As administrator of minorities inclusive movement in RPGs FB group, I'm more than pro for showing emotional side of characters. And we have whole trope of <i>Buffy-Angel </i>romance in popular culture...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T12:34:21-08:00","id":1372017,"title":"","content":"Touchstones would not be part of this clarification. The point of having a Touchstone is to lean into a mechanical expression that grounds you in everyday reality. It's something outside of the Vigil; not in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T12:41:10-08:00","id":1372019,"title":"","content":"Romance pops up, but it usually develops in-game, and I think it would be unlikely with a hunter who odds are isn't going to have as much in common with a supernatural to spawn any interest. A 'your (insert background character here) was really a supernatural all along' seems like it would be rare enough to not need a mechanic. But I could see it being mentioned maybe with a warning that STs shouldn't alter backgrounds without some sort of consent, and maybe a mention of 'won't turn them supernatural' in the True Friend merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T12:42:48-08:00","id":1372020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372019#post1372019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Romance pops up, but it usually develops in-game, and I think it would be unlikely with a hunter who odds are isn't going to have as much in common with a supernatural to spawn any interest. A 'your (insert background character here) was really a supernatural all along' seems like it would be rare enough to not need a mechanic. But I could see it being mentioned maybe with a warning that STs shouldn't alter backgrounds without some sort of consent, and maybe a mention of 'won't turn them supernatural' in the True Friend merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T13:30:51-08:00","id":1372026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372012#post1372012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heya, I have a question for you to dissect. Elsewhere, some players wanted to know what happened when/if a romantic interest turned out to be supernatural, and how that factored into breaking points/The Code. Is this something that a) comes up in your games and b) something you'd want clarity on besides &quot;at the Storyteller's discretion&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether it would show up or not in my group will probably depend on how it's handled by the game. If it's not mentioned then I don't think anyone of us will bother with the idea, but if it's handled in an interesting way it could actually inspire us to include such a plot point.<br /> To compare it to something similar: In Vampire we'd never expect a Touchstone to &quot;betray&quot; our characters like that because it would break expectations in a bad way, but in Deviant it's absolutely welcome and I even designed one of the Touchstones during character creation with the intention of him flipping side (from Conviction to Loyalty, but still), because Deviant has good mechanics for handling that and it makes the idea so much more appealing.<br /> <br /> But if it's not going to be worked into the mechanics, I'd just have a line of &quot;don't mess with the PC's close relationships without the player's consent&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T17:20:09-08:00","id":1372059,"title":"","content":"We are almost as 85k $ now, 4 days to end, with Conspiracy chapter goal of <i>Tending the Flame </i>at92k $. We surely should get it with last 2 days raising, but nothing more, as it seems...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-01-2020, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T19:59:47-08:00","id":1372085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372059#post1372059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are almost as 85k $ now, 4 days to end, with Conspiracy chapter goal of <i>Tending the Flame at </i>92k $. We surely should get it with last 2 days raising, but nothing more, as it seems...</div> </div> </div> </div>well, if the next chapter ain't 20 thousand away, then I think we can at least net conspiracies and one new chapter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T20:09:27-08:00","id":1372088,"title":"","content":"1692! 1692! 1692! 1692!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T03:25:57-08:00","id":1372122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372019#post1372019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Romance pops up, but it usually develops in-game, and I think it would be unlikely with a hunter who odds are isn't going to have as much in common with a supernatural to spawn any interest. A 'your (insert background character here) was really a supernatural all along' seems like it would be rare enough to not need a mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not having enough in common with a supernatural for romances being common might true for the general NPC Hunter population, but for PCs?<br /> Looking back over all the groups I have been part of, my impression the overlap between players that were interested in playing out romances at all and those that would totally go for making their partner a &quot;was secretely a supernatural all along&quot; is close to 100%. I offhandedly can't think of a single one who wouldn't have jumped at that chance for additional drama.<br /> <br /> Some guidance on the fallout when what supposed to have been the &quot;mechanical expression that grounds you in everyday reality&quot; turns out to not have been that at all could be useful.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T13:45:17-08:00","id":1372185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372012#post1372012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heya, I have a question for you to dissect. Elsewhere, some players wanted to know what happened when/if a romantic interest turned out to be supernatural, and how that factored into breaking points/The Code. Is this something that a) comes up in your games and b) something you'd want clarity on besides &quot;at the Storyteller's discretion&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say if the supernatural is within the Hunter\u2019s own allowable window of personhood already , there shouldn\u2019t be an immediate problem that forces a Breaking Point. If however it\u2019s a being who would have been labeled a Monster beforehand, it should be a Breaking Point whether the Hunter is now treating a loved one as a monster, or going through the cognitive dissonance of changing their definition of monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-02-2020, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T16:43:47-08:00","id":1372202,"title":"","content":"Could we get dread powers that bring monsters/horrors up to at least ephemera levels of toughness (downgrade lethal to bashing and defense vs firearms)?<br /> Something to give a monster a Primal Fear type effect (of being able to punch through defense with close combat) would also be really nice. It feels like firearms are disproportionately effective, for and against, hunter antags, by CofD standards.<br /> <br /> There are almost no defensive dread powers at all, in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T16:54:33-08:00","id":1372203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372012#post1372012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heya, I have a question for you to dissect. Elsewhere, some players wanted to know what happened when/if a romantic interest turned out to be supernatural, and how that factored into breaking points/The Code. Is this something that a) comes up in your games and b) something you'd want clarity on besides &quot;at the Storyteller's discretion&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, yes and yes. I think it would be quite important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372017#post1372017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Touchstones would not be part of this clarification. The point of having a Touchstone is to lean into a mechanical expression that grounds you in everyday reality. It's something outside of the Vigil; not in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What constitutes a touchstone in Hunter seems very hazily defined, and so if your spouse gets turned into a supernatural (lets say a nice one, not one defind as a monster) knocking her off your touchstone list is something I kind of think bears mentioning, if that's what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T18:53:27-08:00","id":1372213,"title":"","content":"A Touchstone who has been turned into a vampire may count as a destroyed Touchstone. One who turns out to be a secret witch/mage all along feels like they should be treated differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T21:27:51-08:00","id":1372221,"title":"","content":"And Touchstone that was Werewolf, Beast or Promethean all along? And yet it still loved you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T21:39:28-08:00","id":1372222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372221#post1372221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Touchstone that was Werewolf, Beast or Promethean all along? And yet it still loved you?</div> </div> </div> </div>the role of a Touchstone is psychological, not metaphysical. When you discover the truth, they no longer serve as a psychological connection to \u201chuman world\u201d part of your existence, so they would no longer function as a touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T02:56:27-08:00","id":1372239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372222#post1372222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the role of a Touchstone is psychological, not metaphysical. When you discover the truth, they no longer serve as a psychological connection to \u201chuman world\u201d part of your existence, so they would no longer function as a touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is really just psychological shouldn't there be mechanical differences if the Hunter that thinks of supernaturals as being a natural parts of the world (like Network Zero does).<br /> As long as the Hunter projects that human connection on the relationship its functionally there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T03:50:20-08:00","id":1372244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372239#post1372239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is really just psychological shouldn't there be mechanical differences if the Hunter that thinks of supernaturals as being a natural parts of the world (like Network Zero does).<br /> As long as the Hunter projects that human connection on the relationship its functionally there.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Human world&quot; as opposed &quot;natural world&quot;. A supernatural Touchstone might not be able to ground you to the mundane existence of regular humans.<br /> Besides, belief in one thing does not equate complete acceptance and normalisation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T04:43:49-08:00","id":1372250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372244#post1372244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Human world&quot; as opposed &quot;natural world&quot;. A supernatural Touchstone might not be able to ground you to the mundane existence of regular humans.<br /> Besides, belief in one thing does not equate complete acceptance and normalisation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still leaves cases where you associate with the Touchstone in a mundane context, say going shopping or cooking with your partner.<br /> I find it hard to belief that a CoD gameline would state that regardless of a character's personal belief it's objectively impossible for them to really accept their partner if that partner happens to do magic in their off time.<br /> That's the kind of rules imposing on Players playing their character the system generally shies away from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T04:56:30-08:00","id":1372253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372250#post1372250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That still leaves cases where you associate with the Touchstone in a mundane context, say going shopping or cooking with your partner.<br /> I find it hard to belief that a CoD gameline would state that regardless of a character's personal belief it's objectively impossible for them to really accept their partner if that partner happens to do magic in their off time.<br /> That's the kind of rules imposing on Players playing their character the system generally shies away from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exposure to the supernatural <i>is a breaking point</i>.<br /> <br /> There's imposing on players, and then there's staying true to the themes of the games. Not all games just let you do whatever you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T07:32:06-08:00","id":1372269,"title":"","content":"So, the Storytelling Chapter came out, and I must say, I'm only slightly bummed we didn't get more Relics/Bygones, because the Endowment design guide is awesome. I'm fine with that space wordcount being used for that instead. Also, I'm happy to see the Ashwood Abbey just got slightly refocused while still having them as screaming hellraiser who everyone else is a bit wary of, and the simple fact the AKD's attitude towards the people they blame for kicking them off their home is &quot;Dude, you threw us out because of petty shit and when we got back the whole continent was gone! YOU HAD ONE JOB!&quot; makes them a lot more palatable than &quot;something something we hate all witches because envy of not being them.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think someone forgot to give Mr. White Infernal, though. He's explicitly a demon, and probably a Lucifuge progenitor at that, even has his own True Name. He's a demon, albeit a rather Erinyes-like &quot;embodiment of retribution&quot; one who is likely going to be both patron and adversary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T07:57:41-08:00","id":1372275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372253#post1372253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's imposing on players, and then there's staying true to the themes of the games. Not all games just let you do whatever you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine either way, but its probably something that deserves to be mentioned in the touchstone or integrity section. Just the notion of &quot;some supernaturals are viewed as people, but the hunter still cannot select them as touchstones&quot; or &quot;touchstones must be a nonmagical place, a nonmagical object, or a non-supernatural, non-hunter mortal, and if this status changes, the touchstone is lost&quot; would be helpful.<br /> <br /> Although I don't personally see why, say, absolutely all hunters would be like that: protecting a family member who is a changeling from huntsmen, a kindred from strix, a ghost from reapers, and so forth seems as reasonable a motive for the Vigil as any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11876,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","user":"Deinos","date":". 03-02-2020, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T08:46:34-08:00","id":1372286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372250#post1372250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That still leaves cases where you associate with the Touchstone in a mundane context, say going shopping or cooking with your partner.<br /> I find it hard to belief that a CoD gameline would state that regardless of a character's personal belief it's objectively impossible for them to really accept their partner if that partner happens to do magic in their off time.<br /> That's the kind of rules imposing on Players playing their character the system generally shies away from.</div> </div> </div> </div>you can accept it and love them, they\u2019re just not a touchstone, because they don\u2019t connect you to the thing touchstones connect Hunters to. Touchstones aren\u2019t a measure of how much you love someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T10:43:56-08:00","id":1372300,"title":"","content":"The storyteller chapter is really good and I already have some ideas for new compacts and conspiraies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T14:07:19-08:00","id":1372329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372269#post1372269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think someone forgot to give Mr. White Infernal, though. He's explicitly a demon, and probably a Lucifuge progenitor at that, even has his own True Name. He's a demon, albeit a rather Erinyes-like &quot;embodiment of retribution&quot; one who is likely going to be both patron and adversary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, he may be a Demon, but I think he is hinted to be far more of the Unchained kind than the Infernal kind, and Infernal means to mark those demons related to Hell. Sure, it may be a mistake, but it could also be very intentional, as a way to say &quot;yes, this is a demon, and no, it is not the an Infernal one&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T14:16:37-08:00","id":1372330,"title":"","content":"As I may have mentioned earlier, the Dread Power \u201cInfernal\u201d doesn't <i>really</i> mean \u201cdemonic\u201d, other than the special bit about the true name; what it's <i>actually</i> about is fire: unless Mr. White is immune to fire and able to set his surroundings ablaze, Infernal isn't really appropriate for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T14:45:33-08:00","id":1372335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372330#post1372330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I may have mentioned earlier, the Dread Power \u201cInfernal\u201d doesn't <i>really</i> mean \u201cdemonic\u201d, other than the special bit about the true name; what it's <i>actually</i> about is fire: unless Mr. White is immune to fire and able to set his surroundings ablaze, Infernal isn't really appropriate for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it does also mean &quot;something which the Lucifuge could influence with Castigation&quot;- as it is stated in their writeup. There are demons without the Infernal Dread Power, but they are outside of the influence of Castigation, per writeup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T16:27:06-08:00","id":1372347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372275#post1372275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm fine either way, but its probably something that deserves to be mentioned in the touchstone or integrity section. Just the notion of &quot;some supernaturals are viewed as people, but the hunter still cannot select them as touchstones&quot; or &quot;touchstones must be a nonmagical place, a nonmagical object, or a non-supernatural, non-hunter mortal, and if this status changes, the touchstone is lost&quot; would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>THat would be helpful indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although I don't personally see why, say, absolutely all hunters would be like that: protecting a family member who is a changeling from huntsmen, a kindred from strix, a ghost from reapers, and so forth seems as reasonable a motive for the Vigil as any. </div> </div> </div>See &quot;Exposure to the supernatural <i>is a breaking point.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> See also &quot;The Code and other things such as Risking Willpower are a (bad-though-understandable) psychological response <i>to</i> said breaking point.&quot;<br /> <br /> A hunter is a person with a skewed relationship to the concept of monsters being people like them-there is, for any and all of them, at least some level where that doesn't sit nicely, because monsters <i>aren't people like they are</i>.<br /> <br /> You can still protect a Changeling family member from the Huntsmen, a Kindred from the Strix, a ghost from Reapers. You can do that all you want. But that's not going to change the fact there is still division of the Changeling, the Kindred, the ghost <i>from</i> you, and normal people-<i>humans like you</i>.<br /> <br /> You're not going to affirm that fundamental line of humanity you used to bring yourself to bear against the night in a such a way as you evoke changes by shoring up your humanity with distinct <i>non-humanity</i>. That is not going to be psychologically beneficial to the warped way any and all hunters decided to cope against the supernatural in traditional short term models. Maybe the long game where a hunter reconciles with their damage enough to not be a hunter anymore, but in the meantime, the Vigil calls, and the Vigil is a fancy way of saying &quot;Do unto others who are not like unto you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hunters <i>hunt monsters</i>. The problems of the splat all stem from a failure to resolve <i>that</i> problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-02-2020, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T16:57:03-08:00","id":1372352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372335#post1372335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it does also mean &quot;something which the Lucifuge could influence with Castigation&quot;- as it is stated in their writeup. There are demons without the Infernal Dread Power, but they are outside of the influence of Castigation, per writeup.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's what I meant. If Mr. White's an Infernal demon, that needs to be in there, because it'd massively flavor his interactions with the Lucifuge. I am leaning towards &quot;yes, he's still that kind of demon&quot;, because it emphasizes how ambivalent the Lucifuge are about their relations, but if not, that's cool, it just needs to be clarified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T18:54:57-08:00","id":1372363,"title":"","content":"Just wanna say, you are <i>not</i> just drawing a gun in Yokohama station.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T19:41:59-08:00","id":1372367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372352#post1372352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's what I meant. If Mr. White's an Infernal demon, that needs to be in there, because it'd massively flavor his interactions with the Lucifuge. I am leaning towards &amp;quot;yes, he's still that kind of demon&amp;quot;, because it emphasizes how ambivalent the Lucifuge are about their relations, but if not, that's cool, it just needs to be clarified.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, if I remember Inferno correctly (the book), his virtue and vice line up perfectly, Justice simply being a justification for inflicting his wrath onto people (and he is just a corrupting influence when you get down to it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T19:46:31-08:00","id":1372369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372363#post1372363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wanna say, you are <i>not</i> just drawing a gun in Yokohama station.</div> </div> </div> </div>...this metaphor.<br /> I<br /> I<br /> I<br /> I<br /> My head.<br /> <br /> Explain, please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T19:51:22-08:00","id":1372370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372347#post1372347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hunters <i>hunt monsters</i>. The problems of the splat all stem from a failure to resolve <i>that</i> problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strange alliances and stranger bedfellows is like...absolutely boilerplate for the genre, though. Hunter lives in the liminal space between man and monster, and like half the game is about how the line between them is often subjective and a matter of perspective. Exposure to the Supernatural is a breaking point because unnatural phenomena are freaky. If the relationship represented by the Touchstone is itself a mundane one, I don't really see the issue, except that it's a golden story hook to have the touchstone burn out or endangered due to the &quot;Oh my god honey, you're a vampire?!&quot; effect.<br /> <br /> But until then a lot of the supernaturals are basically just human beings 99% of the time. If a hunter's touchstone is their therapist, and the therapist is a ghostwalker, and the hunter hasn't found out yet, it seems like just a plot hook in waiting. And following the feature episode around that plot hook, the character decides to &quot;forgive&quot; the ghostwalking, make some accommodation, I really don't see it as fatal to the theme. Sometimes exploring a core theme of a game involves compromising it, carving out exceptions, etc. And complex relationships are such good game fodder it seems weird not to indulge it here. Maybe some other hunters are less compromised and decide the ghostwalking therapist really needs to go. Any number of directions you can take a story hook like that.<br /> <br /> At the very least, &quot;Discovering your touchstone is a monster&quot; sounds like a fun breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 03-02-2020, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T19:55:49-08:00","id":1372371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372369#post1372369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...this metaphor.<br /> I<br /> I<br /> I<br /> I<br /> My head.<br /> <br /> Explain, please?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a metaphor. I was actually catching up on Hunter and read...something where the character drew a gun in Yokohama Station, and <i>you do not just draw a gun in Yokohama Station.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372370#post1372370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Strange alliances and stranger bedfellows is like...absolutely boilerplate for the genre, though. Hunter lives in the liminal space between man and monster, and like half the game is about how the line between them is often subjective and a matter of perspective. Exposure to the Supernatural is a breaking point because unnatural phenomena are freaky. If the relationship represented by the Touchstone is itself a mundane one, I don't really see the issue, except that it's a golden story hook to have the touchstone burn out or endangered once the Hunter is exposed to the supernatural reality of their connection, due to the &quot;Oh my god honey, you're a vampire?!&quot; effect.<br /> <br /> But until then a lot of the supernaturals are basically just human beings 99% of the time. If a hunter's touchstone is their therapist, and the therapist is a ghostwalker, and the hunter hasn't found out yet, it seems like just a plot hook in waiting. And following the feature episode around that plot hook, the character decides to &quot;forgive&quot; the ghostwalking, make some accommodation, I really don't see it as fatal to the theme. Sometimes exploring a core theme of a game involves compromising it, carving out exceptions, etc. And complex relationships are such good game fodder it seems weird not to indulge it here. Maybe some other hunters are less compromised and decide the ghostwalking therapist really needs to go. Any number of directions you can take a story hook like that.<br /> <br /> At the very least, &quot;Discovering your touchstone is a monster&quot; sounds like a fun breaking point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely, but the point is that those things happen and have consequences, particularly on either the relationship between the two going onward or the (less likely because more work than just one) reformation of the sense of self and other that mitigates a hunter's psychology.<br /> <br /> But absolutely, all of that. I was not intending to communicate counter to this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-02-2020, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T20:17:44-08:00","id":1372373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372371#post1372371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a metaphor. I was actually catching up on Hunter and read...something where the character drew a gun in Yokohama Station, and <i>you do not just draw a gun in Yokohama Station.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the writeup for the Teke-Teke in the Monsters Around the World preview, where the character in question is an on-duty police officer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T20:46:43-08:00","id":1372375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372373#post1372373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be the writeup for the Teke-Teke in the Monsters Around the World preview, where the character in question is an on-duty police officer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, missed it in the reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T04:29:42-08:00","id":1372426,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else think that perhaps the Compact/Conspiracy creation section should have stated what is considered to be balanced/appropriate for Status benefits? I mean, sure, we can reverse engineer and all, but still it would have been nice to have some guide rules in case you want to be somewhat more creative than the standard ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T09:14:46-08:00","id":1372477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372426#post1372426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else think that perhaps the Compact/Conspiracy creation section should have stated what is considered to be balanced/appropriate for Status benefits? I mean, sure, we can reverse engineer and all, but still it would have been nice to have some guide rules in case you want to be somewhat more creative than the standard ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something I can agree to. As of now, it seems you can just decide whatever you want as a status benefit (yeah I know, you can see a pattern with the status bendits, but clarification)<br /> <br /> Also, I kinda want to see how compacts and conspiracies are seen from the monsters point of view, would be interesting to see how much they THINK they know about them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T10:06:04-08:00","id":1372492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372426#post1372426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else think that perhaps the Compact/Conspiracy creation section should have stated what is considered to be balanced/appropriate for Status benefits? I mean, sure, we can reverse engineer and all, but still it would have been nice to have some guide rules in case you want to be somewhat more creative than the standard ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would also be nice to now what the exchange rates between Merits Types are for the purpose of Status. For example in the Examples, the Ashwood Abbey get a 4-Dot Social Merit benefit at Rank 5 Status... but the Aegis Kai Doru only get a 2-Dot Mental Merit. So there is an obvious difference, but would this also apply to things like Physical or Fighting Merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24424-magus-black","name":"Magus Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T21:51:04-08:00","id":1372619,"title":"","content":"We are just over 800$ till Conspiracies chapter in Tending the Flame book, with 36 hours till end. We get it surely, but probably nothing more...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T00:25:32-08:00","id":1372630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372011#post1372011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I put a note in with the Operations Manager, Matt. He's at a convention this weekend, but will be checking back on Monday.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for trying, but nothing happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T03:54:08-08:00","id":1372660,"title":"","content":"Aaaand we finally got Conspiracies! Onyx Path, please don't ever do something like that again :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T04:07:14-08:00","id":1372665,"title":"","content":"And we got Slasher Chronicle shared. We will see how it looks like. I'm interested how it work as Tier 2 and Tier 3 problem, as Slashers always felt to me as Tier 1 threat...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-04-2020, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T04:33:55-08:00","id":1372667,"title":"","content":"Can I say I love the new names?<br /> <br /> Frankly, it's a solution I didn't see to the whole &quot;Psychos are like less dangerous chatty Masks and have no Talent for it&quot; problem - now, they're Hypnos, and are actually pretty on the ball and self-controlled when focusing on their ideology, thanks. Which makes them infinitely more compelling, dangerous, and has a clear link to Charmers; a Hypno is what happens when a Charmer starts wondering if they can fix what repels them about humanity, no matter how many people need to be stabbed. It also makes them rather more sympathetic, and thus compelling - on some level, the Hypno <i>wants </i>to connect again, and this empathy powers their obsession and their ability to organize other slashers. And try to corrupt a hunter into something like themselves.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, did anyone detect the whiff of candles and undead space bats coming from the Tier Three section of Hong Kong? Just me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 03-04-2020, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T05:40:03-08:00","id":1372681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372010#post1372010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Hardcover version of the Kickstarter campaign is delivered from the USA for 50$. DriveThruRPG ships the POD version from the UK. Therefore it\u2019s much cheaper (9$).<br /> <br /> \u201e(Premium) Hardcover + PDF\u201c comparison<br /> Kickstarter Hardcover version = 50 $ (pledge) + 50 $ (shipping) = 100 $ (based on the current Kickstarter)<br /> Kickstarter POD version = 30 $ (pledge) + 45 $ (POD) + 9 $ (shipping) = 89 $ (based on an old Kickstarter)<br /> DriveThruRPG POD version = 70 $ (POD) + 9 $ (shipping) = 79 $ (based on a similar product)<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> I am also interested in a real storyteller screen, but this seems to be a difference of 41$ compared to the third option. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (Kickstarter Hardcover + Storyteller Screen = 120 $)</div> </div> </div> </div>Your breakdown is pretty close, however we won't know the final price of the PoD until the book is actually complete as it still needs to go through layout and proofing. By backing the KS, you get the PDF much earlier than waiting until it is available for sale, you get the stretch goal PDFs Tending the Flame and the Jumpstart (assuming we hit that goal before the end), as well as access to the PoD version before it goes up for general sale.<br /> <br /> If that doesn't work for you, you can still support the KS at the PDF level today, which gets access to the early PDF, plus stretch goals before general customers, then buy the hardcover whichever way works best for you.<br /> <br /> M","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T06:07:42-08:00","id":1372693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372667#post1372667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Also, did anyone detect the whiff of candles and undead space bats coming from the Tier Three section of Hong Kong? Just me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, while I am not sure about the reference, and I may have missed it, it is probably because I got so excited to see that THE EATER OF NAMES IS HERE RUN FOR YOUR LIVES","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T06:36:39-08:00","id":1372699,"title":"","content":"So, anyone think Together Now will be in Tending the Flames","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T07:21:57-08:00","id":1372707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372693#post1372693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, while I am not sure about the reference, and I may have missed it, it is probably because I got so excited to see that THE EATER OF NAMES IS HERE RUN FOR YOUR LIVES</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. So you don't know the reference.<br /> <br /> Well, delicious friend, all shall be well and all manner of thing shall be well, but remember a reckoning cannot be postponed indefinitely, and if you don't make stories, they shall be made for you, in particular the ones involving being unaccountably peckish and heading in a NORTHward direction.<br /> <br /> (Because I probably just was more confusing; it's Fallen London. Look up Mr. Eaten, or better yet, don't).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T08:28:19-08:00","id":1372714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372707#post1372707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. So you don't know the reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take heart, friend. The light has not yet gone out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T09:35:46-08:00","id":1372727,"title":"","content":"I have mixed feelings about the renamed Undertakings. I totally get it - but at the same time it feels less evocative of the genre. Intellectually I know making the game friendly to players who have to actually deal with \u201cfreak\u201d and \u201cpsycho\u201d hurled at them regularly is more important than emulating Hollywood\u2019s ableism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-04-2020, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T10:40:12-08:00","id":1372743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372727#post1372727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have mixed feelings about the renamed Undertakings. I totally get it - but at the same time it feels less evocative of the genre. Intellectually I know making the game friendly to players who have to actually with \u201cfreak\u201d and \u201cpsycho\u201d hurled at them regularly is more important than emulating Hollywood\u2019s ableism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel that having a nicknames or &quot;AKA&quot; section would help keep the feel of the genre without making the names seem ableist. <br /> <br /> That having been said, I'm not a fan of Undesireable and Virtuoso for renames. Hypnos and Puppeteers are great and feel natural but the other two seem like a mouthful. I would've went with something like Outcast or Pariah for the Undesireables to keep the idea without making it so lengthy. Can't think of anything good for Virtuosos though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T10:50:34-08:00","id":1372755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372743#post1372743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't think of anything good for Virtuosos though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Really? It puts me in mind of a skilled musician or a master gameplayer, which is essentially what they view themselves as, playing the cops like pianos. Maybe Mastermind would be better, but Puppeteers and Hypnos are better at that than they are, much as they would like to believe otherwise.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm on a roll. Here's a fan update to Strangers! Scourge coming when I have time. I renamed them, due to the fact I'm refocusing on them being bloody-handed scholars and questers to differentiate them from Undersirables, with their real danger being their ability to be patient.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Seeker</b><br /> <br /> <i>No. You're going to help me.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Undesirable's equal and opposite is the Seeker. Both are driven ultimately by self-disgust, but while the Undesirable is driven by resignation he will never be anything better and should punish the world for it, his cousin is driven by the hope that she </span></span></span><i>will </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">be something better, if she pokes (and stabs, and scorches, and mutilates, and abrades...) the world in the right way. Faced with the inherent limitations of their selves, Seekers come to despise their own humanity, and become obsessed with removing with what they see as an inherent flaw or infection within themselves. This can be literal; more than one Seeker became that way over being faced with prejudice over a mental illness or physical deformity, in some way trying to become accepted by reforging themselves in its image, and so forcing the world to break in order to fit them. Some were faced with personal tragedies they couldn't move on from and came to blame themselves for, or simply found their own image of perfection was something they could never attain. Whatever the case, a Seeker is almost incidentally a slasher; their true focus is becoming something other than human, and to the Seeker, that means killing whatever is holding them back. Inevitably, that &quot;what&quot; becomes a &quot;who&quot;, and the Seeker comes to the understanding that hurting those most emblematic of what they hate about themselves will yield the hidden lore they need to evoke their own ascension. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Seekers (and their scourge version, Avatars) tend to be the exception that proves the rule in a lot of ways when it comes to slashers. For one thing, they aren't (consciously) looking for new victims at all times, and their goal when speaking with humans is not always murder. In fact, Seekers tend to be quite empathetic with people they regard as being bound by the same flaws they are or show sympathy for their own, and often develop relationships not dissimilar to the Touchstones of hunters. Of course, by the time someone's become a Seeker, these people are mentally regarded as signs of what the slasher regards as their personal weakness and reasons to keep killing. Quite by accident, they end up becoming little more than camouflage and occasional cats-paws for the Seeker when it's time to sharpen their knives. More worrisome, Seekers are almost inevitably at least mildly skilled occult scholars; if one is planning to transcend humanity, after all, inevitably the Seeker starts studying ways it was previously accomplished. As a result, Seekers often aren't noticed until they've already developed quite the kill count, as they spend a long period between killings, their obsessions dedicated instead to researching their own evolution, and able to pretend to be fully human for extended periods of time. Seekers of any success tend to be expert planners, extremely stealthy, or frequently both. Worse, they often end up joining or forming cults and cabals with other slashers or monsters, trading resources and research for their bloody quest.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hunters matching wits with a Seeker often think they're after a rogue hunter at first. To be frank, it's hardly the worst mistake in the world; Seekers are as diverse as their ideas of perfection, and they commonly show up in any culture with a strong mythology or focus on personal spirituality - which aren't small categories. More than a few focus on killing monsters at first to fully quantify their divine selves, which gives a Seeker plenty of opportunity to infiltrate a compact or conspiracy for their lore and techniques when they need to extract data from people. Worse, sometimes they end up valuing the friendships they develop when lurking in a cell's orbit, and try to help their new friends see the world the same way they do in order to preserve them - and Seekers are not so removed from humanity that they don't realize that explaining that maybe a slasher has the right idea is a good way to get exposed. No, the Seeker looking for assistants and peers is a subtle, gentle advocate of the idea that maybe the Code doesn't need to apply in some situations - and when the cell falls, the slasher is there, offering a gloved hand up, and perhaps some ideas on how they might avoid this kind of failure in the future...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Tells: </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A Seeker's Tell is less of a personal ritual they do to their victims and more of the remains of whatever experimental procedure they had in mind for a particular subject of their lethal curiosity. If the slasher is trying to make himself a vampire or other life-stealing immortal, his victims will be exsanguinated or be hooked up to electrical wires in an attempt to drain their bioenergy into batteries. If she is trying to cure her epilepsy through inducing psychic powers, the bodies she leaves in her wake will have the signs of amateur neurosurgery or the signs of dying in extreme fear, an attempt to provoke the sixth sense through trauma and life-threatening danger. Given how Seekers inevitably change their MOs as this technique or that ritual proves fruitless, this makes discovering their profile hard - were it not for the fact that, due to their peculiar patience, a Seeker often leaves a Tell behind when they use the version of their Talent that enables them to put off killing for a few days; the would-be vampire leaves behind holy symbols, garlic, and other folkloric banes behind, crushed in frustration when he realized they didn't have any noticeable effect, the psychic researcher her own jury-rigged isolation chambers and a string of parapsychologists a little frightened by how intense a recent email contact was when suggesting more intensive versions of Zener cards.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Examples: </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Night Goblin steals babies from their cribs and leads their parents on wild, frequently dangerous and usually law-breaking quests and riddle contests as he follows the rule set out in the childhood fables he read when hiding from his abusive father. One day, he will draw the attention of Unseelie and other child-taking fae for them to train him in their magics and become unable to be harmed by those impure of heart. Helen watches as the monstrous cells she injected in her rival professor multiply and attempt to take him over, coldly taking notes as she notes the behavioral changes as they attempt to find and heal their progenitor - which, unlike her, has functioning legs and doesn't need coke-bottle glasses to see, and her cranial transfer tank is already showing promise. Yuriko sings a wailing prayer as her followers bisect the sacrifice, praying to the goddess they don't know is her future self, unable to be outshined by her &quot;normal&quot; twin sister any more. Mac doubles back to stalk the boxer who beat him in their latest match, looking for some sign of Fomorian ancestry. If he finds it, there will be a sudden, unannounced rematch, and this time, Mac will be eager to show his ancestors he's strong enough to beat a troll to death with his bare hands.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Talent: Steps to Transcendence --- </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Seekers may risk Willpower in the same way as a hunter can when pursuing any action dedicated to their personal mission of transcendence, with all the restrictions and benefits, although they cannot join or initiate Tactics. In addition, rather than having Addicted (Murder) as most slashers, Seekers have Addicted (Personal Quest); so long as they leave a Tell similar to their kills behind when pursuing an activity they feel will help them ascend, Seekers can satisfy their cravings. Naturally, murder is the most satisfactory and cathartic, but Seekers are more capable of being patient and getting nearly as much of a hit from less violent (and more easily hidden) means as death when laying low or planning.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Frailty: Not At Peace --- </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Seekers become highly uncomfortable and self-doubting in long-term social situations, unable to ignore their own sense of being less than those around them. They have to open two extra Doors in any Social Maneuvering attempt due to coming off insecure and insincere in regards to others (because they are always trying to hide their perceived deficiencies). When regaining Willpower through Anchors, the Seeker must roll Resolve + Composure if it has been more than a week since their last murder, with a penalty of -(number of weeks beyond the first); failure indicates the Seeker has become so unsettled by stymied progress that they regain no Willpower for the act, and their next satisfaction of their Addiction </span></span></span><i>must </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">be murder. As a side note, a Seeker cannot be cured of their Addiction, but for one who has regained their Integrity, they merely need to fulfill it, nonviolently or otherwise, in order to reset this Frailty.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T10:55:36-08:00","id":1372757,"title":"","content":"While the chapter has a lot of good things in it, I am somewhat disappointing that there was no extensive description of Cabals- I remember that it was mentioned way back that cabals are going to have a great importance in the Slasher Chronicles, and somewhat expected to see a full description of the Hunt Club as an example cabal, but while the concept itself is somewhat present there isn't much of emphasis about dark organizations dedicated towards murder other than the fact that with the new slasher epidemic they have higher tendency to form.I would have also wanted to somewhat see the &quot;slasher point of view&quot; in the story- like, how they view the sudden rise in their number, what they believe is gathering them, etc, etc. Like, when the idigam and the strix and the reapers were presented, I get, more or less their &quot;side of the story- but for slashers it is somewhat lacking, especially compared to the original Slasher book, where there was a strong feeling of the &quot;slasher's side&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T11:01:08-08:00","id":1372758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372743#post1372743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I feel that having a nicknames or &amp;quot;AKA&amp;quot; section would help keep the feel of the genre without making the names seem ableist. <br /> <br /> That having been said, I'm not a fan of Undesireable and Virtuoso for renames. Hypnos and Puppeteers are great and feel natural but the other two seem like a mouthful. I would've went with something like Outcast or Pariah for the Undesireables to keep the idea without making it so lengthy. Can't think of anything good for Virtuosos though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I for one love the Virtuoso name. Really gives that feeling of a Slasher who's killings are an art that only his very mind could make possible. Besides, &quot;Genius&quot; was always seemed like something you would apply to scientific stuff ONLY.<br /> <br /> Still, not a fan of the new names overall. Just love Virtuoso","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T11:18:37-08:00","id":1372763,"title":"","content":"So, does anyone find where the favored attribute for each Undertaking is detailed? The slasher creation rules say that each Slasher gets their Undertaking's favored attribute increased up to five, but it seems to not details what is it.. Does the writeup means that the ST should decide which attribute should fit which Undertaking? Because if so, it would be very, very weird- like Vampire saying that the ST needs to decide the favored attribute for each Clan or something..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T12:15:34-08:00","id":1372776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372763#post1372763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, does anyone find where the favored attribute for each Undertaking is detailed? The slasher creation rules say that each Slasher gets their Undertaking's favored attribute increased up to five, but it seems to not details what is it.. Does the writeup means that the ST should decide which attribute should fit which Undertaking? Because if so, it would be very, very weird- like Vampire saying that the ST needs to decide the favored attribute for each Clan or something..</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point, but I think the intention is that slashers all have unique Attributes. So it's possible to have a Dextrous Mask or a Manipulative Avenger. Which is fine by me, makes them more unique and unpredictable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T12:18:07-08:00","id":1372777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372776#post1372776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see your point, but I think the intention is that slashers all have unique Attributes. So it's possible to have a Dextrous Mask or a Manipulative Avenger. Which is fine by me, makes them more unique and unpredictable.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, saying &quot;an attribute appropriate to the Undertaking&quot; is meaningless, isn't it? It should be &quot;an attribute appropriate to the slasher&quot; or &quot;attribute of your choice&quot;. If the Undertaking does not decide the favored attribute, that reference is redundant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T13:16:20-08:00","id":1372796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372777#post1372777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, saying &quot;an attribute appropriate to the Undertaking&quot; is meaningless, isn't it? It should be &quot;an attribute appropriate to the slasher&quot; or &quot;attribute of your choice&quot;. If the Undertaking does not decide the favored attribute, that reference is redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True dat. Really roundabout way to say that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T14:38:27-08:00","id":1372830,"title":"","content":"Hey, everyone, wait a second-<br /> <br /> Is it me, or that Mythics haven't showed up, like, at all outside of the lexicon? Like, I assume it doesn't have to be outright referenced in the book, but I was kinda expecting to see how hunters react to mythics (yeah, I know it is probably a code name form Beasts and other similar things, but still)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T20:05:53-08:00","id":1372883,"title":"","content":"And now, Transcendents/Avatars!<br /> <br /> <b>Avatar</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Oh God, save me?&quot; Sorry, not in the mood. </i><br /> <br /> The Avatar remembers her past, and thinks of a discarded husk. They are still recognizable as having once been mortal, and can still walk through the herds of two-legged sheep that surround them without notice, but they are divine wolves. Maybe they reached too far into dark magic and saw no reason to stop, maybe they were so warped by a wicked influence they don't remember what they lost, maybe they were just born a little more powerful than average and learned to revel in it in murderous ways. Whatever the case, the Avatar is both the least and most human of all slashers, for they are small gods of murder, mystical powerhouses in ways comparable to true monsters, all the might of which is attached to an intellect that knows how much of it is only in comparison to humans. At their core, Avatars are ultimately just as insecure and empty as Seekers, and are driven to murder because of it - to confirm their identity rather than form it, but the Avatar ultimately still needs to kill to constantly remind themselves that they are strong. Avatars are the ultimate supernatural bullies, and the teasing only ends when their victims are dead.<br /> <br /> Avatars tend to fall into one of two camps. Thankfully for everyone nearby, the majority are loners; these scourges are glory hogs, and other slashers, especially other Avatars, leave less room for the Avatar to flex their powers. This isn't to say that they scorn company, not hardly. Rather, loner Avatars embark on sprees of gore and terror with the express purpose of sowing fear and, to the Avatar's mind, respect in the mortals around them. If these slashers happen to have the same hunting territory as other slashers, they often are driven to compete with said other killers for space in the tabloids; even if the competition exists only within the Avatar's own mind, having &quot;rivals&quot; that detract from the Avatar's own exploits drives them to ever more spectacular (and lurid) deeds to get the media to focus on them and not their contemporaries. They're generally not <i>stupid </i>about it (few things end the murderous career of a slasher in a more embarrassing way than being arrested), but loner Avatars tend to burn like homicidal candles; twice as brightly and half as long. Unfortunately, Avatars who were once part of a cabal of Seekers, increasingly common in the age of both the internet and the slasher epidemic, tend to be of the opinion that the very fact they have powers means they're secure enough to feel like others don't detract from their ego, and the same need for validation that drives them to murder leads to these Avatars forming regular pantheons of murder. Most tend to be lead by the Avatars among the slashers or are composed entirely of them, but even the vanishingly rare ones where the Avatar takes a back seat find themselves with a few minions. Avatars are still the scourge version of Seekers and desperately seek emotional validation, and few creatures do that better than cultists, and so social Avatars are cult leaders. Most set themselves up as the dark gods (or incarnations of the devil) they see themselves as, but some instead cast themselves as the natural evolution of man, or an ideal to aspire to rather than an inherently better creature. Whatever the case, a frightening number seek to raise favored cultists up to their level - like most narcissists, Avatars feel anyone worthy of being called their friend is deserving of the world they are making, and anyone who hurts an Avatar's priest will find a very lethal guardian angel on their heels. Not infrequently, these include monsters; Seekers were already rather learned for slashers, and Avatars seek lore to better carry themselves in the shadowy world and to anticipate potential threats. A few sacred beasts or even more inhuman gods in their pantheon is an excellent way to cement their personal mythos.<br /> <br /> If Seekers are easily confused for hunters, Avatars are the kings of being false positives for other monsters. By certain metrics, they aren't quite slashers either, but a cell bringing garlic for a vampire is going to be surprised when the self-proclaimed Fang of the Night attacks them in broad daylight while in the middle of a church service. In comparison to other monsters, these slashers <i>want </i>attention and notoriety to a degree, and quickly realize that these new blasphemers are trying to keep their existence a secret and under the radar. All the better to force them into situations where they have to chose between secrecy and the scourge getting away with another atrocity. Social Avatars are even worse, because unlike most mastermind-type monsters, Avatars relish in being able to lead from the front, so that both their enemies and followers may tremble and gape at their power. A few more confident Avatars may even blackmail hunters into getting rid of the supernatural competition or tempt them into satisfying their voracious appetite for lore in return for their cult's own expertise. All in all, an Avatar facing a hunter doesn't just want the hunter to fail and die, but to fail and die in such a way that they realize they never should have tried. In most cases. In the worst, the Avatar decides that such bravery to oppose a god deserves respect - and recruitment to their cult. Few things are more creatively sadistic than a god trying to get a hunter to pray for mercy.<br /> <br /> <b>Tells: </b>Avatars are showoffs, either to get the media to gaze upon their deeds and tremble, or to prove to their cultists and peers that they are worthy of their title. Their Tells are thus bombastic and brutal, showing their supernatural powers in such a way that investigators are either completely baffled or intimidated by the realization their quarry had to be more than human. Beyond that, it depends on the exact personal beliefs of the slasher about their nature and powers, but outright apocalyptic imagery, self-written prophecies of doom, or taunts aimed at the concept of humanity itself are common. The cults of Avatars are even more lurid and brutal in their rites to appease their master, though a bit more out of the way, as the very fact a cult is making rituals to appease and honor them is good enough for the ego of most Avatars until they feel it's time for a godly hunt. Of course, the thing about being unsubtle is precisely that, and figuring out exactly what the Avatar's self-image is becomes a break in the case to predicting them.<br /> <br /> <b>Examples: </b>The reservation bars its doors at night now, its inhabitants afraid of more than prejudice. Wendigo Bill stalks their homes, once a white man deformed by a blessing the shaman he brutalized was too terrified to perform properly; he has come to revel in the feel of Native flesh dribbling down his chin, but the relatives of his first meal need to be reminded of their weakness. Okiku Ikiryo holds her entire town in thrall, people regularly praying to the bone-covered shrine she once oversaw so that her disembodied soul doesn't kill them with their own bodies, even butchering the occasional outsider to change out some of the construction by themselves.The scholars bring the corpses of monsters to Esther, not knowing the reason she pays them in money and security against prying cops is that she takes out the best parts to augment her prosthetic arm, every design of which must be tested on a live subject for her to be content with it. The Cobalt Rebis emerges from their sanctum to inspect the intoxicating potions their alchemical circle made for them to enjoy. The best out of every batch is tutored by the master, the worst must supply blood for the lesson, by themselves or otherwise; they are rather forgiving to those who bring them along to harvest the tithe, naturally. <br /> <br /> <b>Talent: Personal Myth --- </b>Avatars are exceptions to the rules of slashers being relatively weak, supernaturally speaking. While they aren't as strong as some monsters, an Avatar believes so completely in their myth that whatever force made them scourges has made them conduits for their own belief. Like Seekers, they do not have Addicted (Murder), but Addicted (Grandeur), and may risk Willpower in pursuit of actions that support their own personal sense of power. Moreover, each Avatar has a personal supernatural identity; the Cobalt Rebis views themself as the alchemical embodiment of the worth of a human life, while Okiku Ikiryo styles herself as both a living woman and a mighty onyro. As a result, they have the ability to manifest new abilities as their own sense of invulnerability demands; in addition to what Dread Powers they normally have, all Avatars have two &quot;free slots&quot; that may be filled with Dread Powers of their own choosing after an hour-long ritual that incorporates their Tell and leaves evidence of it behind (for a lone Avatar, this generally involves menacing their community in a ritual way, for social Avatars it likely involves their cult in some fashion). These Dread Powers must fit the myth somehow, but given how the Avatar is literally living a power fantasy, they often manifest traits that are useful before being directly thematic (Okiku, for instance, might manifest Hex one day to curse someone who she regards as not giving her shrine enough respect, and Infernal the next day despite not being a demon as her &quot;ghost flames&quot;). These Dread Powers last for a day or until the Avatar's stimulus is invoked (see Frailty), and cannot be changed until they have been reverted. In addition to their free slots, Avatars manifest up to three Dread Powers as part of their fundamental myth and general theatrical nature, like Madness and Terror, Predator's Sense, and Reborn (though of all the scourge Undertakings, Avatars are the most varied).<br /> <br /> <b>Frailty: Man in a Mask --- </b>Avatars' grand gestures are driven by their inadequacy. The same penalties for Willpower recovery Seekers suffer apply to Avatars, but their penalties begin two days after their last murder (or Addiction satisfaction for Avatars with Integrity), and increase by one every two days thereafter (the same taste of power ironically makes them far less patient and more easily frustrated). In addition, Avatars have a personal stimulus that effectively breaks their personal myths by reminding them of the human underneath them. This is different for each Avatar (for Wendigo Bill, it's the seeing the name of the shaman who accidentally cursed him due to Bill's own greed and impatience, for Esther it's being wounded by industrial machinery), but whatever the case, this reverts their Personal Myth Dread Power slots to their unclaimed state, ends all ongoing Dread Powers, and the Avatar must spent a Willpower point to avoid fleeing the scene or immediately attacking the stimulus, suffering a -2 penalty on all dice pools so long as it remains present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 03-06-2020, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T21:11:17-08:00","id":1372892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372830#post1372830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, everyone, wait a second-<br /> <br /> Is it me, or that Mythics haven't showed up, like, at all outside of the lexicon? Like, I assume it doesn't have to be outright referenced in the book, but I was kinda expecting to see how hunters react to mythics (yeah, I know it is probably a code name form Beasts and other similar things, but still)</div> </div> </div> </div>Did not seem to find them ether. Maybe they are referenced in SWORN write-up more, with this whole 'cultural creatures of our forefathers'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T22:27:29-08:00","id":1372902,"title":"","content":"You know, if the reason hunters aren't portrayed as interacting with other gamelines is to preserve mystery and so forth, why not apply that to the ephemeral stuff too? As is, the numina are all old ones, and the ephemera are just the same old ghosts and spirits. Hunter having its own selection of numina, or way for ephemera to switch them for dread powers, would really perk things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T23:44:07-08:00","id":1372911,"title":"","content":"We are only 2200$ till Jumpstart - and only 9 hours of Kickstarter!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T03:44:23-08:00","id":1372929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1372830#post1372830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, everyone, wait a second-<br /> <br /> Is it me, or that Mythics haven't showed up, like, at all outside of the lexicon? Like, I assume it doesn't have to be outright referenced in the book, but I was kinda expecting to see how hunters react to mythics (yeah, I know it is probably a code name form Beasts and other similar things, but still)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It seems more like a term that has meaning within Hunter society, like calling a vampire or alike creature a &quot;bloodsucker&quot;. It shows up in the fiction for the Slender Man monster [<i>A mythic impundulu has been spotted near Johannesburg (...)</i>], for True Bygones [<i>(...) because as far as mythic relics go, no one can be certain what would happen if such an attempt were made</i><i>.</i>], and in Aegis Kai Doru's section for Hong Kong [<i>Though Aegis Kai Doru has not found any mythic relics to add to its considerable collection (...)</i>]. &quot;Mythic&quot; is less of a tangible thing and more of a descriptive term that refers to a creature or object's status as something of legend, like the Cerynian Hind or Excalibur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> mythic: Hunters often use the word \u201cmythic\u201d to identify legendary monsters, locations, or relics that either don\u2019t exist (and therefore can\u2019t be hunted) or are a once-in-a-lifetime find. Examples include: the phoenix, the Lost Continent of Mu, and Poseidon\u2019s Trident. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T07:10:59-08:00","id":1372958,"title":"","content":"I admit I only became interested in Hunter: The Vigil because of the WoD: Slashers book. I'm a huge 80s horror fan so the prospect of them being added to the World of Darkness (New or Old) was incredible. I decided to back the Kickstarter for this because of the Slasher chapter which I just read.<br /> <br /> I really enjoyed the Slasher chapter and deeply want more.<br /> <br /> They need some iconic Slasher NPCs, IMHO, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T11:44:39-08:00","id":1373017,"title":"","content":"Dont know if this is ok, but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1870_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1870\" data-vbnamecard=\"1870\">mlvalentine</a>, is it fine if we can know what those other chapters would've been for Tending the Flames?<br /> <br /> Also, congratulations on the successful kickstarter! Cant wait to see the finished product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T13:28:49-08:00","id":1373057,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... so a Hunter can define the line between Person and Monster as it falls among the supernatural without rewriting any of the Code, right?<br /> <br /> What about as it falls among mortals?<br /> <br /> Can you run Amazon\u2019s \u201cHunters\u201d, defining Nazis as Monsters, and not hemorrhage Integrity like they\u2019re people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T13:40:15-08:00","id":1373060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1373057#post1373057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about as it falls among mortals?<br /> <br /> Can you run Amazon\u2019s \u201cHunters\u201d, defining Nazis as Monsters, and not hemorrhage Integrity like they\u2019re people?</div> </div> </div> </div>Killing a person stops being a Breaking Point at Integrity 3. You could also form a compact to be about it and have it be 'okay if they're Nazis.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T13:47:36-08:00","id":1373064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1373060#post1373060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Killing a person stops being a Breaking Point at Integrity 3. You could also form a compact to be about it and have it be 'okay if they're Nazis.'</div> </div> </div> </div>So it\u2019s doable with an organization facilitated Code modification, but it would require that? You can\u2019t just define them as Monsters the way you can subjectively draw the line with supernaturals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T13:55:43-08:00","id":1373068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1373064#post1373064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it\u2019s doable with an organization facilitated Code modification, but it would require that? You can\u2019t just define them as Monsters the way you can subjectively draw the line with supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's doable without the code, you would just be at Integrity 3, if you did it many times, didn't concern yourself with regaining Integrity, and had very bad luck with rolls. I admit I haven't seen the series, but based on the previews it doesn't seem to be about glibly gunning down Nazis with the casualness one might throw a can into a recycling bin.<br /> <br /> With the code change: 'At tiers two and three, whenever a character would suffer a Code breaking point in direct pursuit of the Vigil, she may instead trade that breaking point out permanently for a new Code tenet specific to her compact or conspiracy, which is always at low Integrity on the breaking point scale.'<br /> <br /> Trade 'Kill a person,' with 'Kill a person unassociated with the Nazi regime.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-05-2020, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T14:29:49-08:00","id":1373074,"title":"","content":"You only get one Code modification right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T14:33:24-08:00","id":1373075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1373074#post1373074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You only get one Code modification right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Continued from the previous, 'She may only do this once. The player and Storyteller should work together to come up with an appropriate new breaking point that embodies the character\u2019s commitment to her organization.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T17:09:55-08:00","id":1373101,"title":"","content":"you can probably kill quite a truckload of people if you have 2+ touchstones, its just a -1 bp, at a net +2. Its like a what, a -4 for mortals? I am more than okay with hunters having SOME discomfort with killing other human beings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T14:05:27-08:00","id":1373255,"title":"","content":"Is the Lure Tactic supposed to be \u201cLure the monster out of this cave right here\u201d or \u201cLure the monster from wherever the heck it is right now, could be across town for all we know?\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_H