ng","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T14:46:33-08:00","id":1373263,"title":"","content":"I would say it Lure a monster in the vicinity to where ever you want it to go. so lure a monster from this cave to outside this cave. to lure this monster into a trap. just not a monster on the other side of town. That would be like a Lead a monster tactic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T15:01:28-08:00","id":1373266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1373259#post1373259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Tactics are not magical powers, unless there is a rational for the later, I lean towards the former</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s what I\u2019d assume but a couple bits of the initial and success descriptions and having Streetwise as a \u201cdrawing target in\u201d skill make it seem like it could mean the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T15:12:37-08:00","id":1373267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1373266#post1373266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s what I\u2019d assume but a couple bits of the initial and success descriptions and having Streetwise as a \u201cdrawing target in\u201d skill make it seem like it could mean the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can now see this tactic being performed to lure out a cryptid in Bourbon Street, just to end up having a Teke Teke come out instead","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-06-2020, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T19:04:23-08:00","id":1373301,"title":"","content":"So I was thinking, the Hunt Club is still considered a compact, but what makes it not a Slasher Cabal? The simple fact its composed of just horrible people, with some just happening to be slashers? Or is it still considered a Slasher cabal (assuming cabal and compact/conspiracy are ultimately the same thing besides one hunting monsters and the other humans)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T19:38:54-08:00","id":1373309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1373266#post1373266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s what I\u2019d assume but a couple bits of the initial and success descriptions and having Streetwise as a \u201cdrawing target in\u201d skill make it seem like it could mean the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Streetwise is one of the broad set of skills, that encompass a whole host of legal and illegal activities. You need to know how a prostitute acts, Streetwise. Need to know where the local gang sells stolen merchandise. Streetwise.<br /> Lure using streetwise makes perfect sense in the first way.<br /> Although a Hunter group using mystical abilities to call targets could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T10:15:33-08:00","id":1373398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1373301#post1373301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was thinking, the Hunt Club is still considered a compact, but what makes it not a Slasher Cabal? The simple fact its composed of just horrible people, with some just happening to be slashers? Or is it still considered a Slasher cabal (assuming cabal and compact/conspiracy are ultimately the same thing besides one hunting monsters and the other humans)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's because a significant portion of them are still entirely human murderers, especially those who work as a team and Boston Rules adherents. Their Code's probably like nothing sane, but they have Integrity and things still trying them to humanity. They also probably are an exception to slashers losing Status when discovered, they just probably roll their eyes and point that member in the right direction. <br /> <br /> One of the really intriguing bits is how they actually work to further the Sower wave of slashers, because that means more interesting and varied game. My guess is they hunt monsters too when going for the challenge, but unlike the Abbey they don't really care if the monster is gone or not, or about whether said monster is worth being killed. They just want a new trophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T11:56:50-08:00","id":1373416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1373398#post1373398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say it's because a significant portion of them are still entirely human murderers, especially those who work as a team and Boston Rules adherents. Their Code's probably like nothing sane, but they have Integrity and things still trying them to humanity. They also probably are an exception to slashers losing Status when discovered, they just probably roll their eyes and point that member in the right direction. <br /> <br /> One of the really intriguing bits is how they actually work to further the Sower wave of slashers, because that means more interesting and varied game. My guess is they hunt monsters too when going for the challenge, but unlike the Abbey they don't really care if the monster is gone or not, or about whether said monster is worth being killed. They just want a new trophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. I would keep in mind that the Boston Rules also tend to have their own &quot;unique&quot; rules on people who &quot;hold others back&quot;. Going on that though, I can totally see the Melbourne rules being focused on monsters more than others<br /> <br /> Anyway, back on topic, yeah, the Sower situation is very interesting. It's a win-win for the Club, and I'll admit I feel like they MAY have an ever so slightly increased focus on hunting slashers considering the compact as a whole wants the power epidemic to get worse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T00:13:04-08:00","id":1373491,"title":"","content":"Heath Ledger Joker: Puppeteer (1e Maniac)<br /> <br /> Mark Hamill Joker (+ comic accurate murder): Hypno (1e Psycho)<br /> <br /> Joaquin Phoenix Joker: Avenger on arc to Legend","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5