" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think any further chapters would just be more places and bygones. maybe some NPCs that could be used. I think we got all the big chapters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel that Tending the Flames might actually have more Bygones as Endowments for AKD. The details are vague (by design, I assume) but the backer rewards have stated that we would be getting 8 expanded write-ups for both Compacts and Conspiracies. Considering that there are 7 of each in the core, they might flesh out Aegis Kai Doru for the supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T11:32:14-07:00","id":1374383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1374382#post1374382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I feel that Tending the Flames might actually have more Bygones as Endowments for AKD. The details are vague (by design, I assume) but the backer rewards have stated that we would be getting 8 expanded write-ups for both Compacts and Conspiracies. Considering that there are 7 of each in the core, they might flesh out Aegis Kai Doru for the supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the 8 compacts and conspiracies would all be entirely new though. I think that was even clarified in the comments section","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T12:09:29-07:00","id":1374390,"title":"","content":"Yeah, while the exact wording of the stretch goals was ambiguous, the way they are presented (be it &quot;new compacts baby!&quot; or &quot;more conspiracies and the endowments which come with them&quot;) strongly suggest that we are getting all new organizations- or updated ones. The AKD would probably be there, and I bet that the Knights of St George would also rear their head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T13:03:54-07:00","id":1374402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1374390#post1374390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, while the exact wording of the stretch goals was ambiguous, the way they are presented (be it &amp;quot;new compacts baby!&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;more conspiracies and the endowments which come with them&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> strongly suggest that we are getting all new organizations- or updated ones. The AKD would probably be there, and I bet that the Knights of St George would also rear their head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont forget Utopia Now! So happy Horn has achieved such a milestone. If they do appear, I wonder if they will still be in denial that they use living things for their tech","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T14:20:15-07:00","id":1374427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1374402#post1374402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dont forget Utopia Now! So happy Horn has achieved such a milestone. If they do appear, I wonder if they will still be in denial that they use living things for their tech</div> </div> </div> </div>If we were to assume that every organization which showed up in the core is going to be presented in the companion (which it is hard for me to believe, as I imagine writers would want to use it to add their own organizations to Hunter, especially with the STV allowing both them or other people to offer their own updates to old organizations), that would include the AKD, Knights of Saint George, Knights of Saint Adrian, Utopia Now, Los Angelitos, Ashwood Abbey, Faithful of Shulpae, Promethean Brotherhood, Hunt Club and Together Now. That's 10 out of 16, and in the case of conspiracies 5-6 out of 8 (depends of the Firestealers have already reached a conspiracy status or not). So yeah, as I guess that the writers want to bring whole new organizations, I won't hold my breath for all of those.<br /> <br /> The AKD and the Abbey, of course, are VERY likely, and Utopia Now would be a very pleasant surprise, but I expect that at least half of those groups would be brand new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T14:22:58-07:00","id":1374428,"title":"","content":"Personally I\u2019d rather see expansion of the stuff in the Hunter core + entirely new organizations over prioritizing revisiting orgs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T14:52:46-07:00","id":1374433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1374427#post1374427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we were to assume that every organization which showed up in the core is going to be presented in the companion (which it is hard for me to believe, as I imagine writers would want to use it to add their own organizations to Hunter, especially with the STV allowing both them or other people to offer their own updates to old organizations), that would include the AKD, Knights of Saint George, Knights of Saint Adrian, Utopia Now, Los Angelitos, Ashwood Abbey, Faithful of Shulpae, Promethean Brotherhood, Hunt Club and Together Now. That's 10 out of 16, and in the case of conspiracies 5-6 out of 8 (depends of the Firestealers have already reached a conspiracy status or not). So yeah, as I guess that the writers want to bring whole new organizations, I won't hold my breath for all of those.<br /> <br /> The AKD and the Abbey, of course, are VERY likely, and Utopia Now would be a very pleasant surprise, but I expect that at least half of those groups would be brand new.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, i only think we may see Utopia now since it has fully ascended into becoming a conspiracy. I do find the Promethean Brotherhood extremely unlike, as much I would LOVE for them to come back (actually as a compact, since I found them very interesting like that, but I bet they could be a conspiracy by now)<br /> <br /> While I wont be surprised seeing the AKD, I'll admit I'll be surprised to see Ashwood Abbey. I would dearly love that to be the case though. I always love the idea of Abbey Debauchery all the while with Bach's orchestral suite number 3 in D major in the background playing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T16:33:45-07:00","id":1374450,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t decide whether Ashwood and AKD in Tending would make sense or not. They may be in core in an abridged capacity but they <i>are</i> already in core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T18:06:36-07:00","id":1374464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1374450#post1374450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can\u2019t decide whether Ashwood and AKD in Tending would make sense or not. They may be in core in an abridged capacity but they <i>are</i> already in core.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the abbey was done this way not only for the SWORN, but because of divisiveness. In a companion, they will not be affecting the playerbase (though, I think that will be taking the compacts and conspiracies depiction on them. A very good thing, but one could argue that would've done away with a divisive playerbase)<br /> <br /> And the AKD does have endowments and a huge presence in the world. They may very well be the longest lived conspiracy. It only makes sense to see them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-12-2020, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:22:59-07:00","id":1386869,"title":"","content":"Is it out yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Didn't anyone ever tell you not to bring claws to a gun fight?</span></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3786-leicsfox","name":"LeicsFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:37:38-07:00","id":1386878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeicsFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1386869#post1386869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it out yet?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/news/monday-meeting/\" target=\"_blank\">In Post-Editing Development and Art Direction at the time of this writing</a>. Deviant's KS ended in mid-October and it's in the same phases of production, so I'm not sure why Hunter would be any different considering its KS ended barely two months ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T20:53:12-07:00","id":1386895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeicsFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1386869#post1386869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it out yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>To put it a different way:<br /> <br /> You'd know if it was out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T09:34:08-07:00","id":1418842,"title":"","content":"I recently joined the forums, so what I say will probably be treading old ground but...<br /> <br /> Can I just say how happy I am about the SWORN compact in the Kickstarter preview? I really like indigenous people getting representation in media, even if the TIPI faction seems like a bunch of assholes (though to be fair, the text does mention the other factions call them out on it).<br /> <br /> I also find the renaming of some of the Slasher Undertakings pretty interesting, though I like the changes in general. Can't wait to see what the final product looks like!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T21:29:32-07:00","id":1458614,"title":"","content":"*looks around*<br /> <br /> Huh. Surprised no one mention it but...backer PDF for Hunter 2e core is finally out!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T04:47:15-07:00","id":1458649,"title":"","content":"I haven't dug into it yet, but it seems there are very few changes compared to the manuscript. Some people seem to have expected more, not sure if it was warranted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T13:17:02-07:00","id":1458716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1458649#post1458649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't dug into it yet, but it seems there are very few changes compared to the manuscript. Some people seem to have expected more, not sure if it was warranted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'm happy with it all. I did notice the SWORN don't have their own quote. They have the Null Mysteriis one lol (and they don't have the sub title below them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T16:59:31-07:00","id":1458747,"title":"","content":"I only gave the original backer manuscript a very quick once-over but now that the backer PDF is out and I've taken the time to read it, I'm honestly pretty shocked at how 2e has completely dropped any mechanical framework for representing the other major splats. One of the things I liked best about 1e was the simplified rules it gave for representing Vampires, Werewolves, Mages and so on as targets of the Hunt. This was great, both because you didn't need to purchase another book to represent some of the most popular monster types out there, and because those books contain a lot of ancillary information about Kindred, Uratha and Awakened Society that would be superfluous in a Hunter game, along with special systems that are only really important within those game lines. Vampires using Willpower to fuel Dread Powers was both faster and easier mechanically, plus the system gave plenty of variations and suggestions that allowed you to run Vampire antagonists that clearly <i>weren't </i>the same Kindred presented in Requiem.<br /> <br /> As it stands, chapter 5 is now one of the weakest parts of Hunter 2e, which is a pretty dire situation for a game all about hunting monsters. I do appreciate the new Dread Powers, but other than that the chapter is largely a copy and paste from the Horrors and Antagonists chapter of the Chronicles of Darkness core rulebook. The bit that I find to be a real head scratcher is why they felt the need to include the whole ephemeral entities subsystem. I don't see what it really adds to the game, and it just wastes 10 pages which is a quarter of the entire chapter. For comparison, 9 pages was all the space it took Hunter 1e to give simplified rules for Vampires, Werewolves, and Mages along with a bunch of Hunter lore and a writeup of a sample antagonist for each.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the most glaring omission is any explanation of infernal demons. Demons are pretty important to Hunter - one of the major Hunter conspiracies is composed entirely of their descendants. Hunter 1e recognised this and dedicated 6 pages to explaining how infernal demons work while also explaining that there are a lot of other things called demons in the Chronicles of Darkness. 2e contains a bunch of references to infernal demons but no explanation of what they are or how they should work. Should they be created using the monster rules, or the rules for ephemeral entities? Better figure that out for yourself because Hunter 2e isn't telling. The worst part of this is that if someone wanted to learn more about infernal demons and picked up the splat titled Demon, they would probably come away very confused. The actual information they need is in Hunter 1e and in World of Darkness: Inferno - both 1st edition books that they are unlikely to find unless they already know what they're looking for.<br /> <br /> Honestly as a backer I'm pretty disappointed with Hunter 2e. I feel like I got more for my money from Mortal Remains than I did from this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","user":"Aurumae","date":". 09-04-2021, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T17:58:00-07:00","id":1458753,"title":"","content":"I'll have to double-check to see what the stretch goals included. But if they don't include something like what Aurumae is taking about, I'd like to see a Night Horrors supplement for H2e that <i>does</i>, kind of: what I'd actually like to see in this hypothetical Night Horrors would be vampires that <i>aren't</i> Kindred; werewolves that aren't Uratha; witches that aren't Awakened; constructs that aren't Prometheans; goblins that aren't Lost; and so on. Close enough that adapting them to represent Kindred, Uratha, etc. is simple; but with clear differences. (And yeah; the \u201cdemons that aren't Unchained\u201d would be the 4e adaptation of the Inferno's demons. That's the sort of difference I'm looking for across the board.)<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see a 2e edition of Compacts and Conspiracies, but including \u2014 and possibly exclusively focusing on \u2014 the various 1e Compacts and Conspiracies that were introduced in the supplements. Again, I don't recall if the stretch goals ended up covering this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T18:22:13-07:00","id":1458756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1458753#post1458753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also like to see a 2e edition of Compacts and Conspiracies, but including \u2014 and possibly exclusively focusing on \u2014 the various 1e Compacts and Conspiracies that were introduced in the supplements. Again, I don't recall if the stretch goals ended up covering this.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as additional content, the stretch goals covered a player's companion with 3 chapters - Cells, Compacts and Conspiracies. The Compacts and Conspiracies chapters would each feature 8 entries, so there is a possibility for several first edition Compacts and conspiracies to make a return","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T20:44:57-07:00","id":1458769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1458753#post1458753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to double-check to see what the stretch goals included. But if they don't include something like what Aurumae is taking about, I'd like to see a Night Horrors supplement for H2e that <i>does</i>, kind of: what I'd actually like to see in this hypothetical Night Horrors would be vampires that <i>aren't</i> Kindred; werewolves that aren't Uratha; witches that aren't Awakened; constructs that aren't Prometheans; goblins that aren't Lost; and so on. Close enough that adapting them to represent Kindred, Uratha, etc. is simple; but with clear differences. (And yeah; the \u201cdemons that aren't Unchained\u201d would be the 4e adaptation of the Inferno's demons. That's the sort of difference I'm looking for across the board.)<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see a 2e edition of Compacts and Conspiracies, but including \u2014 and possibly exclusively focusing on \u2014 the various 1e Compacts and Conspiracies that were introduced in the supplements. Again, I don't recall if the stretch goals ended up covering this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doubt the bottom would happen to be exclusive. A few compacts, even conspiracies such as Les Mysteres, are defunct. While I disagree getting rid of them so blatantly, 2nd edition wants to stress the fragility of the Vigil, even for those people who've made a congregation of candles in the darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T21:00:06-07:00","id":1458771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1458747#post1458747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only gave the original backer manuscript a very quick once-over but now that the backer PDF is out and I've taken the time to read it, I'm honestly pretty shocked at how 2e has completely dropped any mechanical framework for representing the other major splats. One of the things I liked best about 1e was the simplified rules it gave for representing Vampires, Werewolves, Mages and so on as targets of the Hunt. This was great, both because you didn't need to purchase another book to represent some of the most popular monster types out there, and because those books contain a lot of ancillary information about Kindred, Uratha and Awakened Society that would be superfluous in a Hunter game, along with special systems that are only really important within those game lines. Vampires using Willpower to fuel Dread Powers was both faster and easier mechanically, plus the system gave plenty of variations and suggestions that allowed you to run Vampire antagonists that clearly <i>weren't </i>the same Kindred presented in Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean...the regular old Horrors system that was incorporated into 2e as a whole?<br /> <br /> Unless if there's additional material from the 1e version that was never incorporated into the 2e version that I'm not aware of, I'm not sure how that's an issue aside from the inconvenience of pulling up a second book not directly in the same gameline.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T22:14:48-07:00","id":1458781,"title":"","content":"I doubt we will get any <b>HtV</b> 2E books beside those marked in KS Stretch Goals, as Paradox seems to ax CoD gamelines. So be prepared that's all we will get.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> Where are 2E Dread Powers templates for non-Kindred vamps, non-Awakened witches etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-05-2021, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T23:53:19-07:00","id":1458785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1458781#post1458781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as Paradox seems to ax CoD gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>...no they don't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T02:07:31-07:00","id":1458794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1458785#post1458785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...no they don't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's move this discussion to the <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448950#post1448950\">proper topic about C</a></b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448950#post1448950\"><b>oD future </b></a>- where at least few long time OPP posters pointed, like me, that Paradox is doing things like they <b><i>would</i></b> ax CoD games. Talk there about this 'CoD future' sub topic.<br /> <br /> I still looks for this 'Dread Powers build up mechanics' - or did you mean <b>Witch Finders</b>, <b>Night Stalkers</b> and <b>Spirit Slayers</b> from 1E? And <b>Mortal Remains</b> book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-05-2021, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T02:37:21-07:00","id":1458796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1458785#post1458785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...no they don't?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> there's already a thread for this, but to put it briefly we are coming up on 1 year since the last CofD book was announced, 2 years since the last kickstarter and at Onyx Path Con, when Dixie was asked what was next for CofD and her response was essentially &quot;if you want more books talk to Paradox&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T10:38:55-07:00","id":1458847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1458796#post1458796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> there's already a thread for this, but to put it briefly we are coming up on 1 year since the last CofD book was announced, 2 years since the last kickstarter and at Onyx Path Con, when Dixie was asked what was next for CofD and her response was essentially &quot;if you want more books talk to Paradox&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And my response in that thread is still the same as it is now: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448951#post1448951\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448951#post1448951\"> CoD: any plans for the future? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448951#post1448951\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1446753-cod-any-plans-for-the-future?p=1448951#post1448951 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Is there anything new planned for the CoD from Onyx Path? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T10:43:02-07:00","id":1458850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1458794#post1458794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still looks for this 'Dread Powers build up mechanics' - or did you mean <b>Witch Finders</b>, <b>Night Stalkers</b> and <b>Spirit Slayers</b> from 1E? And <b>Mortal Remains</b> book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there clear and decisive proof Dread Powers can't recreate &quot;classic&quot; powers of vampires, shifters, and witches?<br /> <br /> Show me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T12:08:24-07:00","id":1458859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1458850#post1458850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there clear and decisive proof Dread Powers can't recreate &quot;classic&quot; powers of vampires, shifters, and witches?<br /> <br /> Show me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you? Sure. Is it easy? No. Does the book provide any guidance on how to do so? No.<br /> <br /> The really odd thing is that it wasn't this way in 1e. Hunter 1e had the following to say about Vampires:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hunter: The Vigil</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Powers of the Blood<br /> All vampires have the Drain Dread Power, with dots in that determined roughly by their age (for every 50 years dead, assume they gain an additional dot in Drain). Most drink blood, but some seem capable of consuming other elements (memory, dreams, flesh) to gain Willpower, instead. They use Drain, therefore, to gain Willpower to fuel their Dread Powers. Note that each Willpower taken in this way (via the bite) incurs one lethal damage. (See \u201cBite,\u201d p. 157, World of Darkness Rulebook.) Vampires can spend Willpower to heal, meaning they effectively repair their own bodies by consuming the bodies (blood) of others: one Willpower heals two bashing or one lethal; aggravated cannot be healed. Oh, and bullets only cause bashing damage to vampires.<br /> Common Dread Powers include (but are not limited to) Agonize, Ecstasy, Fury, Hypnotism, Impress, Unholy Attribute (Dexterity, Stamina, Strength).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not a lot of text, but provides most of the guidance you need. Furthermore, if you were to try to apply this to 2e you would quickly find that several of the suggested Dread Powers - including the most important one Drain - are not to be found in Second Edition. There is a Numen called Drain but it is not a valid replacement. The Numen is only capable of stealing essence or Willpower, and doesn't require a grapple. The key point made above that Vampires steal Willpower while also dealing damage would have to be houseruled, as would the rule that they take Willpower equal to their dots in the Dread Power (since the Numen Drain doesn't have ranks), and the fact that they need to initiate a grapple to do so.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the Dread Power Ecstasy from 1e has not been duplicated in 2e. In 1e this is used to model the euphoric effect of the Kiss, but if you wanted to do this in 2e (or use the power in some other way) you would again have to houserule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T11:47:33-07:00","id":1459323,"title":"","content":"Where do i post mistakes in the backer pdf? Like there is a grammatical error on page 254 and the table of contents is missing social tactics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T12:09:49-07:00","id":1459324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1459323#post1459323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do i post mistakes in the backer pdf? Like there is a grammatical error on page 254 and the table of contents is missing social tactics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Errata form is <a href=\"https://forms.gle/vUP6HrvAAwxvhRZT7\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Link presents at the checkout/download screen on DTRPG after you &quot;buy&quot; it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T15:04:01-07:00","id":1459346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1458747#post1458747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the most glaring omission is any explanation of infernal demons. Demons are pretty important to Hunter - one of the major Hunter conspiracies is composed entirely of their descendants. Hunter 1e recognised this and dedicated 6 pages to explaining how infernal demons work while also explaining that there are a lot of other things called demons in the Chronicles of Darkness. 2e contains a bunch of references to infernal demons but no explanation of what they are or how they should work. Should they be created using the monster rules, or the rules for ephemeral entities? Better figure that out for yourself because Hunter 2e isn't telling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hunter 2E</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">INFERNAL <br /> The monster is an infernal demon from hell. This Dread Power must be taken for any infernal demon. Infernal creatures are immune to the effects of fire and can spend 1 Willpower and make an appropriate roll to inflict the Inferno Environmental Tilt on an area.<br /> <br /> Special: All demons have a true name. If anyone knows and uses that true name, they gain a +2 bonus to all rolls against the demon. The demon has an additional ban that it must come when it hears its name called, though it does not have to reveal itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>We seem to have different ideas of &quot;isn't telling.&quot; &quot;This power makes this monster a demon, ephemeral or physical&quot; seems pretty clear.<br /> <br /> And of course, there's also a vampire in there - Sea Trow. So it already has an example of &quot;non-Kindred monsters&quot; as an example to follow. And Amarok as something that could be werewolves. So you'll forgive me for being a might skeptical of your criticisms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T16:36:22-07:00","id":1459367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1458859#post1458859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you? Sure. Is it easy? No. Does the book provide any guidance on how to do so? No.<br /> <br /> The really odd thing is that it wasn't this way in 1e. Hunter 1e had the following to say about Vampires:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is not a lot of text, but provides most of the guidance you need. Furthermore, if you were to try to apply this to 2e you would quickly find that several of the suggested Dread Powers - including the most important one Drain - are not to be found in Second Edition. There is a Numen called Drain but it is not a valid replacement. The Numen is only capable of stealing essence or Willpower, and doesn't require a grapple. The key point made above that Vampires steal Willpower while also dealing damage would have to be houseruled, as would the rule that they take Willpower equal to their dots in the Dread Power (since the Numen Drain doesn't have ranks), and the fact that they need to initiate a grapple to do so.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the Dread Power Ecstasy from 1e has not been duplicated in 2e. In 1e this is used to model the euphoric effect of the Kiss, but if you wanted to do this in 2e (or use the power in some other way) you would again have to houserule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Id rather word count not be wasted on explaining how make each individual monster per gameline. Besides with the mechanics we have it's pretty easy for a storyteller to figure &quot;hey, this would be perfect for X monster&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T17:44:31-07:00","id":1459375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1459346#post1459346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We seem to have different ideas of &quot;isn't telling.&quot; &quot;This power makes this monster a demon, ephemeral or physical&quot; seems pretty clear.<br /> <br /> And of course, there's also a vampire in there - Sea Trow. So it already has an example of &quot;non-Kindred monsters&quot; as an example to follow. And Amarok as something that could be werewolves. So you'll forgive me for being a might skeptical of your criticisms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be frank, I was already aware of the Infernal Dread Power and the Sea Trow. There are multiple problems with each of these.<br /> <br /> First, having the explanation (if it can even be called that) of demons exist in a Dread Power is just silly. If I am looking for information on how demons work the Dread Powers section isn't where I would start looking. This, if nothing else, is incredibly poor layout and should be called out as such.<br /> <br /> Beyond that though, Hunter 1e had a separate section in chapter 5 after Dread Powers where it explained in detail how demons work. Much of this information didn't make the transition to 2e. This is fine for the most part - maybe demons don't need to have a Fiendish Flaw and so on in 2e. But 1e gave advice on what demons <i>do.</i> What their motivations are. Why they corrupt mortals. It explained how Hunters can spot demons, how demonic pacts work and so on. All these things are what make the demons <i>demons</i>. In 2e, you've just got generic Horrors with a True Name. Everything else you have to invent for yourself. Worse there isn't even a Dread Power that lets Horrors regain Willpower when mortals indulge their Vices, meaning by the book you <i>can't</i> build the kind of demons that existed in 1e. I don't know about you, but to me driving mortals to sin is much more core to the idea of a demon than immunity to fire damage, and this should be reflected in the mechanics.<br /> <br /> As to the Sea Trow - I think this monster rather proves my point. In order to make this monster function somewhat like a Vampire, they had to break the rules established in the Dread Powers section earlier, and even then it doesn't quite work. This monster has a bite attack that can only be used in a grapple, deals 2 lethal and inflicts the drugged tilt. The drugged tilt here seems to be intended to replace the Ecstasy Dread Power from 1e, or the euphoric effects of the Kiss described in VtR. It's a poor substitute since it doesn't make the target placid, just bad at fighting back, but I digress. The attack itself is built using Dread Attack 2 (Bite) - which specifies that the attack deal 2 lethal and inflict a condition or tilt. However the Dread Power also states &quot;If the creature\u2019s natural weaponry includes a bite, it doesn\u2019t need to establish a grapple in order to bite&quot; so the rule about the Trow needing to grapple and then bite (like a Vampire) isn't possible using the Dread Powers they give you, and has to be handwaved in.<br /> <br /> Worse though, the Trow doesn't have <i>any </i>mechanics for drinking blood. It has the Drain Numen, but unlike the Drain Dread Power in 1e, the Drain Numen just directly steals Willpower from the target (and can be done from across the room). You <i>could</i> houserule that the Trow automatically uses the Drain Numen for free whenever it hits with a bite attack, but they don't suggest that in the book and frankly at that point you might as well just ditch the Dread Powers given to you by Hunter 2e and make your own.<br /> <br /> This is all leaving out the fact that Hunter 2e doesn't have any few short paragraphs saying &quot;here is some guidance on making a Vampire (or Werewolf, or Mage, etc) using the rules presented in this chapter&quot;. Frankly I would happily exchange the page detailing the Sea Trow for an update of page 316 from Hunter 1e (which gives rules and advice for Vampires).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T17:54:08-07:00","id":1459378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1459346#post1459346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We seem to have different ideas of &quot;isn't telling.&quot; &quot;This power makes this monster a demon, ephemeral or physical&quot; seems pretty clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, \u201csets things on fire\u201d doesn't really match up with the demons of the Inferno, name notwithstanding. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1459367#post1459367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather word count not be wasted on explaining how make each individual monster per gameline. Besides with the mechanics we have it's pretty easy for a storyteller to figure &quot;hey, this would be perfect for X monster&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more or less my thought was well, which is why I was suggesting that instead of trying to faithfully recreate the other gamelines using the Horrors rules, they instead do something gameline-adjacent. And Leliel <i>does</i> have a point about some of the existing sample Horrors kind of filling that role, if you look hard enough. That said, I'd still like to see a Night Horrors book that makes the task easier, by explicitly organizing its sample monsters by gameline and encouraging a compare-and-contrast mindset between the gameline protagonists and these alternatives. In short, I'd like something roughly along the lines of a second edition of Mortal Remains, but also covering the \u201cBig Three\u201d as well as Beasts and Deviants while being even less beholden to the visions of the existing gamelines than <b>Witch Finders</b>, <b>Spirit Slayers</b>, and <b>Night Stalkers</b> were: my one big complaint about <b>Mortal Remains</b> is that it <i>didn't</i> take any liberties with the monsters it covered: it tried too hard to produce faithful replicas of the source gamelines and didn't put enough (or often <i>any</i>) effort into considering how the source gamelines' assumptions could be played with to produce something similar but different. Compare how the Created are described in <b>Mortal Remains</b> with how the Reanimated are described in the first edition's core book, for example.<br /> <br /> Now, where I disagree with Aurumae is that I don't feel the need for this sort of stuff in the core book. I'm fine with it being put in a supplement, and not as a \u201cwell, that's the next best thing\u201d attitude. 1e's approach kind of made it feel like the Vigil <i>had</i> to be about going after knock-offs of the other gamelines' protagonists; taking those \u201cknock-offs\u201d out of the core book removes that impression, and replaced it with the impression that there are a <i>lot</i> more monsters or there, both in terms of variety and numbers, than what's in the other gamelines: a cell could spend an entire chronicle hunting down monsters without ever encountering another gameline's monster type; and that's actually quite <i>likely</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-08-2021, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T17:56:26-07:00","id":1459379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1459367#post1459367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Id rather word count not be wasted on explaining how make each individual monster per gameline. Besides with the mechanics we have it's pretty easy for a storyteller to figure &quot;hey, this would be perfect for X monster&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This was my point, it's <i>not</i> easy. If you're a new storyteller with nothing but Hunter 2e and you want your players to go up against a classic Vampire you have <i>fewer</i> tools to do so in 2e compared to 1e because they took the relevant Dread Powers out as well as the advice. As I keep pointing out, there isn't a single Dread Power that can represent a Vampire drinking blood, but there was a Dread Power designed to do just that in 1e. Why didn't they reprint it and rename it if necessary? I have no idea.<br /> <br /> When I backed Hunter 2e on Kickstarter one of the taglines was &quot;more monsters today than ever before&quot;. But instead of getting a book with a really robust monster creation chapter, packed with advice, we instead got a copy/paste of the Horrors and Ephemeral Entities rules from the CofD core book, <i>no</i> advice for making popular monster types, and a list of Dread Powers that was missing the basics needed to make staple monsters like the Vampire work properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T14:18:19-07:00","id":1459470,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Ignore this. I was ranting and really didn't think it through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 09-09-2021, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T15:41:08-07:00","id":1459479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1459379#post1459379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was my point, it's <i>not</i> easy. If you're a new storyteller with nothing but Hunter 2e and you want your players to go up against a classic Vampire you have <i>fewer</i> tools to do so in 2e compared to 1e because they took the relevant Dread Powers out as well as the advice. As I keep pointing out, there isn't a single Dread Power that can represent a Vampire drinking blood, but there was a Dread Power designed to do just that in 1e. Why didn't they reprint it and rename it if necessary? I have no idea.<br /> <br /> When I backed Hunter 2e on Kickstarter one of the taglines was &quot;more monsters today than ever before&quot;. But instead of getting a book with a really robust monster creation chapter, packed with advice, we instead got a copy/paste of the Horrors and Ephemeral Entities rules from the CofD core book, <i>no</i> advice for making popular monster types, and a list of Dread Powers that was missing the basics needed to make staple monsters like the Vampire work properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I kind of agree. The Dread Powers list has some good entries but it seems to lack fairly basic ones 1E had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T17:19:04-07:00","id":1459483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1459379#post1459379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was my point, it's <i>not</i> easy. If you're a new storyteller with nothing but Hunter 2e and you want your players to go up against a classic Vampire you have <i>fewer</i> tools to do so in 2e compared to 1e because they took the relevant Dread Powers out as well as the advice. As I keep pointing out, there isn't a single Dread Power that can represent a Vampire drinking blood, but there was a Dread Power designed to do just that in 1e. Why didn't they reprint it and rename it if necessary? I have no idea.<br /> <br /> When I backed Hunter 2e on Kickstarter one of the taglines was &quot;more monsters today than ever before&quot;. But instead of getting a book with a really robust monster creation chapter, packed with advice, we instead got a copy/paste of the Horrors and Ephemeral Entities rules from the CofD core book, <i>no</i> advice for making popular monster types, and a list of Dread Powers that was missing the basics needed to make staple monsters like the Vampire work properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an example monster called the Sea Trow that is described as 'a type of aquatic vampire.' In its power set you can see Numen (Drain). One of the Dread Powers available is Numen, which lets you choose a Numen to use in lieu of a Dread Power, in this case the Numen is Drain, which drains power from the target (this was the first edition Dread Power you're mentioning, Drain, which drained Health or Willpower). The issue becomes that, as written, it only allows for the drinking of Essence or Willpower. Since for most Hunters Essence is irrelevant, they should probably swap that for Health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T00:02:42-07:00","id":1459513,"title":"","content":"For the Sea Trow, it's not the Drain Numen that turns it into a vampire-like being (although it's perfect for psychic vampires) but rather it's Dread Attack (Bite). Unfortunately it doesn't really get much out of biting people, except for a single WP per session (as oppossed to successes WP each time it uses Drain) due to fulfilling its Aspiration.<br /> <br /> But not having a dedicated feeding Dread Power is a pretty bad oversight, imo. Vampire hunters is by far the most common subgenre in the hunting-supernatural-monsters genre which this game is all about. A feeding Dread Power would also work with a lot of similar monsters as well, if you just leave it open what they need to feed on; blood, flesh, bones, a specific organ, etc. That way you could replicate monsters who feed on flesh or gnaws on bones, as well as cannibalistic immortals who increase their lifespan by eating, say, their victim's liver <s>with fava beans and a nice Chianti</s>.<br /> <br /> I also agree that the Infernal Dread Power is a bad take on Infernal demons from 1e. Aside from the terrible idea to have them be represented through a single Dread Power with no real description for them, it's not even the most suitable Dread Power in the book. Damnation would've been a much, much better choice, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T00:27:41-07:00","id":1459514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1459479#post1459479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I kind of agree. The Dread Powers list has some good entries but it seems to lack fairly basic ones 1E had.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the thing about that...<br /> <br /> 1. OPP has been upfront in saying that they're trying to avoid going nuts with &quot;convert 1e-Thing to 2e&quot; when it comes to 2e material. For instance, why they haven't been in a hurry to convert into 2e EVERY single 1e Bloodline, Lodge, Legacy, etc.<br /> <br /> 2. I can only assume that extends to 1e Dread Powers as well where OPP doesn't want to redo ALL of them for 2e...and thus you're left to convert them yourself to 2e.<br /> <br /> Now, yes I'll concede that feeling like it's mandatory grabbing for an extra book not part of the current edition isn't the best thing...but to be honest, this really isn't an issue with Hunter 2e specifically and is an issue with ALL of the CofD 2e gamelines. And taking into account point #1, and how it looks like 2e is definitely not going to end with having as many supplements as 1e did, well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T04:58:43-07:00","id":1459541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1459514#post1459514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the thing about that...<br /> <br /> 1. OPP has been upfront in saying that they're trying to avoid going nuts with &quot;convert 1e-Thing to 2e&quot; when it comes to 2e material. For instance, why they haven't been in a hurry to convert into 2e EVERY single 1e Bloodline, Lodge, Legacy, etc.<br /> <br /> 2. I can only assume that extends to 1e Dread Powers as well where OPP doesn't want to redo ALL of them for 2e...and thus you're left to convert them yourself to 2e.<br /> <br /> Now, yes I'll concede that feeling like it's mandatory grabbing for an extra book not part of the current edition isn't the best thing...but to be honest, this really isn't an issue with Hunter 2e specifically and is an issue with ALL of the CofD 2e gamelines. And taking into account point #1, and how it looks like 2e is definitely not going to end with having as many supplements as 1e did, well...</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems at odds with some of the other purposes of 2e. OPP have stated that the reason they're reprinting the core rules in every 2e book is so that groups only need one book to run the game. If you're going to do that, then reprinting core abilities from 1e seems like a necessity too. I don't expect them to reprint every Compact and Conspiracy from 1e, nor do I expect them to reprint every Dread Power. But I do think the Dread Power list that we got lacks some of the essentials. There are other problems too, like is a chapter on mysterious places really a better use of space in the Hunter core book than a section dealing with how to run Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, and Demons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T05:40:29-07:00","id":1459544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are other problems too, like is a chapter on mysterious places really a better use of space in the Hunter core book than a section dealing with how to run Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, and Demons? </div> </div> </div>That's a matter of taste. But to me, it is. I <i>don't</i> view Hunter as essentially a crossover game, with the default antagonists being (knock-offs of) the other gamelines' protagonists; so I don't mind the core book not really dealing with (simplified versions of) vampires, werewolves, mages, etc. My view of it is that, for example, the Kindred are so focused on their own issues that they're generally just as ignorant of the sheer variety of monsters that inhabit the shadows as your average mortal is. But hunters are all too aware of just how many things there are that go bump in the night; and to them, the Kindred don't really make up that much of the monsters that are out there. They don't necessarily even make up that much of the <i>vampires</i> that are out there (see <b>Night Horrors: Wicked Dead</b>). So, the \u201cdefault\u201d antagonist for a hunter is more likely to be a one-off monster than a member of one of the societies of monsters that feature in the other gamelines. <br /> <br /> Which, again, doesn't mean that I don't want to see H2e address, e.g., vampire hunters. But I don't need it to be in the core book, and I <i>do</i> need it to <i>not</i> be attempts to carbon copy the Kindred. To me, the whole point of using the Horror rules to stat up a vampire is that the vampiric Horror <i>isn't</i> like the Kindred, and is more like the Wicked Dead. <br /> <br /> And that's what I'd like to see in a Night Horrors supplement for Hunter: a sampling of monsters that are to the other gamelines as the Wicked Dead are to the Kindred. If I want to have my hunters hunt an actual Kindred, I'll break out my copy of Vampire: the Requiem and do an honest to goodness crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T10:40:16-07:00","id":1459565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1459544#post1459544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a matter of taste. But to me, it is. I <i>don't</i> view Hunter as essentially a crossover game, with the default antagonists being (knock-offs of) the other gamelines' protagonists; so I don't mind the core book not really dealing with (simplified versions of) vampires, werewolves, mages, etc. My view of it is that, for example, the Kindred are so focused on their own issues that they're generally just as ignorant of the sheer variety of monsters that inhabit the shadows as your average mortal is. But hunters are all too aware of just how many things there are that go bump in the night; and to them, the Kindred don't really make up that much of the monsters that are out there. They don't necessarily even make up that much of the <i>vampires</i> that are out there (see <b>Night Horrors: Wicked Dead</b>). So, the \u201cdefault\u201d antagonist for a hunter is more likely to be a one-off monster than a member of one of the societies of monsters that feature in the other gamelines.<br /> <br /> Which, again, doesn't mean that I don't want to see H2e address, e.g., vampire hunters. But I don't need it to be in the core book, and I <i>do</i> need it to <i>not</i> be attempts to carbon copy the Kindred. To me, the whole point of using the Horror rules to stat up a vampire is that the vampiric Horror <i>isn't</i> like the Kindred, and is more like the Wicked Dead.<br /> <br /> And that's what I'd like to see in a Night Horrors supplement for Hunter: a sampling of monsters that are to the other gamelines as the Wicked Dead are to the Kindred. If I want to have my hunters hunt an actual Kindred, I'll break out my copy of Vampire: the Requiem and do an honest to goodness crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>But like Tessie said, many people who play Hunter will want to fight classical monsters and vampires are as classical as they get. It's not just about imitating Kindred. It's about vampires. And if crossover isn't a default Hunter assumption, the book should have a way to make a vampire antagonist without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T11:25:56-07:00","id":1459569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1459565#post1459565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But like Tessie said, many people who play Hunter will want to fight classical monsters and vampires are as classical as they get. It's not just about imitating Kindred. It's about vampires. And if crossover isn't a default Hunter assumption, the book should have a way to make a vampire antagonist without it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to this, the number of references to Vampires, Werewolves, and Mages in chapters 1-4 makes it seem like those creatures are what a Hunter should expect to see as core antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T20:12:13-07:00","id":1459616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1364695-hunter-the-vigil-2e-kickstarter?p=1459541#post1459541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems at odds with some of the other purposes of 2e. OPP have stated that the reason they're reprinting the core rules in every 2e book is so that groups only need one book to run the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not comparable since the core rules are needed in for the corebook to function as a game. Not having a Drain Dread Power listed doesn't suddenly make Hunter 2e unplayable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T20:58:15-07:00","id":1459620,"title":"","content":"Well now I know after this discussion what I\u2019d start writing up if I ever pick up the kickstarter manuscripts (or Hunter 2E itself, since time flies by)\u2026\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}